1785606078604092	continuum-dev	itc:v3:AWKSTzM5JJnJPkQAAAAAQar23VW6voAAAAEylQc		item.comment	bn-3ayom	{"body":"Landed @ b31135a. Lead ran all continuumd suites in-workspace (60 green incl. the 5 new bump/reject-frame tests) and confirmed version=3.1 / idl_version=1.2 in the IDL. Dispositions RATIFIED: F1 paid in full (CapabilityProfile — T3 now read off the wire; the full-four-gaps argument over the flag's own minimal fix is correct); F4 paid (ServerReject; untagged-by-required-fields ACCEPTED — wrapping ServerWelcome would break 3.0 clients; frame tagging is PR-5 transport); F5/F7 paid (the audit-correlation derivation-from-request-identity rule is exactly right — a random id would have been the existence oracle P5 exists to prevent); F6 paid as obligation with the no-manifest honesty stated; F2/F3/F8 deferred with reasons ratified. T4 bidirectional placement (corrections 41/27) ratified. The @since re-dating catch and the brief-error correction (major window [3,2] serves 2.x — my brief was wrong, the agent was right) both noted with appreciation. majors_served disclosure ACCEPTED as safe (probe-learnable; server identity rightly omitted). Store-side descriptor subset clause accepted. The two conformance catches during mirroring are the drift-discipline's proof of function."}	blake3:JCB-C-UICh17RSYsDfkOdk4Qj7idB_GGlduogCTEwHU
1785606078641233	continuum-dev	itc:v3:AWKSTzM5JJnJPkQAAAAAQar23VW6voAAAAEylgc		item.move	bn-3ayom	{"state":"done"}	blake3:_FkvDeP1XLWXCacFgWpZgkRVxWZ_tXfjCHVYU73sL1c
1785606112790411	continuum-dev	itc:v3:AWKSTzM5JJnJPkQAAAAAQar23VW6voAAAAEyAQ		item.comment	bn-2d0e	{"body":"PR-8 IMPL-01 delivered: programmatic transition model in crates/continuum-engine-reference (ident/domain/expr/model/diehard, 5 modules, ~2.1k src lines) + 72 tests across 3 integration suites (model_contract 28, diehard_evidence 16, adversarial_model 28).\n\nDesign: guards and updates are a closed expression AST (data), NOT Rust closures — argued against INV-005 in src/expr.rs: a closure makes ambient nondeterminism unenforceable and unscannable by GOV-1-04, has no PartialEq/Ord/encoding so a model_digest for RFC 0005's claim envelope could not exist, and defeats docs/16 PO-MOD-002's termination obligation. Actions are guard + non-empty set of outcomes (one = deterministic, several = enumerated nondeterminism); assignments within an outcome are simultaneous over the pre-state, unassigned variables are unchanged (frame rule, stated once). Initial states are an explicit named-binding enumeration; an init *predicate* is deliberately absent because solving one is exploration, not declaration.\n\nOrdering rule (the load-bearing decision): canonical order is byte-lexicographic by name, NOT declaration order — kernel-core wire.rs:311-314 (Token derives Ord on Vec<u8>, 'Ordered by bytes') and wire.rs:89-95/496-497. Variables sorted by name fix state-vector positions; action index = position in ascending-name order = the certificate action table; initial states and successor rows are strictly ascending state vectors. Tested: declaration_order_is_not_part_of_the_model asserts two differently-ordered builders produce EQUAL models.\n\ncontinuum-value was evaluated and DECLINED with a citable reason: its Name::Ord is shortlex (value.rs:1083-1085 compare_blobs), which disagrees with the kernel's byte order — on Die Hard's own action names the two orders differ outright. The crate therefore has zero dependencies (also avoids a dependency-rationale.toml entry).\n\nDie Hard: transcribed line-for-line from corpus/tla-examples/ports/TV-009/DieHard.ctm (state block :3-6, init :8, six actions :10-25, invariants :30-31); DieHard.ctm:27/:29 deliberately not transcribed (Next is what successors() computes; Spec is temporal). Corpus CamelCase names kept — they sort to the same relative order, hence the same action indices 0-5, as kernel-core fixture.rs:247-256's kebab-case list. Frozen facts asserted at this layer via a plain closure walk IN THE TEST (no engine module): 16 reachable states (exact list), 96 labelled transitions, shortest big==4 witness at depth 6 at (4,3), the 6-step Lean solution path replayed as real labelled transitions, TypeOK true everywhere reachable, NotSolved false at exactly (4,0)/(4,3), closure Post(S) subset S.\n\nTyped, never clamped, never panicking: out-of-domain update = EvaluationError::UpdateOutOfDomain (docs/16 PO-MOD-003 failing as data), checked arithmetic = EvalError::Overflow, expression depth bounded at 32 by both builder and evaluator. Crate-level deny of indexing_slicing/unwrap_used/expect_used/panic/arithmetic_side_effects, matching kernel-core lib.rs:96-104.\n\nSeams left for siblings (table in model.rs docs): BFS = initial_states()+successors(); checking = evaluate_predicate() + empty successors() as the deadlock/disabled witness (NO invariant-vs-goal policy encoded here); witness = Step::action()/target() in returned order; certificate = variables()/actions()/State::as_slice() plus rows already in wire row order.\n\nGates: cargo fmt/clippy -D warnings/test clean, cargo doc no warnings, full 'just check' exit 0. START_HERE PR-8 bullet 1 annotated, traceability regenerated (PR-8-IMPL-01 active->satisfied, 731->730 active), validation-results.json NOT touched.\n\nHONEST GAP: I carry req:phase-a-del-07 ('executable finite reference engine and certificates from Revision 2') and did NOT annotate it. It needs the remaining four PR-8 bones — BFS, checking, witness, and Revision 2 certificate emission — none of which is in this slice; certificate emission in particular is untouched, so the fourth frozen TV-009 fact ('certificate accepted by independent checker') is deliberately unasserted. PR-8-EXIT also stays active: it is a daemon-API claim and this bone touches no daemon code."}	blake3:ZnYGrZ87PPLYLAhJrNQ2QmdSXHa5e6bTcgS3ljhLfBU
1785606216716016	continuum-dev	itc:v3:AWKSTzM5JJnJPkQAAAAAQar23VW6voAAAAEylwc		item.comment	bn-2d0e	{"body":"Landed. Lead ran all three suites in-workspace (72 green). Ratified: combinators-not-closures with the three-way INV-005 argument (governance scanability + model_digest existence + structural PO-MOD-002); non-short-circuit connectives for order-independent error sets; byte-lexicographic canonical order with the kernel-core wire citations; continuum-value DECLINED with the shortlex-vs-byte-order reason recorded (two orders on one type would breach GOV-1-12) — zero deps as a consequence; the fourth frozen TV-009 fact deliberately unasserted rather than quietly three-of-four. The self-caught depth-8 bug is the frozen-facts discipline paying rent. Seams table accepted for the four sibling bones."}	blake3:1Wyl-k6PqJ9sP74nt38OEPvlzlBKjjnTMBkXgJGxOPM
