1785612326322489	continuum-dev	itc:v3:AWKSTzM5JJnJPkQAAAAAQar23VW6voAAAAEyAQ		item.comment	bn-dw81	{"body":"INV-014 evidence delivered. New file: crates/continuum-kernel-core/tests/inv014_version_explicit_evidence.rs (8 tests, all passing; just check green, exit 0, incl. Lean/dossier/governance/boundaries/covenant).\n\nControl -> evidence map (plan.md:359-361's six-item sentence):\n\n1. \"Lean version\" — lean/lean-toolchain pins leanprover/lean4:v4.32.1 (docs/23_LEAN4_FORMALIZATION_PROGRAM.md: \"The dossier pins v4.32.1\"); `just check`'s `lean:` recipe runs `lake build` under that pin (Justfile:89-99). lean/artifacts/axiom-manifest-t0-t1.{json,txt} (ADR-0035) separately records the version. New: positive_lean_version_in_the_axiom_manifest_matches_the_pinned_toolchain cross-checks the pin file against both recorded copies byte-for-byte — closes a real gap (see Finding below).\n\n2. \"library closure\" — RFC 0035's own worker-key term (\"Lean version, library closure, source snapshot, options, resource policy\"). lean/lake-manifest.json: \"packages\": [] (self-contained metatheory by design; lean/AxiomManifest.lean doc comment: \"nothing in the metatheory may depend on it\"); lean/lakefile.toml requires no package. New: positive_library_closure_is_recorded_as_empty_and_nothing_requires_a_package pins both files agree.\n\n3. \"theorem hashes\" / \"axioms\" — lean/AxiomManifest.lean walks the RFC 0012 T0/T1 ladder (68 theorems), records axioms via Lean.collectAxioms (same source #print axioms uses); lean/scripts/axiom-manifest.sh --check (wired into `just check`) fails on drift between checked-in artifacts and a fresh regeneration. theoremsWithAxioms: 0 records PR-4A's \"empty axiom manifests\" exit criterion directly. New: positive_axiom_manifest_json_and_transcript_agree_on_the_zero_axiom_claim cross-checks the JSON counts against the .txt transcript's line counts (0 \"depends on axioms:\", 68 \"does not depend on any axioms\") — nothing previously checked the two artifact forms agree with each other.\n   Literal per-theorem content hashes (as opposed to axiom-manifest presence/pinning) do not exist anywhere; see Finding/Deferred below re: the proof-receipt schema's `lean` block.\n\n4. \"certificate schema\" — notes/plan/schemas/proof-receipt.schema.json (RFC 0024), validated by tools/validate_dossier.py (`just check`'s `dossier` recipe) against schemas/examples/finite-closure.proof-receipt.json, and independently re-validated at the Rust layer by tools/check_kernel_covenant.py's KCOV-09 (rule_receipt_conformance, explicitly named for INV-014 in its own summary line and self-tested against 4 fixtures: tools/kernel-covenant/fixtures/kcov-09-{wire-epoch-id-unqualified,magic-collision,checker-epoch-written-into-epochs,receipt-carries-an-unknown-field}/). bn-ww5ic added the typed assurance_class/trusted_components fields. New: positive_certificate_schema_pins_the_checker_and_lean_block_shapes pins the checker/lean block required-field lists and the lean-theorem conditional-requirement branch (schema's allOf if/then) — that branch is never exercised by tools/validate_dossier.py's SCHEMA_PAIRS (its one example is a closed-set certificate), so this closes an unexercised-schema-branch gap.\n\n5. \"checker identity\" — crates/continuum-kernel-{core,sat,smt,temporal}/src/receipt.rs each declare a qualified WIRE_EPOCH_ID (`<crate>/<magic>/<epoch>`, e.g. continuum-kernel-core/CONTCERT/1), carried in checker.version as semver build metadata (RFC 0026 correction 17: \"There is no checker epoch ... checker identity is ... engine identity for native checkers\"). KCOV-09 statically cross-checks every crate's declared WIRE_EPOCH_ID against its own wire.rs constants and flags shared magics. Existing per-crate tests: every_seam_field_is_shape_checked, a_receipt_without_a_reproduction_command_is_refused, the_receipt_names_which_crates_wire_epoch_it_means — present, structurally identical, in all four crates' receipt.rs. New: positive_all_four_kernel_crates_have_distinct_qualified_wire_epoch_ids and positive_golden_receipts_name_their_own_crate_and_carry_the_matching_wire_marker read all four crates' sources live from one Rust test (previously this cross-crate distinctness was only checked by the Python tool, never by cargo test) — belt-and-suspenders, not a replacement.\n\nCandidate gap named in the brief: \"is there a test asserting a receipt REFUSES emission when a seam field is absent/malformed?\" — checked. Already covered, byte-identically, in all four crates: every_seam_field_is_shape_checked (7 fields), a_seam_string_with_a_control_byte_is_refused, a_receipt_without_a_reproduction_command_is_refused, a_receipt_id_outside_the_schema_pattern_is_refused. No gap; no test added for this candidate.\n\nFinding (real, previously uncaught — not patched, src/ and lean/AxiomManifest.lean out of scope): lean/AxiomManifest.lean hand-writes the Lean version into both checked-in artifacts as a string literal (\"leanprover/lean4:v4.32.1\", twice: the JSON's leanToolchain field, line ~167, and the .txt transcript's \"# toolchain:\" header, line ~143) rather than reading lean/lean-toolchain — the file elan/lake actually use to select a Lean version. `axiom-manifest.sh --check` only diffs a regeneration of that same generator against the checked-in files, so it would still pass if lean-toolchain were bumped without updating the two literals — \"Lean version ... recorded\" would keep passing every existing gate while naming a stale toolchain. Verified live: temporarily editing the checked-in JSON's leanToolchain to a different version made the new positive_lean_version_in_the_axiom_manifest_matches_the_pinned_toolchain test fail with a clear message, then reverted (git status confirms only the new test file changed). The new test pins this permanently going forward; the underlying generator is unpatched per scope.\n\nDeferred, not a gap in bn-dw81's scope: proof-receipt.schema.json's `lean` block (version/theorems/imports/axioms/environment_hash) is the schema-side home for a Lean-flavored *receipt* per RFC 0035 (\"Statement/environment/proof hashes, theorem, imports, axiom output, kernel/tool version, worker artifact\"), but no code anywhere emits or checks a lean-theorem-kind receipt today — no example instance, no Rust producer. This is bn-3ie (\"Proof receipts with theorem and axiom manifests\", Phase D, req:pr-28), which depends on PR 28 (isolated Lean proof service, RFC 0035) opening in Phase D. bn-dw81 depends only on bn-3af (PR 4a, done) and bn-6tv (PR 9, done); PR 28 hasn't started.\n\nAnnotation: checked the invariant extractor's satisfaction path (tools/traceability.py's `_extract_headings`, used for invariant/threat/proof-obligation headings alike — a `(delivered: bn-...)` suffix on the heading summary sets status \"satisfied\"). Precedent (T02, docs/09_THREAT_MODEL.md) shows this annotation is added only when *every* control is fully delivered — T02's own worker bone (bn-2res) explicitly left docs/09 unannotated while one of its four controls was a documented deferral, and the annotation landed later, at the successor bone's close (bn-30eym), once all four controls were satisfied. INV-014 is in the same state: 5 of 6 controls (Lean version, library closure, axioms, certificate schema, checker identity) are satisfied for the native-checker/seed-theorem scope this bone covers, but \"theorem hashes\" in the RFC-0035-receipt sense is not yet built anywhere (owned by bn-3ie/PR 28). Per the convention, plan.md's INV-014 heading is NOT annotated `(delivered: ...)`. Recommend annotating once bn-3ie lands and the `lean` receipt block gets a real producer/example.\n\nScope respected: no src/ changes (Rust or Lean), no existing test touched, no notes/plan edits (so no traceability regen needed), no maw ws merge / git push / bn state change. continuumd/ and the boundaries checker (INV-004's territory) untouched. Committed in-workspace: \"test: INV-014 version-explicit proof evidence map (bn-dw81)\"."}	blake3:QPTls-7HwcYHlpRVdOi6hhy3WGQJUIi4qKCI9wldFTY
