1785619207324231	continuum-dev	itc:v3:AWKSTzM5JJnJPkQAAAAAQar23VW6voAAAAEy_gc		item.comment	bn-i4aem	{"body":"Delivered @ 7838f72 (8 commits). IDL 1.2->1.3, protocol 3.1->3.2, one bump taken once at the end on the 3.1 precedent. DISPOSITIONS — fixed in the IDL: (1) errors.common gains UnsupportedSemanticFeature among the always-admissible codes; the contradiction bit 25 of 72 operations (3 with 'errors []' + 22 that never named it), 50 already declared it, so the union is the small move and a per-operation list would be wrong again next registration. (2) struct FileComponent + SnapshotComponents.file_components optional + rule snapshot.file_components; the rank-1 schema already required path beside digest on every files[] item, so this was an IDL/schema disagreement, not a wish. Fixed in the daemon: (9) Effect gains a Completion lane and result::success reads it, so task_started/task_suspended are reachable; verification.start reports suspended-with-continuation when a campaign parks, task.resume reports a re-park (which was bn-18z defect (8), 'no field for it' — the envelope had two all along), task.update_budget may not because it is not @task_starting. (12) task.resume's model-gone collapse to a denial is gone: the honest code is now inside the union and the existing registry-driven guard picked it up with zero code change. DEFERRED with reasons in RFC 0026 correction 47 + F14-F18: (3) toolchain component — IDL agrees with plan 4.2 AND the schema; the gap is continuum-workspace's, and an IDL field would create a NEW rank-1 disagreement. (4) CHECKED_BY edge — refused to invent: a CHECKED_BY 'to' is a required ev_ NODE handle and a checker is a service-identity string, so there is nothing to point at; plus undeclared edge identity and unstated edge authority; plus a new verb is a plan 10.2 + RFC 0027 + IDL edit together. (5) validation_basis — sharper than reported: the schema conditions it on status=validated and the IDL requires it on every response while this daemon promotes to Observed, so it is required where its vocabulary is undefined; both fixes are non-additive. (6) producer-is-only-checker code — InsufficientEvidence stays; a dedicated code reports deployment topology to a caller who asked about evidence. (7) observe.classify Opaque — already IDL open item 3 group 3 / F3. (8) Cost transitions — SD-12 holds one nine-dimension list across four artifacts, one rank-1. The WITNESS half is WITHDRAWN not deferred: VerificationResult.crashpack is its wire home and always was; the missing thing is a producer. (11) EpochSet.protocol required — a symptom of F9 (no Continuation struct), appended there. CODEC DECISIONS, each cited: field order = code-point order of field names (RFC 0037 ID5, reference impl continuum-intent/canonical_json; declaration order rejected because an omitted optional has no position, a map has no declaration order, and a reader would need the IDL to read a document it can parse); unions externally tagged (the IDL's own variant production, and internal tagging emits a field rule envelope.unknown_fields forbids); Opaque resolved by the carrying object's own required 'operation' field, so it is a function of the message alone. TRANSPORT: LocalPair of channels, u32-BE length-prefixed canonical frames, Server::serve drives dispatch, ServerReject reachable pre-negotiation, ResultEnvelope.payload carries real bytes. CONFORMANCE CAUGHT: nothing in the mirror (the suite was green after the first commit) — but writing the mutation sweep found that the reader re-sorted out-of-order keys instead of rejecting them, which accepted a second byte spelling; rule encoding.canonical_form now states the reader-side half and JsonError::KeyOrder enforces it. Also found: rule bodies are lexical noise to the conformance parser, so errors::COMMON was unchecked against the rule that states it — new case closes that. TESTS: 193 continuumd (13 codec + 10 transport new; 6 golden vectors; 8757 mutants). just check exits 0."}	blake3:KY-IZXgHBHG9xtli5HabsXagh6_0HyBLPzLwqXvZ5DY
1785619326305745	continuum-dev	itc:v3:AWKSTzM5JJnJPkQAAAAAQar23VW6voAAAAEy_wc		item.comment	bn-i4aem	{"body":"Landed @ 8acd9e9 (with bn-3bhkp). Lead ran all 12 continuumd suites in-workspace (193 tests green). Dispositions RATIFIED including the two standouts: item 8's witness half WITHDRAWN as wrong-artifact (crashpack is the wire home; the gap is a producer) — exactly the discipline; item 4's refusal to invent the CHECKED_BY surface (RFC 0038 must decide which node plays the role). Codec decisions ratified with their citations; the FOURTH decision (reader rejects out-of-order keys — found by the mutation sweep catching the reader re-sorting into acceptance of a second spelling) is the canonical-form rule growing its missing half. Concern 2 ratified: status-agrees-with-body-discriminator is the honest reading. PR 5 EXIT ANNOTATION ACCEPTED — the exit sentence (idempotent replay, same identities, byte-identical frames through the transport) is delivered; canonical_cbor is a conforming-daemon obligation recorded in RFC 0026/START_HERE, not the exit sentence → follow-up bone created. F14–F18 recorded against their owning artifacts."}	blake3:jMxDED4mzkY-UdO66cAc5_e8V6EAYfrUadEJ5mbUm7Q
