1785620937500345	continuum-dev	itc:v3:AWKSTzM5JJnJPkQAAAAAQar23VW6voAAAAEyAQ		item.comment	bn-1jg0	{"body":"PR-8 exit evidence delivered: crates/continuumd/tests/pr8_exit_evidence.rs (4 tests), all through the daemon API's byte boundary (LocalPair/Server), not Daemon::dispatch directly. Positive test asserts the wire carries TaskRecord.cost.states=16 (destructured Cost exhaustively, no ..; a future wire revision adding a transitions field would fail this file's compilation); the 96 transitions and depth-6 witness are read from Daemon::state one layer down with an explicit honesty note (RFC 0026 F16 — no wire field; VerificationResult.crashpack is the witness's declared but unbuilt home), corroborated against daemon_task_operations.rs's operation-layer test of the same claim. Determinism test replays the whole scripted frame sequence (handshake+create+seal+start+status+result) from two independently-built fresh daemons and asserts byte-identical transcripts. Negative tests: a captured genuine verification.start frame is proved dispatchable, then two single-byte mutations (outer JSON brace; one byte in the embedded \"target\" field name) are both rejected — one at the transport decode layer (Err, no answer owed), one as a typed MalformedRequest result — neither growing the task table past the one genuine task. Unregistered-model negative test forks DieHard.ctm to different bytes through workspace.fork/seal frames and confirms verification.start refuses UnsupportedSemanticFeature with no task minted. START_HERE PR-8 Exit line annotated '(delivered: bn-1jg0)'; traceability regenerated (PR-8 and PR-8-EXIT now satisfied, active 711->709); dossier validator run standalone (not redirected into validation-results.json, per known pitfall) — exit 0. Full 'just check' run once — exit 0, all suites green including the new file's 4 tests. Committed in-workspace; no maw ws merge, no bn state changes, no push."}	blake3:illtv6As06yXG3AMAx6eTU3MnderpF7jP0opdfP40zM
1785621015335255	continuum-dev	itc:v3:AWKSTzM5JJnJPkQAAAAAQar23VW6voAAAAEykAg		item.comment	bn-1jg0	{"body":"Landed @ a0f21b7. Lead ran the 4 evidence tests in-workspace (green). Ratified: the wire-vs-operation-layer honesty statement (16 crosses a frame; 96 awaits F16; depth-6's wire home exists with no producer — confirmed absent rather than assumed); the no-.. Cost destructuring (future wire fields fail compilation); the two-daemon byte-identical transcript claim (stronger than single replay); the tamper test's two documented rejection paths cited to the codec's own finding rather than overclaiming every mutation."}	blake3:X0xQnDpSDOh3MmS6G_SMIirjI5r2-_hw6nz9KUglzWM
