1785622124993747	continuum-dev	itc:v3:AWKSTzM5JJnJPkQAAAAAQar23VW6voAAAAEymQg		item.comment	bn-3nfy	{"body":"T01 evidence delivered @ daebf1d (part 1/2: control map). just check green end to end (fmt, clippy -D warnings, tests, boundaries, covenant, governance, dossier, Lean).\n\nControl -> evidence map (bone's 6 controls):\n\n1. \"length/depth limits\" — MAX_DEPTH=64 checked *before* recursion in every recursive decoder: continuum_value::value (Cursor::value), continuum_intent::canonical_json::Parser::value + independently re-checked by codec.rs/ast.rs/fairness.rs walking the already-parsed tree, continuumd::codec::json::Parser::value, continuum_workspace::snapshot::decode_node. Plus per-field caps: MAX_TOKEN_BYTES=128, MAX_SEGMENT_BYTES=255, MAX_CERTIFICATE_BYTES=64MiB (all 4 kernel crates), MAX_FRAME_BYTES=16MiB (continuumd transport). Existing tests: continuum_value's decoder_bounds_its_own_recursion, continuum_intent's nesting_past_the_bound_is_a_typed_error_and_not_a_stack_overflow (+ per-field-group variants in all 5 adversarial_decode.rs files), continuum_workspace's MAX_DEPTH+1/+8 rejection tests.\n\n2. \"streaming decoding\" — every decoder is a forward-only, bounds-checked reader over &[u8]: continuum_value::value::Cursor, continuum_{kernel-core,kernel-sat,kernel-smt,kernel-temporal}::wire::Reader (doc: \"the reader never seeks backwards, which is what makes streaming validation a property of the format\"), continuum_workspace::snapshot::Cursor, continuumd::transport::Channel::take_frame (returns None for a partial frame, leaves bytes in place — exercised one byte at a time by a_frame_is_read_only_once_all_of_it_has_arrived).\n\n3. \"checked arithmetic\" — every offset/length computation is checked_add (Reader::take / Cursor::take in all four kernel crates + continuum_value + continuum_workspace, all returning a typed Truncated/UnexpectedEnd rather than wrapping or panicking), and every running-total budget uses saturating_add (kernel crates' MAX_TRANSITIONS/MAX_TOTAL_LITERALS/MAX_TOTAL_HINTS accumulators). reader_take_is_bounds_checked_at_the_edge (kernel-core) exercises usize::MAX directly.\n\n4. \"allocation budgets\" — MAX_CERTIFICATE_BYTES and MAX_FRAME_BYTES gate total input size before any decode work starts (kernel crates' `if bytes.len() > MAX_CERTIFICATE_BYTES` is the first line of `decode`; continuumd's take_frame checks the 4-byte prefix against MAX_FRAME_BYTES before touching the queue). Existing tests: all 4 kernel crates' check.rs has a MAX_CERTIFICATE_BYTES+1 rejection test. Kernel wire formats additionally cap *cumulative* work across the whole certificate (MAX_TRANSITIONS/MAX_TOTAL_LITERALS/MAX_TOTAL_HINTS), checked per-row/per-step before that row's elements are read, so no single in-range count can be repeated to blow the total budget.\n\n5. \"no recursive descent on unbounded attacker structures\" — the JSON-shaped decoders bound recursion by MAX_DEPTH checked pre-recursion (see control 1). The certificate wire formats go further and have no recursion at all by construction: kernel-core's wire.rs doc states \"Nothing nests, so the format has no recursion for RFC 0005's 'cycle/recursion bounds' to bound and the decoder cannot overflow a stack\" — true of all four kernel crates' grammars (domain/table/rows are flat sequences, not nested structures).\n\n6. \"fuzzing and corpus tests\" — this codebase's realization of the control (docs/19 SS6) is deterministic exhaustive-sweep testing rather than coverage-guided fuzzing (no cargo-fuzz/libFuzzer harness exists; continuum-corpus is the unrelated TLA+ semantic corpus). Evidence: garbage_from_outside_the_crate_never_panics (every prefix of a valid cert + every single-byte filler 0..=255, all 4 kernel crates), every_prefix_of_a_valid_certificate_is_rejected_not_accepted (kernel-core), a_domain_pack_count_beyond_the_declared_ceiling_is_rejected_from_bytes_alone (CountOutOfRange boundary, all 4 kernels), continuumd's no_single_byte_mutation_of_a_golden_vector_decodes_to_the_same_document (~8.7k byte-mutants over 6 golden vectors, none silently reinterpreted), continuumd's adversarial_construction.rs (linear, MAX_FIXTURE=8192-bounded identifier sweeps), continuum_intent's 5 *_adversarial_decode.rs suites (truncation/duplicate-key/vocabulary-closure/depth sweeps per field group), continuum_workspace's snapshot truncation/garbage-tag/deep-nesting sweeps.\n\n(continued in part 2/2: with_capacity audit, gap, test, annotation, gates)"}	blake3:VmWOaBED5AfQHo_7khPxXvJ2Z-1ZYjTz3uUoKtYll2s
1785622128904802	continuum-dev	itc:v3:AWKSTzM5JJnJPkQAAAAAQar23VW6voAAAAEymgg		item.comment	bn-3nfy	{"body":"T01 evidence delivered @ daebf1d (part 2/2: with_capacity audit, gap, test, annotation, gates).\n\nwith_capacity audit (every decode path named in the brief, plus a full repo grep of all ~40 with_capacity call sites):\n\n- continuum-value/src/value.rs (CVNF-1 decoder): Cursor::take is checked_add + range-checked, returns a borrowed slice (zero allocation); blob()/items()/set()/multiset()/record()/map() all grow via Vec::new()/BTreeSet::new()/BTreeMap::new() + push, never with_capacity(declared_len). Bound: whatever take() has already verified is <= remaining bytes. Existing test decoder_does_not_trust_a_declared_length declares a 2^64 length with 0 payload bytes and asserts UnexpectedEnd/LengthTooLarge. SAFE, no gap.\n- continuum-intent/src/{canonical_json,codec,ast,fairness}.rs: zero with_capacity in any of the four files. Parser::array/object grow via Vec::new()/BTreeMap::new(); depth checked before recursion. SAFE.\n- continuum-{kernel-core,kernel-sat,kernel-smt,kernel-temporal}/src/wire.rs: Reader::take checked_add + range-checked (borrowed slice, zero allocation); counted_u16/counted_u32 range-check every declared count against MAX_DOMAIN_PACKS/MAX_VARIABLES/MAX_STATES/MAX_ACTIONS/MAX_CLAUSES/MAX_ATOMS/MAX_ASSERTIONS/MAX_LEMMAS/MAX_STEPS/MAX_HINTS/MAX_DELETIONS before the corresponding loop starts; every sequence (tokens, states, transitions, clauses, literals, steps, hints, deletion ids, ranks) grows via Vec::new()+push, never with_capacity(count). Doc comment states the invariant explicitly (\"no wire-derived Vec::with_capacity — a declared count is never allowed to reserve memory before its bytes have been read\"). Bound: MAX_CERTIFICATE_BYTES (total) + per-field MAX_* + running MAX_TRANSITIONS/MAX_TOTAL_LITERALS/MAX_TOTAL_HINTS budgets. SAFE, no gap, identical pattern in all four crates (deliberate, per docs/03 SS8 diversity).\n- continuumd/src/transport/mod.rs Channel::take_frame: declared u32 checked against MAX_FRAME_BYTES=16MiB before anything else; then requires the full declared byte count already resident in the VecDeque before drain/collect. Bound: MAX_FRAME_BYTES, and allocation only ever copies bytes already buffered. GAP: correct code, zero adversarial test anywhere in the repo (grepped every test file for FrameError/TooLarge/take_frame — only positive/partial-delivery paths were exercised). Fixed by 3 new tests (below).\n- continuumd/src/codec/json.rs: same MAX_DEPTH-before-recursion + Vec::new()/BTreeMap::new() pattern as continuum-intent's. base64url/from_base64url with_capacity calls are proportional to already-resident text/bytes, not wire-prefix-driven. SAFE.\n- continuumd/src/codec/mod.rs encode_list/decode_list/encode_map: with_capacity(items.len()) sizes off an ALREADY-MATERIALIZED Json::Array/BTreeMap (second-stage typed decode over a tree Json::parse already bounded), not a raw wire count. SAFE.\n- continuum-workspace/src/snapshot.rs Snapshot::decode: Cursor::length() is documented and implemented as \"read a length and check it against what is left, before anything is allocated\" (rejects len > remaining() pre-take); TAG_FILE content and TAG_DIRECTORY child count both go through this gate before any Vec/BTreeMap growth; MAX_DEPTH=64 checked before decode_node recurses. Existing test (~snapshot.rs:3690) declares TAG_FILE length = u64::MAX with 0 payload and asserts LengthOutOfRange, its own comment reading \"rejected before anything is allocated\". SAFE, no gap. (seal_file/seal_directory's with_capacity calls are encode-side, sizing off already-resident content.)\n- ~25 remaining with_capacity sites (grepped exhaustively): hex/base64 encoders sizing off already-resident bytes, path/record builders sizing off already-checked MAX_DEPTH/MAX_SEGMENT_BYTES-bounded segments, or continuum-engine-reference's bfs/certificate/witness.rs building a certificate FROM an already-explored in-memory model (encode direction). None sizes a heap allocation from an unvalidated wire/document length prefix.\n- continuum-dap/continuum-lsp/continuum-mcp are unimplemented scaffolds (~20 lines each, no decoder) — out of scope, nothing to audit yet.\n\nGap found + test added: continuumd::transport::Channel::take_frame's oversized-declared-length rejection had no adversarial test. Added 3 tests to crates/continuumd/tests/transport_local.rs's existing \"framing\" section (no src/ changes — code was already correct):\n- a_declared_frame_length_past_the_transport_bound_is_rejected_before_any_wait (MAX_FRAME_BYTES+1 declared, 0 payload bytes)\n- a_maximally_hostile_declared_length_is_rejected_from_four_bytes_alone (u32::MAX declared, 4 input bytes total)\n- a_declared_length_at_the_bound_is_incomplete_not_rejected (boundary: exactly MAX_FRAME_BYTES is legal, Ok(None) not TooLarge)\nAll fixtures are 4-8 bytes (no doubling, no gigabyte materialization, per the OOM-incident brief-writing rule); each asserts a typed rejection rather than ever allocating.\n\nAnnotation decision: added \"(delivered: bn-3nfy)\" to T01's heading in notes/plan/docs/09_THREAT_MODEL.md, mirroring T02's. bn-3nfy is the only bone under req:t01 and all six controls came back comprehensively evidenced (the one coverage gap was closed inline, not deferred), so this is a complete delivery. Ran `just traceability`: regen flipped T01 active -> satisfied in PLAN_REQUIREMENTS.json/PLAN_BONE_TRACEABILITY.md (threat category: 14 active/1 satisfied -> 13 active/2 satisfied). Ran the dossier validator directly (no pipe/redirect into its own output file): status \"pass\", exit 0.\n\nScope respected: one test-only addition (transport_local.rs), one notes/plan/docs edit + its mechanical regen output, no other src/ changes, no maw ws merge / git push / bn state change. Committed in-workspace: \"test: T01 — parser and decoder memory exhaustion evidence (bn-3nfy)\" @ daebf1d.\n\nConcerns: none blocking. continuum-dap/continuum-lsp/continuum-mcp have no wire decoder yet — when one lands (Content-Length-style framing is the classic place for this exact bug), it needs this same audit; today they're simply out of T01's scope."}	blake3:bUb6scfev9Jl99v0O2xD6gA-oc0-ZZTATImjQUwZIBA
1785622171828664	continuum-dev	itc:v3:AWKSTzM5JJnJPkQAAAAAQar23VW6voAAAAEymwg		item.comment	bn-3nfy	{"body":"Landed @ 2d7d187. Lead ran the transport suite in-workspace (13 green incl. the 3 new frame-bound tests). Ratified: the repo-wide with_capacity audit's clean verdict (grow-and-gate everywhere, no declared-length front-loading); the tiny-fixture discipline honoring the OOM rule; T01 annotated satisfied with all six controls delivered. The DAP/LSP/MCP future-audit flag (Content-Length framing, the classic site) recorded for when those scaffolds gain decoders."}	blake3:ZQqcnJqxdqxEo3nJ68rBfKsXUf1xzQqBUirLIW2g0qU
1785622171868594	continuum-dev	itc:v3:AWKSTzM5JJnJPkQAAAAAQar23VW6voAAAAEynAg		item.move	bn-3nfy	{"state":"done"}	blake3:LUjaBtjSmO0WufMuQTtbWoGRZhI2Whub2EAz3RGrvzw
1785622251391833	continuum-dev	itc:v3:AWKSTzM5JJnJPkQAAAAAQar23VW6voAAAAEyAQ		item.comment	bn-2eeg	{"body":"INV-006 evidence delivered. New file: crates/continuumd/tests/inv006_replay_stability_evidence.rs (2 tests, both passing; just check green, exit 0, incl. Lean/dossier/governance/boundaries/covenant).\n\nControl -> evidence map (plan.md:327-329's sentence: \"A failure advertised as replayable must reproduce under its pinned semantic epoch or be downgraded to an engine defect.\"):\n\n1. \"must reproduce\" (determinism, generally) -- vast pre-existing coverage, cited not duplicated: crates/continuumd/tests/pr8_exit_evidence.rs's positive_the_whole_frame_sequence_replayed_from_a_fresh_daemon_is_byte_identical (two independently built daemons, one scripted exchange, byte-identical transcripts frame for frame -- stronger than transport_local.rs's single-daemon idempotent replay). Determinism holds across every crate's own suite (snapshot/BFS/witness/checking/codec/transport); mechanically enforced by --locked everywhere (Justfile:25-40), overflow-checks=true in release (Cargo.toml:90-119, cites docs/19 SS7's determinism matrix), GOV-1-03 deterministic-collections (BTreeMap-only in semantic paths, tools/governance/check_code_policy.py, enforced in `just check`'s governance recipe) and GOV-1-04 no-ambient (continuumd/src/daemon/mod.rs's own module doc: \"no async...no ambient anything\"), and the codec's canonical one-spelling discipline (codec_canonical_form.rs: a leading zero, a `+`, a non-canonical byte quantum are all refused as \"a second spelling of a value that already has one\").\n\n2. \"under its pinned semantic epoch\" -- crates/continuum-value/src/epoch.rs's own module doc quotes ADR-0018 by name for INV-006/INV-014; daemon_task_operations.rs's resume_admissibility_separates_an_epoch_disagreement_from_an_unheld_epoch (a continuation pinning a different semantic/engine epoch than the daemon currently serves is ContinuationEpochMismatch, never silently resumed under the new one) and budget_exhaustion_parks_a_continuation_that_update_budget_and_resume_complete (a suspended campaign resumed under its own epoch completes to the frozen TV-009 facts -- 16 states/96 transitions -- not an approximation, cross-checked against an independent bfs::explore call).\n\n3. \"or be downgraded to an engine defect\" -- THE GAP THIS BONE CLOSES. crates/continuum-value/src/assurance.rs's InconclusiveReason::EngineError is the closed-vocabulary type this downgrade lands in, doc-linked to INV-006 by name (\"Also where a failure advertised as replayable but not reproducible is downgraded to (INV-006)\"). daemon/verification.rs:775 lifts continuum_engine_reference::checking::Unresolved::EngineError into that wire member; checking_contract.rs's engine-layer test proves the engine produces it. But no existing test drove a real Daemon::dispatch down that arm -- every daemon-level InconclusiveReason test (budget_exhaustion_parks_a_continuation..., codec_canonical_form.rs) exercised only ResourceExhausted. New: positive_an_engine_evaluation_failure_reaches_the_wire_as_a_typed_engine_error builds a tiny self-looping model (public ModelBuilder/ActionDecl/BoolExpr/IntExpr API, same overflow recipe as checking_contract.rs's private unevaluable() helper, rebuilt here because tests/*.rs is its own crate) whose one predicate overflows i64 unconditionally, registers it, runs verification.start/result through the full daemon dispatch, and asserts Inconclusive/EngineError/Validated crosses the wire. Verified live before committing: commented out the EngineError arm of verification.rs's match (folding it into ResourceExhausted) -- the new test failed with a clear diff (ResourceExhausted vs EngineError); reverted (git diff confirms verification.rs untouched, only the new test file is new).\n\nBoundary (real, not patched, src/ untouched): \"downgraded to an engine defect\" also has a wire-operation-level reading -- program.replay / ErrorCode::ReplayDiverged (RFC 0026, registry.rs:284-296) -- that is scaffolding only. No daemon::family::Arguments variant exists for it (family.rs's enum has 25 members, one per landed family, of 72 registry rows); codec::operations::decode_arguments's own doc comment says so directly (\"the 47 of the 72 whose families have not landed\"); git grep confirms ErrorCode::ReplayDiverged is constructed nowhere in src/, only declared (vocabulary.rs token table + this one registry row). This is PR 11 (Context Pack ReplayPreserving -- continuum-context is a PR-1/IMPL-01 stub today) and PR 14/15 (asupersync journal, program.replay's real producer) territory, neither landed. New: boundary_program_replay_is_declared_vocabulary_with_no_decodable_producer pins registry.operation(\"program.replay\").errors containing ReplayDiverged AND decode_arguments(\"program.replay\", ..) == Err(CodecError::UnknownOperation), so a future PR landing the producer is what turns this test red rather than leaving the claim to prose.\n\nSecond boundary, un-pinnable (nothing exists to pin against): full multi-operation daemon-session replay after a process restart (state rebuilt from a durable store) -- checked directly. Daemon::builder only ever constructs a fresh in-memory DaemonState; there is no store-backed reconstruction path anywhere in continuumd/src. docs/35's own \"On restart the daemon MUST resolve every task it left in Running to exactly one of two outcomes... MUST NOT reconstruct task state by inference\" (absorbed from plan SS4.5) is unimplemented normative text, not a regression -- the existing store-level crash recovery (fsck, publication.rs, dx13_falsification.rs) covers content/index-commit ordering only, never the daemon's task/idempotency table. Owning bone: bn-3dr (\"Daemon crash recovery: no stale index entries or orphan tasks\"), open, blocked on bn-19u (PR 6, also open). notes/plan/notes/G0_SPIKE_MATRIX.md's own words for this exact gap: \"daemon-scale linearizability and crash-injection evidence remains PR 6+ per docs/35.\" Recorded here, not patched.\n\nAdded: 2 tests (1 positive closing the EngineError daemon-lift gap, 1 boundary pinning the program.replay/ReplayDiverged scaffolding mechanically). Cited, not duplicated: the vast pre-existing determinism/epoch-pinning suites above.\n\nAnnotation: declined, per the invariant-annotation precedent (bn-dw81/INV-014: annotate only when every control is fully delivered at the scope the bone covers). Two of three controls are solidly evidenced (reproduce; pinned epoch) and the third's PR-8-grain producer is now proven live (this bone's new test), but the sentence also has an unbuilt wire-operation reading (PR 11/14/15) and the daemon-durability/cross-restart reading (bn-3dr, PR 6+) is open. plan.md:327's INV-006 heading is NOT annotated (delivered: ...); no notes/plan edits were made at all, so no traceability regen is needed.\n\nScope respected: no src/ changes (Rust or Lean) -- the EngineError mutation above was verified live then reverted, confirmed by git diff showing verification.rs clean before commit. No existing test touched. No notes/plan edits. No maw ws merge / git push / bn state change. Siblings' territory (continuum-asupersync/task, T01, kernel decoder tests) untouched. Committed in-workspace: \"test: INV-006 replay stability evidence map (bn-2eeg)\" @ f6488f1."}	blake3:eBTI5-IHvSviSnAORGt8tyzP6zsOYZkfdbWRxiN2_BY
