1785703263614855	continuum-dev	itc:v3:AWKSTzM5JJnJPkQAAAAAQar23VW6voAAAAEy-gg		item.comment	bn-1n6r	{"body":"PR-6 exit evidence delivered — `crates/continuumd/tests/pr6_exit_evidence.rs`, five tests through `Daemon::dispatch` and nothing else. continuumd 314 → 319; continuum-task 146 and continuum-workspace 256 unchanged. `just check` exit 0. (1/2 — clause map and mechanics; the exit narrative follows in 2/2.)\n\n## Clause → test map\n\n| Clause of the exit sentence | Test |\n|---|---|\n| \"cancellation at every instrumented phase\" — all twelve wire-reachable phases: the four G0-DX-14 lanes' ten dispatch phases, the dispatch that faulted, and phase zero where the cancel arrives before the task exists | `positive_cancellation_at_every_instrumented_phase_leaves_one_of_the_two_declared_outcomes` |\n| \"leaves either a valid continuation\" — validity proved by USE, byte-identically on a second fresh daemon | `positive_a_cancelled_tasks_continuation_is_valid_by_use_on_a_second_fresh_daemon` |\n| \"or no published partial artifact\" — both dispositions, named publications checked against the region layer's committed count | `positive_a_cancel_with_no_continuation_leaves_no_published_partial_artifact` |\n| the arm with **no constructor**, asserted at the wire over every phase | same test, second half |\n| closure — post-cancel the record is CLOSED, and the exit disjunct does not move under the suffix that falsified it | `regression_the_cancelled_record_is_closed_and_the_exit_side_does_not_move` |\n| anti-vacuity — more than one behaviour class, and the classifier can say no | `positive_the_exit_phases_exercise_more_than_one_behaviour_class` |\n\n## How the sentence is made mechanical\n\n`exit_side` is a total function of what a client reads off one `task.cancel` answer — the answered status, the wire's nullable `continuation`, and `ResultEnvelope.artifacts` — onto three dispositions: `valid-continuation`, `nothing-published`, `closed-and-complete`. Its fourth branch is `None`: artifacts named, no continuation to resume them from, and a campaign that did not close. That is the shape the exit sentence forbids and the shape `CancelOutcome` has no constructor for. Two mutation probes were run and both caught: replacing the `None` branch with an accepting one fails the anti-vacuity test by name; flipping one lane row's declared disjunct fails two tests with the phase named.\n\nThe third arm is the right-hand side, and the file says why rather than asserting it: the sentence's word is **partial**, a closed campaign's artifact is a whole answer, and RFC 0026 names committed-non-resumable separately and requires a typed reason. That reason is read off the region layer's own `CancelOutcome` and asserted, not assumed.\n\nCommitted evidence is counted **three independent ways on every phase** — `ResultEnvelope.artifacts` (the wire), `TaskEntry::publications` (the task table), and the cancel scope's own `EvidenceLedger::committed` (the region layer) — plus `Publications::is_staging()` false, so a bug that fooled one accounting has two more to get past. Every named artifact is checked to carry a `commitment`: bn-23j7s's publications are *named*, never counted.\n\n\"Valid by use\" needed a device, and the device is stated rather than worked around. After the cancel, daemon A's task is terminal, so `task.resume` there is bn-10093's documented no-op — the continuation cannot be spent on the daemon that answered it. So: A parks, is cancelled, hands back `cont_*` C; B is built from scratch, runs the identical `verification.start`, and mints the **byte-identical** handle (content identity — no counter, no clock, no address); **A's** handle is then spent on B and closes the campaign on Die Hard's frozen 16 states, adding a publication rather than replacing one; a third daemon answers the identical resume byte for byte. The refusal `dx14_falsification.rs` records — A's handle denied on a fresh B that has not run the campaign — is the other side of the same coin, which is why step 2 is load-bearing rather than decorative.\n\n## Exhaustive half cited, not re-run\n\nPer the exit-file convention (`pr8_exit_evidence.rs`): one sample per equivalence class, campaigns named. Cited — bn-2zy's 5,472-run calculus matrix (324 + 108 + 5,040) and its daemon-grain twin; bn-2gk's 3,570 teardowns over 210 interleavings; bn-1gc's 1,680 reconciliations; bn-3p32's 18 attacks; bn-1kp6's 27 tests. No sweep is repeated here.\n\n## Annotated / corrected\n\n- **PR 6 Exit line** now carries `(delivered: bn-1n6r — …)` in the house convention, which flips `PR-6-EXIT` and `PR-6` to **satisfied** in `PLAN_REQUIREMENTS.json`. Active requirements 695 → 693; `pr` and `pr-exit` satisfied counts each +1. The only other diff is 162 `line` renumberings from the added paragraph.\n- **Bullet verification.** All six bullets re-read against current `src/` post-fixes. Five read true unchanged; the citations were re-verified mechanically (`daemon_task_regions.rs` ten tests, `pr6_impl02_budget_evidence.rs` ten tests, `verification::unenforced` genuinely absent, `TaskRegions::is_total` genuinely reading `defects`).\n- **One correction, cited.** The three fix bones are cited nowhere in the PR-6 block, which therefore read as though nothing had happened since the bullets landed. A new paragraph before the Exit line records the two campaigns, the defects, the three repair bones, and the one sentence bn-10093 **narrowed**: bullet 2's \"`task.update_budget` and `task.resume` now name a declared ceiling nothing meters instead of accepting it in silence\" is now true only when the resume *accepts* the budget — a resume of an already-terminal task returns above the ledger write, so it records nothing and names nothing, which is the repair's point rather than a gap. No bullet sentence was found false.\n\n## Gates\n\n`cargo fmt --all --check` clean; `cargo clippy --all-targets --locked -- -D warnings` clean; `cargo test -p continuumd --locked` 319 passed; `just check` exit 0 including lean. `validation-results.json` untouched; no `src/` change; no `.bones/` change in the workspace commit; no pre-existing test edited, weakened or moved. Commit `fb0472e` in `.maw/workspaces/bn-1n6r`, unmerged and unpushed."}	blake3:rORE-qRUFHDq9dx4Cu0ueqEm1GPVpwIFm-hLMOgxYIM
1785703334545068	continuum-dev	itc:v3:AWKSTzM5JJnJPkQAAAAAQar23VW6voAAAAEy-wg		item.comment	bn-1n6r	{"body":"PR-6 exit narrative (2/2) — the arc for the Phase A exit package, and what remains named honestly.\n\n## The arc\n\nSix bullets landed across four bones. **bn-2gk** built the region calculus: the one-way `Open → Draining(Closed | Cancelled) → Finalized` lifecycle with RFC 0026's request → drain → finalize as its three operations, `region::scoped` as the only way to open a scope (`open` and `settle` private, `scoped` calling the second on every path out of the first including the fault path), `finalize` requiring workers to be **terminal** rather than merely quiescent, and no-orphan-workers enforced by construction with three independently computed accountings behind `Finalization::is_total`. **bn-1gc** built the typed budget ledger over SD-12's nine dimensions, held to three independently maintained sources, with declared and enforced separated as a total 2×2 and lowering *admitted* rather than forbidden — B18 parks with committed partial evidence plus a continuation instead of truncating. **bn-12t** put `continuumd`'s task work inside the regions and answered the question the rewiring forced: **a parked continuation is not a live worker**. It is a durable artifact, so a resume mints a new worker in a new region — two `RegionId`s on one task — and keeping the region open across dispatches was rejected on exactly the leak G0-DX-14 asks about, since a task parked and never resumed would hold an open region for the daemon's lifetime. **bn-23j7s** gave committed partial evidence **artifact identity**: a publication is named by the content identity of the campaign that produced it, and `Publications` is a linear typestate in which a staged publication is unobservable, so \"uncommitted partials are absent, never half-visible\" is a property of what compiles rather than of care taken.\n\nThen the evidence arc, which is the part worth telling.\n\n**Constructive first.** bn-2zy's every-phase matrix established the declared outcome table with no change to the system under test — 5,472 runs across the calculus grain and the daemon grain, every one checked for a balanced obligation ledger, no artifact left neither committed nor absent, agreement with `EvidenceBook::reconcile`'s independent budget-side accounting, and RFC 0026's both-or-neither on every arm.\n\n**Then two adversarial campaigns, `src/` frozen** (the bn-21dd precedent, so the evidence that a defect is real is produced with no opportunity to shape the implementation around it): **bn-3p32**, 18 attacks against G0-DX-14's two conjuncts, and **bn-1kp6**, 22 attacks / 27 tests against G0-DX-03's three. Between them they found **four real defects, one found twice independently from two different axes**:\n\n- **record closure** — bn-3p32's A1, and bn-1kp6's attack 18 arriving at the same place from the idempotence side. `task.resume` applied a request budget *before* it tested terminality, so `cancel` → `resume(continuation, budget)` rewrote a `Cancelled` task's ceilings and could append a `task.budget_suspended` milestone, and its `TaskEvent`, to a closed record. Fixed by **bn-10093** — the terminal check moved above the ledger write, so a resume's budget arm produces `task.update_budget`'s own observable for a terminal task: nothing written, no milestone, no event, record byte-identical.\n- **lineage rewind** — bn-1kp6's D1, three tests. `workspace.create` named a lineage by the content identity of the snapshot it created and inserted it unconditionally, so an identical create under a fresh idempotency key rewound the `Fork` to its origin: the superseded snapshot was served again, the snapshot that *was* the head was stranded as `CapabilityDenied`, and an unsealed re-create revoked a live continuation. Fixed by **bn-n1xou** — an identical create converges, put-if-absent on the lineage, `sealed` monotone so no create un-seals.\n- **replay-key gap** — bn-1kp6's D3. `daemon::state::ReplayKey` omitted `RequestEnvelope.budget`, which is in the `task_*` preimage, so one key answered two different canonical requests with one campaign instead of `IdempotencyKeyReused`. Fixed by **bn-h1zqz** — the whole canonical request in the key, with the field-by-field audit of what stays out, and why, recorded at the type.\n\nEvery pin was flipped into a **regression guard running un-ignored in the default suite**, with its localising control left unchanged beside it. The named conjuncts held under all eighteen of bn-3p32's attacks. **Deterministic resume held on every axis attacked and needed no repair.** Both G0 rows — DX-14 and DX-03 — now sit at **Evidence (reference implementation)** with complete falsification-and-fix cycles recorded in `G0_SPIKE_MATRIX.md`.\n\n`pr6_exit_evidence.rs` closes the arc by re-asserting closure not as a record comparison but as the **exit sentence's own stability**: the disjunct a cancellation landed on is recomputed after the hostile suffix and must not move. A closure defect that walked a task from \"valid continuation\" to \"published partial artifact with nothing pointing at it\" is precisely the failure PR 6's exit is about; holding the record byte-identical is a proxy for that rather than the thing itself.\n\n## What remains, named honestly\n\n- **Durability is bn-3dr's.** Nothing here writes a task table to disk. What PR 6 claims is the identity binding and the wire surface: two fresh daemons name one campaign's continuation and its publications identically, so a name is something a store could be asked to return. `pr6_impl02_budget_evidence.rs` asserts that for the publications; this file asserts it for the continuation, by spending it.\n- **Mid-publication cancellation at the wire opens with asupersync, PR 14.** `Daemon::dispatch` holds `&mut DaemonState` for a whole call, so no wire cancel lands between a stage and its commit; this grain proves the *residual* teardown is correct at every phase. The in-flight case is proved exhaustively one crate down — `frontier-staged`, `answer-staged`, `lemma-staged`, `next-candidate-staged`. Saying which half proves which is the point of splitting them.\n- **DX-14's reopening condition** stands: the four lanes are lifecycle **profiles** rather than engines, because `CancelOutcome` is a function of committed evidence and declared resumability alone, so a profile presents everything the rule can see. A real DPOR/solver/proof/synthesis engine is held to this table — **unless one needs a third fact to decide the arm**, which is the condition on which the row reopens.\n- **Concurrency is G0-DX-13's axis.** One thread, one request at a time; `Daemon::dispatch` takes `&mut self`.\n- Two DX-03 concerns remain recorded without being defects, unchanged by this bone: `LineageError::Unknown` maps to `CapabilityDenied` in `workspace` and to `StaleSnapshot` in `task`/`verification`; and `Continuation::bounds`/`frontier` are pinned at creation and read by nothing on the resume path.\n\n## Concerns from this bone\n\n1. `_clean` in `traceability.py` strips underscores from generated summaries, so `pr6_exit_evidence.rs` renders as `pr6exitevidence.rs` in `PLAN_REQUIREMENTS.json` — identical to the existing PR-5 precedent. Cosmetic; the markdown is the source of truth, so it was left alone rather than worked around.\n2. `exit_side`'s `nothing-published` disposition is reachable for a `Suspended` task that published nothing. That shape is unreachable in this daemon — `continuation.is_some() ⇒ publications > 0` holds by construction — so the function is total rather than partial, but no phase samples it.\n3. Phase zero is asserted inside the \"every phase\" test rather than as its own named test, because there \"what did the cancel leave\" is answered by nothing having happened. A three-line split gives it its own name if a reviewer wants one."}	blake3:YMwjvETEOkRyU6K_oOMqbSduB7bLSL-Qsc2pOowXt9c
1785703410614599	continuum-dev	itc:v3:AWKSTzM5JJnJPkQAAAAAQar23VW6voAAAAEy_Ag		item.comment	bn-1n6r	{"body":"Landed @ ff73c1800470. Lead re-verified in-workspace: all continuumd suites green (319), fmt/clippy clean, no src change, no pre-existing test touched.\n\nRATIFIED. (1) The exit_side device: three dispositions plus a fourth None branch that IS the forbidden shape, with the anti-vacuity test feeding that branch a real artifact list — the exit sentence held as a total function rather than a per-case assertion. (2) Validity-by-USE across daemons: A's cancelled-task continuation spent on a fresh B closing to the frozen 16 states, byte-identical on a third — necessary precisely because bn-10093 made A's own task terminal, and stronger than any static validity check. (3) Committed evidence counted three independent ways per phase (wire/table/region ledger). (4) Both load-bearing mutations reverted-after-proven (accepting None fails by name; flipping one declared disjunct fails naming the phase). (5) The one narrowing correction to bullet 2 (terminal resume returns above the ledger write and names nothing) — exactly the post-fix truth, cited. (6) The new pre-Exit paragraph recording both campaigns, four defects, three repairs — the exit line now tells the whole arc including its falsifications, which is what an exit sentence is FOR.\n\nCONCERNS ACCEPTED AS RECORDED: underscore-stripped summary matches PR-5 precedent; the unsampled Suspended-zero-publications arm is unreachable by the proven implication; phase zero named inside the every-phase test.\n\nPR-6-EXIT and PR-6 satisfied. This closes the last child of bn-19u — PR 6 becomes the TENTH PR fully exited, on the strength of six delivered bullets, a 5,472-run constructive matrix, two adversarial campaigns (45 attacks/tests combined), four real defects found and fixed with pins as permanent regression guards, and both G0 rows at Evidence (reference implementation) with complete falsification-and-fix cycles."}	blake3:CWlbsa6TwBRORV-RgbfPyOEjjD-K121EyHdUWAMU-Ug
