1785720795977839	continuum-dev	itc:v3:AWKSTzM5JJnJPkQAAAAAQar23VW6voAAAAEy9Ak		item.comment	bn-1mhcr	{"body":"Bootstrap-rule successor: bn-1h158."}	blake3:Q7fDcFmLDUcaQ0W7YiTCI44nwJaEIOAGzHreVvokiso
1785721321594238	continuum-dev	itc:v3:AWKSTzM5JJnJPkQAAAAAQar23VW6voAAAAEy9Qk		item.comment	bn-3tz60	{"body":"bn-3tz60 — context expand and task lifecycle command family, delivered.\n\n## Command surfaces\n\nNew `continuum-cli` (first real code since PR-1 scaffold): `src/{wire,render,context,task,cli,format,error}.rs` + `src/bin/continuum.rs`.\n\n- `continuum context expand --context <ctx_*> --anchor <text> --relation <token> [--depth N] [--states N]`\n- `continuum task status <task_*>` / `resume <cont_*> --states <N>` / `cancel <task_*>`\n- plus `--actor`/`--capability`/`--protocol-version` (default 3.2) and `--format text|pretty|json`/hidden `--json`, resolved explicit>FORMAT-env>TTY per cli-conventions.md.\n\n`cli::Scan` is a hand-rolled `--name value` scanner (no clap — keeps the one external-facing edge at `continuumd`; dependency-rationale.toml is this wave's hot file). No CLI sibling had landed (bn-3rqvm/bn-1g7e4/bn-ybh1z all open), so `cli::run` recognizes only `context`/`task`, erroring on any other verb rather than guessing.\n\n`wire::Connection` holds only the negotiated version + speaking principal (plan §20, mirrors `continuum_mcp::AgentClient`'s shape) — NOT built on continuum-mcp, itself an adapter and a forbidden edge under `RULE adapters-are-sinks`. `task.*` decode through continuumd's real `Arguments`/`Payload` tables; `context.expand` has no variant there (see below) and is built/decoded by hand via `codec::to_opaque`/`from_bytes` against the real `ContextExpandRequest`/`Response`.\n\n`bin/continuum.rs` wires `wire::NullTransport`: continuumd ships no socket/process transport (`LocalPair`'s own doc: \"not a stand-in ... the grain the daemon is built at\"), so every real call answers `LinkError::NoTransportConfigured` at exit 2, honestly, rather than faking an ephemeral daemon. Everything above that seam is tested in-process exactly as continuum-mcp/continuum-benchmark already do.\n\n## context expand: honest-decline, with receipts\n\n`context.expand` is wire-registered (real request/response structs, `ExpansionRelation`/`Omission` vocab) but PR-11/IMPL-04 (bn-28jj) is open: no `OperationFamily`, and `Arguments`/`Payload` carry no `ContextExpand` variant — confirmed via `decode_arguments`'s own comment (\"47 of 73 whose families have not landed\") and daemon dispatch order (decode precedes family lookup). Every call here builds a genuinely well-formed frame and gets `ErrorCode::UnsupportedSemanticFeature` back for real (`CodecError::UnknownOperation`'s mapped code) — proven against a real Daemon in `tests/context_expand.rs`. The success renderer (pack embedded verbatim as canonical JSON, manifest beside it) is unit-tested against real wire types directly so it's correct the day bn-28jj lands.\n\n## INV-007 non-suppressibility — the argument\n\n`render::omission_lines`/`omissions_json` render the FULL manifest, never a count (a deliberate departure from `continuum_benchmark::shell`'s documented count+expand-command handicap, which is for a byte-graded benchmark this bone isn't). JSON envelope always carries `omissions`, `[]` or not. `cli::Scan` has no suppression flag at all (checked by reading the parser). Tested: `context_expand.rs::the_json_envelope_always_carries_the_omissions_key`, `render.rs` unit tests.\n\n## Refusal rendering\n\nShared `wire::Refusal`/`render::refusal_lines`/`refusal_json`: `error.code` (typed, `as_wire()`, never a synonym), `.detail`, `.retryable`, `.recovery` count, `.continuation`, `.non_resumable_reason` — present-or-`none`, never silent. `task resume`'s StaleSnapshot path is wire-tested (not asserted from docs): `resume_refuses_a_continuation_whose_pinned_snapshot_the_lineage_superseded` parks Die Hard (budget 4→cost 3, continuumd's own documented off-by-one), forks the base snapshot past it (dx03_falsification.rs's attack-6 recipe, reproduced against the CLI's render path), asserts `error.code=StaleSnapshot`/`refused=true` in text+JSON and that the record is untouched. `ContinuationEpochMismatch`/`EpochUnsupported` share the same render path but aren't separately wire-exercised (would need a second, differently-epoched daemon for identical rendering — not worth the fixture weight).\n\n## task cancel — PR-6 contract, named\n\n`task::CancelOutcome::{ValidContinuation,NothingPublished,ClosedAndComplete}` mirrors `pr6_exit_evidence.rs`'s `ExitSide` for `rule task.cancel_correct`. Continuation present → full handle printed; absent → clean absence named, never silent. Both arms wire-tested: `cancel_of_a_suspended_task_reports_a_valid_continuation_and_prints_its_handle`, `cancel_of_a_completed_task_reports_a_clean_absence` (accepts either clean-absence shape — this daemon's publish-on-complete behavior wasn't a fact worth pinning).\n\n## Clause → test map\n\n| Clause | Test |\n|---|---|\n| expand surfaces manifest alongside slice | `context_expand.rs::the_success_renderer_prints_the_expanded_pack_beside_the_full_omission_manifest` (unit; live round trip unreachable, bn-28jj open) |\n| manifest non-suppressible/visible | render.rs unit tests + `the_json_envelope_always_carries_the_omissions_key` |\n| resume refuses stale epoch/inputs, typed reason | `resume_refuses_a_continuation_whose_pinned_snapshot_the_lineage_superseded` |\n| cancel: valid continuation or clean absence | `cancel_of_a_suspended_task_reports_a_valid_continuation...`, `cancel_of_a_completed_task_reports_a_clean_absence` |\n| status renders cost/budget/omissions faithfully | `status_renders_a_suspended_records_cost_budget_and_continuation_faithfully` |\n| rendering = wire projection (INV-003) | every renderer takes real continuumd types, no fabricated strings |\n| refusal paths tested, typed reasons in output | above resume test + `context_expand.rs::a_real_daemon_refuses_...` |\n\n## Counts / Gates\n\n24 new tests (15 unit + 4 context_expand + 5 task_lifecycle), all pass. `cargo test --workspace --locked`: 2,164 passed, 0 failed, all pre-existing intact. `cargo fmt --all --check`, `cargo clippy --workspace --all-targets --locked -- -D warnings` (missing_docs=deny), crate-boundary + governance (GOV-1-07 dependency-rationale) self-tests — all clean. Cargo.lock diff: 7 lines, continuum-cli's new edges only, no new external crate.\n\n`just dossier` false start: my first edit turned PR-13 into 4 top-level bullets, which `traceability.py::_extract_prs` reads as 4 new leaf requirements — 3 with no bone `plan-key:` (sibling bones out of scope to edit). Fixed by rewriting as flowing prose (no top-level `-` bullets, adds zero leaf requirements). `just traceability` regenerated cleanly (PLAN_BONE_TRACEABILITY.md byte-identical to before); validation-results.json untouched. **`just check` (full gate incl. Lean) — exit 0, end-to-end.**\n\n## Concerns, named honestly\n\n- No live daemon reaches `bin/continuum.rs` (continuumd infra gap, not this bone's to close).\n- context expand has zero live-success evidence (bn-28jj open) — unit-level only.\n- `--format pretty` is minimal (one header line over text; no color/tables) — `format`/`render`/`error` explicitly named as a starting instance for bn-ybh1z, not a claim on its scope.\n- Epoch-mismatch refusal codes render-complete but not wire-exercised.\n- `Justfile`'s `install:` comment is now stale (continuum-cli has a `[[bin]]` now) — left untouched, packaging is a bigger decision than this bone."}	blake3:clf7OVZaKHXA-Es7rz3mTTNZUMpQ_wiSbSllA8nPAqg
1785721404579381	continuum-dev	itc:v3:AWKSTzM5JJnJPkQAAAAAQar23VW6voAAAAEy9gk		item.comment	bn-3tz60	{"body":"Landed @ post-merge epoch. Lead re-verified post-sync: continuum-cli 24 tests green, workspace 2,164, gates clean.\n\nRATIFIED. (1) The honest refusal on context expand — every call today is UnsupportedSemanticFeature traced to decode_arguments, proven against a real daemon, with the success-path renderer unit-tested against real wire types so bn-28jj's landing makes it live without a CLI change. Refusing to fake a daemon (LinkError::NoTransportConfigured at exit 2) is the same discipline. (2) The dx03 attack-6 recipe reproduced as a CLI refusal test — the falsification campaigns are now regression infrastructure for OTHER crates' render paths, which is what retained evidence is for. (3) cancel rendering the three-way disjunction matching pr6_exit_evidence's ExitSide — one vocabulary, two surfaces. (4) INV-007 non-suppressible with the JSON omissions key unconditional. (5) The flowing-prose annotation lesson (bulleted sub-requirements fragment the registry when sibling bones lack plan-key labels) — noted for the loop.\n\nGAPS as named: context-expand live success waits on bn-28jj (PR-11 IMPL-04, next wave); the dialable daemon transport is continuumd infrastructure for a later PR (recorded, not bone'd — it rides the PR-13 exit's own integration story); pretty-format scoped to bn-ybh1z.\n\nPR-13 third command group satisfied via bullet annotation."}	blake3:oOaDgnyyKCbasKBTdZLhwbla394AMJfFOonbfmo85Lw
