1785873769637012	continuum-dev	itc:v3:AWKSTzM5JJnJPkQAAAAAQar23VW6voAAAAEy5Qo		item.comment	bn-2a8v	{"body":"Delivered in workspace `.maw/workspaces/bn-2a8v` at `a698d97` — \"feat: target/verdict/assurance typed references (bn-2a8v)\". Not merged, not closed; bone left in `doing`.\n\n**What the bullet turned out to be.** `target`/`verdict`/`assurance` are *not* three more `selected[].kind` members — `context-pack.schema.json`'s `kind` enum is the closed eleven IMPL-03 already transcribed and has no such token. RFC 0028's normative mapping table (\"Required fields, reconciled with plan §6.2\") homes the three words as the pack's **answer header**: `intent` + `question` (the \"target intent and property\" row), `verdict` + `inconclusive_reason`, and `assurance` = `{class, envelope}` (the \"exact verdict and assurance envelope\" row). So the delivery is three typed field groups that each emit the `(key, value)` pairs they own — fragments of a pack, never a pack, because whole-pack assembly is the compiler's and no single IMPL bullet's (`selection`'s decline, unreversed).\n\n**Files.**\n- `crates/continuum-context/src/target.rs` — `Target` (class-checked `in_*` `ArtifactHandle` + `Question`), `Question` with exactly the RFC's two constructors (`compiled`, `of_expansion` over IMPL-04's `ExpansionQuestion`), `QuestionError`, `TargetError`.\n- `crates/continuum-context/src/verdict.rs` — the closed four, `Verdict::Inconclusive(InconclusiveReason)`, `from_wire`, `VerdictError`.\n- `crates/continuum-context/src/assurance.rs` — `Assurance { class: AssuranceLevel, envelope: AssuranceEnvelope }` (both reused from `continuum_value::assurance`), the nine-dimension encoder.\n- `crates/continuum-context/tests/pr11_impl01_target_verdict_assurance_references.rs` — 11 tests.\n- `crates/continuum-context/src/lib.rs` — three `pub mod` lines, one doc paragraph, and one surgical correction: the \"Declined here\" paragraph named target/verdict/assurance as IMPL-01's *undelivered* scope and no longer does. **Lead note:** the same sentence still names the replay reference (IMPL-05); the sibling delivering that bullet will want the rest of the clause, so expect a small conflict there.\n\n**Discipline carried over from IMPL-03.**\n- **Not the IDL's `Target`.** `struct Target { kind: TargetKind, id }` is `verification.start`'s request shape; the pack schema has no `target` key and declares `additionalProperties: false`, and RFC 0028 says a §6.2 bullet with no schema home \"is a defect in one of the two documents, never a licence to invent a field\". `snapshot` is declined by the mirror image of that reasoning (RFC 0028 sources it to plan §4.2, among the four required properties §6.2 does not name).\n- **INV-008 unrepresentable, not validated.** The schema's `allOf[0]` conditional has no failing instance left: `Inconclusive` carries its reason, `to_json_fields` emits `inconclusive_reason` exactly when the variant is that one, and a `compile_fail` doctest pins that `Inconclusive` is not a unit variant. Same discipline `omission::Retrievability` used for the two conditionals on `expandable`.\n- **INV-016 gains no new fabrication route.** `SelectedItem::new` stays `pub(crate)`, none of the three modules calls it, and a new `compile_fail` doctest (with a passing anti-vacuity companion) pins that a `Question` — the one caller-authored string this bullet carries — cannot become a `selected[].summary` from outside the crate. A rejected question is never echoed into its own error, which names a byte offset instead.\n- **Per-key artifact discipline**, decided by the schema: the header names exactly one artifact, the `in_*` intent, class-checked like `ModelActionRef::with_model`; `verdict` is a bare enum string and `assurance` is `{class, envelope}` with `additionalProperties: false`, so neither has a field a handle could occupy. Asserted by parsing every string in both fragments through `ArtifactHandle::from_str` rather than a prefix heuristic — `proof_status` is a dimension *name* that starts with a registered class token and is not a handle (the first version of that test failed on exactly this).\n- **Canonical encoding** via `continuum_intent::canonical_json` (ID5), determinism asserted both directions, plus `rule ordering.deterministic` over independently built target lists and over envelopes whose dimensions were set in different orders.\n\n**Reuse decisions.** `AssuranceLevel` (five schema tokens, derived `Ord` = RFC 0028's \"RFC 0031 total order\" for this field) and `AssuranceEnvelope` (already the mirror of `assurance-result.schema.json`; cannot be built with a dimension missing, so `rule envelope.assurance_required` is a property of the type) and `InconclusiveReason` are taken from `continuum_value::assurance` rather than re-declared. `continuumd` declares its own `AssuranceClass` beside them, but for a reason that does not apply here — its `protocol_enum!` types generate a wire codec.\n\n**Three things worth the lead's attention.**\n1. **A stated narrowing.** The schema *permits* `inconclusive_reason` beside a decided verdict (the `allOf` only ever adds a requirement). `Verdict` cannot spell that and `from_wire` refuses it, because a reason attached to `satisfied` is a document with two readings. A closed conditional at that key is raised for the schema sweep; no schema was edited.\n2. **`Question` is printable-ASCII-with-spaces**, on the identity reasoning `Name`/`UnsupportedReason` already state. Real cost, recorded rather than hidden: no non-Latin-script question until a normalizer this crate does not have lands.\n3. **`in_*` has a producer in-tree**, unlike IMPL-03's `model_*`: `IntentContract::mint_intent_id` derives `in_<digest>` (RFC 0037 ID1), and `an_intent_id_drops_straight_into_the_slot` pins that `IntentId` and `ArtifactHandle` spell it identically. What is declined is *resolution* against the daemon's intent registry.\n\n**Also declined:** whole-pack assembly; the SD-12 identity check of the envelope copy against `assurance-result.schema.json` (that is `validate_dossier.py`'s, and reusing the one Rust type both schemas describe is how this stays on the right side of it); \"a pack MUST NOT report an envelope stronger than the result's\" (second operand reaches no crate this one depends on); reporting an envelope *narrowing* in the manifest (needs a compile stage no bullet has built).\n\n**Bookkeeping.** START_HERE bullet annotated in the house style; `python3 notes/plan/tools/generate_traceability.py` run in-workspace and the regenerated `PLAN_REQUIREMENTS.json` / `PLAN_BONE_TRACEABILITY.md` committed with the work (`PR-11-IMPL-01` flips `active` → `satisfied`).\n\n**Gates, all exit 0, from the workspace root.** `cargo fmt --all --check`; `cargo clippy --all-targets --locked -- -D warnings`; `cargo test -p continuum-context --locked` → 139 passing; full `just check` → 0, **2,502 passing**. Measured baseline at this workspace's base commit `1bedd42` is **2,461** (stash-and-run), so the delta is **+41** = 26 unit + 11 integration + 2 `compile_fail` doctests + 2 passing doctests. The 2,460 figure in my brief is one below this workspace's base — a different commit, not a lost test."}	blake3:HBXPArfLACfzhsaeF6FPRD9PNyKZE_HyGh3BYiI7tEI
1785873870401385	continuum-dev	itc:v3:AWKSTzM5JJnJPkQAAAAAQar23VW6voAAAAEy5go		item.comment	bn-2a8v	{"body":"Lead: reviewed and merged @ epoch 371de07. Corrective reading RATIFIED (second of the wave): target/verdict/assurance are the pack's ANSWER HEADER field groups per RFC 0028's mapping table, not selection kinds — the closed eleven has no such tokens, and inventing a schema field would violate the RFC's own no-licence-to-invent rule. Ratified per group: Target = class-checked in_* + typed two-form Question, NOT the IDL's verification.start Target (different surface); Verdict's Inconclusive CARRIES InconclusiveReason (INV-008 unrepresentable, compile_fail-pinned non-unit variant); Assurance wholesale-reuses continuum_value (derived Ord IS the total order; envelope-with-no-missing-dimension makes envelope.assurance_required a type property). The stated narrowing (refusing inconclusive_reason beside a decided verdict) rides the schema sweep beside RFC 0028 F13. The artifact-discipline test self-correction (prefix heuristic → ArtifactHandle::from_str) is the right paranoia. NOTE: lib.rs 'Declined here' paragraph is now stale about kind ownership — lead will restore truth in one edit after bn-2l1e lands. 139 context tests, 2,502 workspace."}	blake3:O1XZAp5znILUai76QR8z6NBkY2SK_nrH9NCLUpnjcuM
1785873870433432	continuum-dev	itc:v3:AWKSTzM5JJnJPkQAAAAAQar23VW6voAAAAEy5wo		item.move	bn-2a8v	{"state":"done"}	blake3:PF5_jf7VZz7mL2EpR02Sov1DCgLhNi8TT0MlVbegQto
1785873952992009	continuum-dev	itc:v3:AWKSTzM5JJnJPkQAAAAAQar23VW6voAAAAEy6Ao		item.comment	bn-2l1e	{"body":"Delivered: `crates/continuum-context/src/{event,state_delta}.rs`, following the IMPL-03 precedent (bn-16ek) exactly.\n\n**What each kind carries, and why**\n\n- `EventRef` (`selected[].kind = \"event\"`) — RFC 0028's \"causal core and surrounding frontier\" row, docs/38's two-member causal-core split: `event: Name` + `role: EventRole` (`Observed | CausalPredecessor`, docs/38's own wording — \"events directly observed by the property; causal predecessors\"), plus an optional artifact. The event identifier is `continuum_value::value::Name`, not a real CIR `EventId`: RFC 0001 fixes `EventId` as a semantic hash (`H(cir_semantics_version, origin, actor_epoch, …)`) and `schemas/cir.schema.json` fixes its wire spelling, but `continuum-cir` (docs/01 §4.2, PR 17) is an unopened scaffold with no `Event`/`EventId` type — building that hash construction here would invent `continuum-cir`'s own artifact ahead of the bone that owns it, the same overreach `ModelActionRef::with_model` already declined for `continuum-cml-elab`'s `model_*` handles. `EventRef::with_execution_graph` class-checks a real handle against `ArtifactClass::CausalExecutionGraph` (plan §4.4 `cir_*` — RFC 0001's own event set), refusing every other class; `EventRef::new` carries none.\n- `StateDeltaRef` (`selected[].kind = \"state_delta\"`) — RFC 0028's \"concrete and abstract state deltas\" row, docs/38's \"State delta\" example: `variable: Name`, `class: StateDeltaClass` (RFC 0028's own two words, `Concrete`/`Abstract`), `before: Option<Value>`, `after: Value`. Value domain: `continuum_value::value::Value`, deliberately **not** the reference engine's `i64` state vector — `continuum-engine-reference::domain`'s own module doc states outright that `Value`'s richer lattice \"is the right vocabulary for the CIR\" (where a state delta lives — docs/38's pipeline computes it *from* the normalized causal graph) and that `i64` is the certificate-bound engine's own narrower thing, \"not a dependency of this one\". Every docs/38 example row is representable without a coercion `i64` cannot express: `replies[e7] reserved → published` as `Value::Symbol`, `acknowledged[e7] false → true` as `Value::Bool`. `StateDeltaRef::new` refuses `before == Some(after)` — a record naming no change is not a delta.\n\n**INV-016 shape**\n\nReuses the mechanism IMPL-03 already built, unchanged: `SelectedItem::new` stays `pub(crate)`, and `EventRef::into_selected_item`/`StateDeltaRef::into_selected_item` are its third and fourth callers, taking no string parameter — an `event`/`state_delta` item's summary is synthesized only from typed fields. Canonical encoding reuses `continuum_intent::canonical_json` unchanged; no second writer, no edit to `selection.rs`.\n\n**Declined, honestly**\n\n- A real CIR `EventId` and any cross-item event↔delta linkage (docs/38's `[e7]` keying) — `continuum-cir` is PR 17's unopened scaffold, and `selected[]` items carry no sibling-reference field to invent one on.\n- A standalone artifact for a state delta — plan §4.4's nineteen-member class list names none; the closest object, `crashpack.schema.json`'s `artifacts.state_diff`, is a bare unreconciled Revision-2-era string with no `ArtifactClass` token.\n- Rendering fidelity for `Value`'s composite kinds (set/record/map/…) beyond `Debug` — total, never panics, but no corpus fixture this bone exercises one.\n\n**Files**\n\n- `crates/continuum-context/src/event.rs` (new)\n- `crates/continuum-context/src/state_delta.rs` (new)\n- `crates/continuum-context/tests/pr11_impl02_state_event_slice_references.rs` (new, 6 tests)\n- `crates/continuum-context/src/lib.rs` (two `pub mod` lines + one doc paragraph; corrected the now-stale \"declined\" list that named `event`/`state_delta`)\n- `notes/plan/notes/START_HERE_IMPLEMENTATION.md` (delivered annotation on the \"state and event slice\" bullet)\n- `notes/plan/notes/{PLAN_BONE_TRACEABILITY.md,PLAN_REQUIREMENTS.json}` (regenerated via `generate_traceability.py`)\n\nDid not touch `selection.rs` (not structurally required) or any protocol/IDL/schema file, and added no new crate dependency — `continuum-value` was already a dependency; `continuum-engine-reference` and `continuum-cir` are not depended on.\n\n**Gates (from workspace root)**\n\n- `cargo fmt --all --check` — clean\n- `cargo clippy --all-targets --locked -- -D warnings` — clean (workspace-wide)\n- `cargo test -p continuum-context --locked` — 95 lib unit tests + 6 new integration tests + 7 (IMPL-03) + 10 (IMPL-06) + 1 doctest, all green\n- `just check` (fmt-check, lint, test, boundaries, covenant, governance, dossier, lean) — exit 0\n- Workspace test count: **2,482** passed, 0 failed (baseline 2,460; this bone adds 21: 15 unit + 6 integration)\n\n**Anything surprising**\n\nThe two value-domain candidates for a state delta (`continuum_value::value::Value` vs. the reference engine's `i64` state vector) looked interchangeable at first glance, but `continuum-engine-reference/src/domain.rs`'s own module documentation settles it explicitly in `Value`'s favor for CIR-level content (\"the right vocabulary for the CIR … That crate is not a dependency of this one\") — worth citing directly since it's the deciding text and not something either RFC 0028 or docs/38 states outright. Also: `schemas/cir.schema.json` and `crashpack.schema.json` both exist and are schema-normative even though their owning crates (`continuum-cir`, and the crashpack wiring) are unopened — real, checked-in vocabulary I read but did not build against, on the same declined-scope ground as `model_*` in IMPL-03.\n\nBone left in `doing`; no merge/close/push performed."}	blake3:Fr6CsEc5ZGZxFq8n5Fsgs4puxas2la_8fngkk3TpZXo
1785874091435088	continuum-dev	itc:v3:AWKSTzM5JJnJPkQAAAAAQar23VW6voAAAAEy6Qo		item.comment	bn-2l1e	{"body":"Lead: reviewed and merged @ epoch 04ff53b. Ratifications: (1) EventRef's identifier is Name, NOT a constructed CIR EventId — RFC 0001 fixes EventId as a semantic hash owned by unopened continuum-cir (PR 17), and building the hash here would invent another bone's artifact; with_execution_graph class-checks cir_* per the with_model pattern. (2) StateDeltaRef over continuum_value::Value not the engine's i64 — decided by continuum-engine-reference/domain.rs's OWN module doc naming Value as CIR's vocabulary; refuses before==Some(after). (3) Declined-scope honesty on EventId linkage, standalone delta artifacts (crashpack's state_diff is an unreconciled Rev-2 string — noted), and composite rendering. LEAD RESOLUTION at merge: the lib.rs 'Declined here' paragraph was three-ways stale — final truth written in one edit: four typed constructors (IMPL-03 source/model, IMPL-02 event/state_delta), the other seven kinds owned by NO PR-11 bullet, carried through expansions unclaimed — IMPL-01/05 turned out to own the answer header and the replay field, not kinds. Full context suite green post-resolution (127 lib + all integration), clippy clean. PR-11 bullets now complete except the compiler pipeline and exit case."}	blake3:dd8OFp4WX3DkY7RtkeCvGhKZC_WuJstjGr46ZAJ2uZY
