1785875118338302	continuum-dev	itc:v3:AWKSTzM5JJnJPkQAAAAAQar23VW6voAAAAEy8Qo		item.comment	bn-2688c	{"body":"DECISION: retired, with pointer — not regenerated.\n\nWHY: `validate_dossier.py` (notes/plan/tools/validate_dossier.py) has zero reference to VALIDATION_REPORT.md — it never asserted the file's existence or shape, so retiring it doesn't touch the validator's own checks (confirmed by grep before and after). The file itself was hand-authored once during Revision 3 authoring and hand-edited across five commits total (86ed17e, 3d06ba7, dd9d45e, 28daa25, cb8f2ac — last touch 2026-07-29, cb8f2ac, itself a manual patch of embedded pass/fail counts), never regenerated by any script. Meanwhile validation-results.json in the same directory has been regenerated on effectively every bone close since (hundreds of \"regen\" commits in git log). The staleness isn't limited to the SD ledger the bone named: live `check_spec_debt` today shows all fourteen SD items paid (open: []) vs the file's \"open: SD-01, SD-07, SD-08, SD-09, SD-10\"; the file's traceability line's five embedded counts (846 registered requirements / 827 active-and-covered / 904 active Bones / 796 leaves / 2,119 edges) are also stale — none match a live run. That's the lead's own prior confirmed: a prose duplicate of a machine-regenerated JSON file drifts again by construction, so it's retired rather than patched with fresh numbers (which would just recreate the same problem on the next close).\n\nWHAT REFERENCES IT (grepped notes/plan, tools/, notes/plan/tools/, top-level tools/):\n- notes/plan/tools/validate_dossier.py and top-level tools/*.py — no reference at all (confirmed, safe to retire).\n- README.md (root) item 7, notes/plan/README.md prose pointer — both live entry-point docs, updated to describe VALIDATION_REPORT.md as retired and point to validation-results.json as the live source.\n- notes/plan/plan.md — two citations updated: the Lean evidence-boundary bullet (§0.3, was citing \"(VALIDATION_REPORT.md, docs/18 C035)\", now cites \"(validation-results.json lean_source check, docs/18 C035)\"), and the §25 opener's regen-discipline sentence (dropped the VALIDATION_REPORT.md half of \"VALIDATION_REPORT.md / validation-results.json are regenerated\", since only the latter still is).\n- notes/plan/plan.review.{1,4,5}.md, notes/plan/archive/README-revision-2.md — left untouched: these are dated historical review/archive documents describing the dossier as it stood at review/authoring time, not live docs (plan.review.*.md is explicitly excluded from the validator's retired-name scan for the same reason).\n- notes/plan/plan.typ — left untouched: confirmed no generator script references it (grepped tools/ and Justfile), and it's already independently stale for unrelated reasons per bn-2br's prior comment (\"plan.typ ... is a generated render with no validator check\") — same scoping precedent applied here.\n- .bones/events/*.events — immutable event log, never edited.\n\nWHAT I DID: rewrote notes/plan/VALIDATION_REPORT.md as a retirement/pointer doc (no live numbers embedded — only the old, now-frozen stale numbers quoted as evidence for *why* it was retired): explains what it was, why it drifted, points to validation-results.json as the live report, documents who regenerates it and when (the lead, as a fixed step of the bone-close sequence, after generate_traceability.py, whenever a merged bone could move validator-visible state — not per-commit, not CI), and documents the scratchpad-then-cp regen mechanic (never `python3 tools/validate_dossier.py > validation-results.json` directly — the shell truncates the destination to 0 bytes before the process starts, and the validator's own `empty_files` check scans the whole tree including that file mid-run, so a direct redirect fails against its own not-yet-written output). Pointed the narrative Lean/spike/corpus boundary paragraphs at their canonical live homes (docs/18 C035, docs/53, spikes/R3_SPIKE_REPORT.md, corpus/tla-examples/check_inventory.py) instead of restating them. Kept the Reproduction command block (still accurate).\n\nEditing plan.md shifted line numbers, so I regenerated notes/plan/notes/PLAN_REQUIREMENTS.json via `tools/generate_traceability.py` (146-line diff, pure `source.line` shifts — verified, no structural change) to keep `plan_bones_traceability` green; PLAN_BONE_TRACEABILITY.md content was unaffected. Did NOT touch notes/plan/validation-results.json (fenced off — that's the lead's regen at close/merge time, per the file's own newly-documented discipline).\n\nGATES: `cd notes/plan && uv run --with jsonschema python3 tools/validate_dossier.py` → \"status\": \"pass\" (spec_debt open: [], all 14 paid). Full `just check` from workspace root (fmt-check, lint, test, boundaries, covenant, governance, dossier, lean) → exit 0, all tests green, Lean build green, axiom manifest up to date.\n\nFiles touched: README.md, notes/plan/README.md, notes/plan/VALIDATION_REPORT.md, notes/plan/plan.md, notes/plan/notes/PLAN_REQUIREMENTS.json. Committed in-workspace @ 9c1e5d1. Bone left in doing; no merge/close/push."}	blake3:NxzhkZ62O42qMFmd9OFUClqNx3LxL4ionIUx4EszwdM
1785875154648131	continuum-dev	itc:v3:AWKSTzM5JJnJPkQAAAAAQar23VW6voAAAAEy8go		item.comment	bn-2688c	{"body":"Lead: retirement ratified and merged @ epoch 0c8f827. The evidence base was exactly right: hand-authored, hand-patched five times, never script-generated, stale on BOTH the SD ledger and its embedded traceability counts — while validation-results.json regenerates at every close. Pointer doc quotes the frozen numbers as drift evidence rather than asserting new ones (no hand-edited numbers, per the bone's own rule), documents the lead regen discipline including the scratchpad-then-cp mechanic and WHY direct redirect fails. Live entry points (both READMEs) and plan.md's two citations moved to the live JSON; archived/historical reviews correctly left frozen. Validator green, spec_debt open: []."}	blake3:oZgVTkDu51a7Gr8XCMykcjmuyi9woJlKdyTMR7yGq5c
