1785881228976065	continuum-dev	itc:v3:AWKSTzM5JJnJPkQAAAAAQar23VW6voAAAAEyhgs		item.comment	bn-14dqx	{"body":"Synced plan.typ's §24.5 frontier register (~line 2716-2812, now 2716-2882) to plan.md's ratified rows. plan.typ carried zero `quote-id=` markers before this change (fully unratified snapshot); plan.md has 6.\n\n**Rows updated in place (existing typ rows, wording only):**\n- **FR-01** General context compilation (§6): \"win margin fixed at ratification — draft\" → ratified text with `quote-id=context-compilation-win-margin` (the 10-pp win-margin / 10x byte-reduction / hidden-variant-generalization threshold).\n- **FR-04** Causal minimization (§6, §12): \"≤10% of trace length — draft, pending ratification\" → ratified text with `quote-id=causal-minimization-core-ratio` (same ≤10% figure, now with the corpus-definition clause plan.md added).\n- **FR-05** Neighborhood adequacy (§8.3): Lane cell \"research/33 --- lane to be opened\" → \"research/33\" (lane is open); Threshold \"target fixed at lane opening — draft\" → ratified text with `quote-id=neighborhood-adequacy-catch-rate` (90% overall catch / 80% one-sided lower bound / 75% per-class floor).\n\n**Rows added (did not exist in plan.typ's table at all — table had only 17 rows, plan.md has 21):**\n- **FR-18** Agent–computer interface (B2, §10) — new row, `quote-id=aci-benchmark-margins` (10-pp success margin, 30% byte reduction, 50% invalid-action reduction).\n- **FR-20** Workbench security (§18) — new row, `quote-id=workbench-security-promotion-gate` (45-case red-team corpus gate).\n- **FR-21** Multi-agent evidence graph enforcement (§11.7) — new row, `quote-id=evidence-graph-enforcement` (the four §11.7 properties under bounded-model + adversarial-campaign verification).\n\nInserted 18/20/21 in plan.md's row order, after the existing 17th row (Timed/probabilistic semantics).\n\n**Further drift found, left alone (out of scope, no quote-id in plan.md):** row 19, Explanation science (§12), is also absent from plan.typ's table. plan.md still has this row as draft (no `quote-id`), so per the no-invented-ratification instruction I did not add it. Flagging so the next sync pass (or this bone, if grown further) adds it once research/34 ratifies.\n\n**No md/typ content conflicts found** beyond the staleness itself — plan.typ's Lane/Fallback cells for the six rows already matched plan.md wherever plan.md hadn't changed them (e.g. FR-01/FR-04 Lane and Fallback cells were already correct; only FR-05's Lane cell needed a second-column fix alongside the Threshold cell).\n\n**Verification:**\n- `typst compile` (typst 0.14.2, available via mise) on the edited plan.typ succeeds with only the pre-existing, unrelated \"unknown font family: liberation sans\" warning — table markup is valid. Did not commit a regenerated plan.pdf (not requested; source-sync was the deliverable).\n- `just check` from the workspace: exit 0. Dossier validator's `register_rows` check reports `\"rows\": 21, \"ratified_quotes_checked\": 6\"` against plan.md (confirms all six FR-NN rows are the ones I mirrored) — plan.typ is not read by the validator, unaffected either way.\n\nNote for the lead: mid-task I initially edited the trunk-root copy of notes/plan/plan.typ by mistake (wrong path) before realizing my error; caught it before committing anything, stashed and dropped that stray change, and redid all edits correctly inside .maw/workspaces/bn-14dqx/. Trunk root was verified clean (only unrelated concurrent-agent .bones/events activity, never touched by me) before I proceeded.\n\nLeft in `doing`. No merge/close/push performed."}	blake3:NGH91g8Z6zb6dLodYYECwzR2E5hOHvw4uczROJzjaw8
