1785882147447643	continuum-dev	itc:v3:AWKSTzM5JJnJPkQAAAAAQar23VW6voAAAAEyiQs		item.comment	bn-3ehdm	{"body":"IMPL delivered: `tools/governance/check_revision_delta.py` — the two-revision half of GOV-1-08/09, wired into the `governance` recipe. Commit 5134ee3 in .maw/workspaces/bn-3ehdm. Nothing merged, pushed or closed.\n\n## The two delta rules\n\n`semantic-change-adr-delta` (GOV-1-08):\n- `semantic-change-cites-a-decision-record` — a semantic-tier source file whose *code* changed between base and head must cite `ADR-NNNN`/`RFC NNNN` at head, unless the delta itself adds or modifies a record under notes/plan/adr|rfcs/ (the other accepted form: the change ships with its decision).\n- `added-semantic-source-cites-a-decision-record` — a file the delta *adds* must cite one regardless; an unrelated ADR edit does not excuse a new module.\n\n\"Semantic tier\" is not invented: the checker imports `check_code_policy.SEMANTIC_CORE`, the same 27-crate partition GOV-1-03/04/05 use and `tier-partition-covers-plan-20` holds to plan 20, so the halves cannot drift. \"Changed\" = comment-stripped, whitespace-normalized text differs, so a doc rewrite or `cargo fmt` pass is not a semantic change. The house inline waiver is honoured with its 12-char reason floor, file-scoped, listed in `waivers_granted`.\n\n`epoch-discipline-delta` (GOV-1-09):\n- `schema-bytes-changed-without-epoch-advance` — schemas/*.schema.json bytes changed, `schema_epoch` unmoved (also fires when the epoch is unreadable either side). FREEZE-GATED.\n- `published-schema-document-deleted` — at base, gone at head. FREEZE-GATED.\n- `schema-epoch-never-retreats` — epoch went down. Every regime; the counter is monotone.\n- `epoch-advance-publishes-a-compatibility-statement` — an advance with no markdown in the same delta naming that class with Preserved/Revalidate/Incompatible. Every regime: plan 4.6 wants it *before* the advance, and the pre-freeze clause excuses in-place edits, not advances.\n\nFREEZE-GATED = read from schemas/README.md's own clause at head (\"Until PR 5 freezes the interface ... epoch 1 is a draft ... edited in place\"). While present, those two checks emit DEFERRED findings — printed on stderr, listed under `deferred`, not failures; when it goes they become violations. Absent or reworded reads as *in force*: doubt fails closed. `--freeze` overrides.\n\n## Base resolution and degradation\n\n`--base <rev>`, else `git merge-base HEAD main` falling back to `origin/main`. Head defaults to the WORKING TREE (untracked included via `ls-files --others`, so an added-but-unstaged source is not invisible); `--head <rev>` for a revision. No resolvable base (no work tree, no `git`, unborn HEAD, no trunk ref, shallow checkout) -> prints the reason on stderr, reports `\"status\": \"skip\"` with the resolution trail, and states the delta rules were NOT enforced. Exit 0 by default (a fresh clone must not fail the local gate); exit 1 under `--require-base`, which is how CI says a base is owed. An explicit `--base` that does not resolve is a HARD FAILURE, not a skip — a wrong input must not degrade into a pass. A base that resolves but a `git diff`/`ls-files` that fails is an explained skip too, not an empty delta read as \"nothing changed\". No path reports a pass it did not earn. The guard is in the checker, not the Justfile: a shell guard would duplicate the resolution logic and could disagree with it.\n\n## Fixtures and self-test\n\n15 base->head PAIRS under `fixtures/delta/<id>/` (54 files): a `base` map, a `head` map, `expect: violation|deferred|clean`. 7 violating pairs cover all six sub-checks (a check with no violating pair fails the self-test as vacuous); 1 deferred pair proves the pre-freeze branch defers rather than passes; 7 passing pairs prove the allowed shapes do not trip — change landing with its ADR, file already citing its record, comment-only edit, boundary-tier crate, waived change, new cited file, advance with its statement. One violating pair's waiver reason is 4 chars: unusable reasons are reported, not honoured.\n\nPairs are hermetic (a delta rule's whole input *is* its pair), so the self-test needs no git and no repo state — but they rot loudly the one way they can: every crates/<name>/ path must still be a crate `check_code_policy.py` classifies. The self-test also drives 11 base-resolution scenarios through a stubbed git and the exit-code policy as a pure function. Mutation-checked: silencing rule 08 or 09 fails it (5 and 9 failures), as does forcing the freeze reading (4).\n\n## Evidence\n\n- `evidence/gov-1.json`: GOV-1-08/09 `boundary` rewritten — the \"PROXY ... needs a revision-diff gate\" caveat is gone, replaced by what each half now enforces and what genuinely remains (whether the cited record *governs* the change is still docs/12 s4 review; the pre-freeze deferral; a breaking IDL/RFC change touching no schema file). New `delta_gate` field per requirement names the two-revision rule and its checks (null for the other ten).\n- `evidence/gov-1-delta.json` (new): rules, sub-checks, pairs proven caught, degradation matrix, freeze regime, boundary — and NO run verdict on purpose, since a run is a function of two revisions rather than of the tree and recording it would break the house byte-for-byte rule. Verified identical across reruns and `--base` values.\n- `README-gov1.md`: \"The two-revision gate\" section, \"Known gaps\" item 1 replaced (was \"No revision-diff gate\"), running/wiring/evidence updated, and \"What the delta gate finds on the current tree\" pinning the findings below.\n\n- docs/12 s1: the sentence calling this gate \"follow-up work\" now names the file, rewritten LINE-NEUTRALLY (2 lines for 2) so PLAN_REQUIREMENTS.json source lines do not shift — registry byte-unchanged, no regen needed. The \"(delivered: bn-...)\" annotation is yours.\n\n## Real findings — pinned, not fixed\n\nDefault base = empty delta = pass. Against the first commit (`--base \"$(git rev-list --max-parents=0 HEAD)\"`):\n\n1. 21 SEMANTIC-CORE FILES CARRY CODE AND CITE NO DECISION RECORD — invisible to the crate-scoped single-revision rule because each of those crates has *some* citing file. All 21 pinned in README-gov1.md (certificate/family.rs, twelve lib.rs, five engine-reference modules, task/region/schedule.rs, workspace/{diff,seal}.rs). Not fixed here — this bone adds enforcement, not edits to the enforced — and `just check` does not fail on them, since the gate judges deltas: each is asked for a record when next touched.\n2. 15 SCHEMA DOCUMENTS EDITED IN PLACE since the first commit with no epoch advance (all 15 named in README-gov1.md: assurance-result, cir, context-pack, domain-pack, intent-contract, workspace-snapshot among them) — all DEFERRED, correct pre-freeze. That is the blast radius the PR 5 freeze inherits: when the draft clause goes, each is a violation unless its epoch moved.\n\nNOISE: replayed commit-by-commit over the 40 most recent trunk commits it reports ONE violation (8b0b130, continuum-context/src/lib.rs, no cited record and no ADR in the delta — since fixed on trunk) and ONE deferred finding (f6c3247, in-place context-pack.schema.json edit). 103 of 124 semantic-core files already cite a record.\n\nYour call: since head defaults to the working tree, an agent editing an uncited semantic-core file without touching an ADR now fails `just check` in their workspace. That is the obligation working (fix = a citation, an ADR, or a waiver), but it is a live change for in-flight work; `--head HEAD` judges only committed work if you want it softer.\n\n## Gates\n\n`just check` exit 0 from the workspace root (fmt, clippy, test, boundaries, covenant, governance x6, dossier, lean); `just governance` exit 0 with the checker wired in.\n\n    --self-test: \"status\":\"pass\",\"fixture_pairs\":15,\"failures\":[]; 6 checks / 7 violating\n                 pairs; 1 deferred; 7 passing; 11 base_resolution_cases\n    real run:    \"status\":\"pass\", base 718cc7275474 (merge-base with main), head \"the\n                 working tree\", freeze in_force:false, violations:[], deferred:[]\n    --base nope: exit 1 \"FAILED\"; --root <non-git>: exit 0 \"skip\" / 1 with --require-base\n\nStdlib only, no new dependency; the only subprocess is `git`, called with `--no-renames` and `core.quotepath=false` so the answer depends on neither rename heuristics nor local config (INV-005)."}	blake3:DqqOyCgY_J7Od47encUbPcEqkaH_wi-03XZaUDNNwxk
1785882281547752	continuum-dev	itc:v3:AWKSTzM5JJnJPkQAAAAAQar23VW6voAAAAEyigs		item.comment	bn-3ehdm	{"body":"Addendum (hash + post-rebase re-verification): maw rebased the workspace onto trunk fa32bfe after the comment above was written, so the commit is now 7156ec4, not 5134ee3 — same content, new parent. Re-verified on the rebased tree: `just check` exit 0 again (fmt, clippy, test, boundaries, covenant, governance x6, dossier, lean); the delta gate resolves base fa32bfed2419 by merge-base with main and reports status pass over 61 changed files with no semantic-tier source and no schema document in the delta; regenerating both evidence files (gov-1.json, gov-1-delta.json) against the rebased tree leaves them byte-identical, so nothing in the merged work moved the policy state. Working tree clean; bone untouched otherwise."}	blake3:kxQ7victQiys_EkmINoLRdBVjjn5fzGqH7H88VFC0fY
1785882408826058	continuum-dev	itc:v3:AWKSTzM5JJnJPkQAAAAAQar23VW6voAAAAEyiws		item.comment	bn-3ehdm	{"body":"Lead: merged @ epoch fccda6ae5b50. check_revision_delta.py lands as the sixth governance checker — GOV-1-08 (semantic-change-cites-a-decision-record + added-semantic-source variant, comment/format-only edits excluded, file-scoped waivers honoured) and GOV-1-09 (schema-bytes/deletion freeze-gated as deferred pre-freeze; epoch-never-retreats + compatibility-statement always in force). Shared SEMANTIC_CORE/strip_rust_comments/waiver imports from check_code_policy.py so the one-revision and two-revision halves cannot drift. 15 hermetic fixture pairs, mutation-checked both directions; explained-skip (not silent pass) on missing base or failed git subprocess. just governance green on trunk post-merge with the delta gate live. Lead judgement on the flagged default: working-tree head STANDS — a worker touching uncited semantic-core code should fail in-workspace where the fix (citation or reasoned waiver) is cheapest; --head HEAD remains available if noise appears. The 21 pinned uncited semantic-core files and 15 pre-freeze in-place schema edits in README-gov1.md are inherited blast radius for the PR 5 freeze, correctly pinned not fixed. Closing."}	blake3:beqIkIvoo1ARU3ZAxP-6v0eGnFPRHA8aTDIGFMBq7IA
