1785883422593191	continuum-dev	itc:v3:AWKSTzM5JJnJPkQAAAAAQar23VW6voAAAAEykws		item.comment	bn-7vg7	{"body":"PR-12 / IMPL-03 delivered: crates/continuum-semantic-diff/src/assumptions.rs, RFC 0031's `assumptions` field classification over continuum-intent's AssumptionSet, closed over continuum-intent::change_policy::Relation (no second vocabulary, no second order).\n\nWHAT RFC 0031 SPECIFIES for assumptions (read from the RFC text, not intuition):\n- Unit of classification: one assumption, keyed by `id` (same as `properties`). Membership: a unit present on one side only classifies added/removed.\n- For a unit present on both sides, the relation is computed on `expression` \"exactly as for claims — the same order, on the same normal form\" — i.e. behavior-set inclusion over CPNF-1, with NO antitone dual. This differs from `fairness[].condition`, which sits in an antitone position (weaker condition -> stronger constraint) and therefore needs `dualize`. An assumption's expression has no such inversion.\n- Direction inverts in *danger*, not in mechanism: for `properties`, `weakened` is the gaming move; for `assumptions`, `strengthened` is — \"an assumption strengthened admits fewer environments and makes verification easier.\" This matches plan §5.3 (assumption strengthening is one of the seven G3 dimensions) and docs/50 (\"strengthen assumptions\" is its own attack class). Confirmed against RFC 0037's INV-001 framing per the brief.\n- `classification`/`fidelity_profile` changed with an unchanged expression MUST classify `incomparable` — implemented literally, scoped to exactly that case (expression held fixed).\n- `source` is display-only and MUST NOT affect classification (R2/CPNF-1 interaction) — implemented via `expression_unchanged`, which compares `ast`+`fragment` only, never `PropertyExpression`'s derived `PartialEq` (which includes `source`).\n\nDIVERGENCES / GAPS RECORDED (annotated, not silently decided):\n1. No Finite-fragment inclusion oracle exists yet anywhere in continuum-intent (confirmed: `property.rs` and `assumptions.rs` both defer classification explicitly to \"RFC 0031's question (PR 12)\", and bn-8mlg/IMPL-02 — the `properties` bone that would land such an oracle — has not landed). So an unequal expression classifies `unknown`, never a guessed `strengthened`/`weakened`, matching `fairness::formula_relation`'s identical answer for the identical reason (S2). This is a real, current gap, not invented here — flagged for whoever lands the Finite oracle next.\n2. RFC 0031's own \"Completeness guarantee\" gaming-move table (the eight-row table mapping field/relation/blocking-verb) carries NO row for `assumptions`, even though \"assumption strengthening\" is named as one of the seven G3 dimensions two paragraphs earlier and docs/50 lists it as its own attack class. Treated as an editorial gap in that one table (the `assumptions` prose section already states relation+field+direction), not a substantive open question — recorded in the module doc rather than silently resolved.\n3. RFC 0031 states the declaredness->incomparable rule only for \"an unchanged expression\"; it is silent on the combined case (expression AND classification/fidelity_profile both move in the same revision). Reading adopted: when expression differs, `unknown` governs regardless of a coincident declaredness edit — both `unknown` and `incomparable` are non-affirmative and fail closed identically under P2, so this costs nothing the fail-closed rule cares about while avoiding an invented case split RFC 0031 never states.\n4. `fragment`-only movement (identical `ast`, different `fragment`) is folded into the same \"unequal canonical encoding -> unknown\" path as an `ast` change, since `fragment` is part of the ID2 preimage exactly as it is for `properties`. RFC 0031's `assumptions` text doesn't separately name this case; conservative reading, not a guess.\n5. `unsupported` is deliberately never emitted: unlike `faults`/`fairness`/`observers` (none of which carry a `fragment` member), `assumptions[].expression.fragment` IS a real schema member, so the `unsupported` question is genuine here — but deciding it needs the after-contract's `scope.fragments`, external to a two-`AssumptionSet` classifier (same boundary `AssumptionSet::check_fragments` already draws). Left to whatever assembles the full diff artifact.\n\nEVIDENCE: tests/pr12_impl03_assumption_add_remove_evidence.rs (11 tests) closes the real corpus fixture (replicated-register-contract.json, 3 real assumptions, policy.assumptions=\"review\") into PolicyTable::verdict for: narrowing an expression (never silent, reviewed), removing an assumption outright, adding one, reclassifying with expression held fixed — all reviewed under the fixture's own review verb. Adversarial: rename-while-preserving-expression proven removed+added never unchanged; source-only rewrite proven still unchanged (mirror-image check); a 3-mutation sweep pinning that no content edit ever emits a guessed strengthened/weakened. Two anti-vacuity mutants (blind-to-declaredness, matches-by-expression-instead-of-id) proven wrong where the real classifier is right. Module's own 20 unit tests cover membership, unchanged/incomparable/unknown mechanics, determinism, and the field-classification contract (admits_relation, to_classification_record).\n\nVERIFICATION: 142 crate tests pass (93 lib + 49 across four evidence files). `just check` exits 0 in the workspace (fmt, clippy -D warnings workspace-wide, full test suite, boundaries, kernel covenant, governance, dossier, Lean — all green). lib.rs touched only to add `pub mod assumptions;` in alphabetical position plus one new dedicated doc paragraph (matching the bn-ycn6/bn-3vxp precedent), no shared prose edited. START_HERE_IMPLEMENTATION.md's \"assumption add/remove\" bullet annotated; traceability regenerated (one requirement moves active->satisfied, 670->669 active)."}	blake3:J8Fm1_DGAgS9UPSKwJZushPmHs7929MdpQef52CTOig
1785883465372505	continuum-dev	itc:v3:AWKSTzM5JJnJPkQAAAAAQar23VW6voAAAAEylAs		item.comment	bn-7vg7	{"body":"Lead: merged @ epoch 52570f55c807. assumptions.rs closed over change_policy::Relation per the family discipline: id-keyed membership for added/removed, canonical-encoding comparison (ast+fragment, display-only source excluded) mirroring properties — no antitone dual; equal-encoding declaredness moves → incomparable per RFC 0031's explicit rule; unequal encoding fails closed to unknown because no Finite-fragment inclusion oracle exists yet (bn-8mlg's lane) — no guessed strengthened/weakened. Dangerous direction confirmed strengthened (mirror of properties' weakened) from RFC 0031 + plan §5.3 + docs/50. Five divergences honestly recorded rather than silently decided, incl. the RFC's own gaming-move table missing an assumptions row (editorial gap) and the fragment-carrying unsupported question needing scope.fragments external to a pairwise classifier. 142 crate tests, just check green in workspace. Closing."}	blake3:oLQX_zEsb-9DBfyym0MtneDBBs0eRZsKtRCZ-kIpp5E
