1785883736133417	continuum-dev	itc:v3:AWKSTzM5JJnJPkQAAAAAQar23VW6voAAAAEylgs		item.comment	bn-2hmk	{"body":"PR-13 exit evidence delivered in workspace bn-2hmk (commit b094798). What landed: crates/continuum-cli/tests/pr13_exit_evidence.rs (9 tests) + 42 committed golden artifacts under crates/continuum-cli/tests/golden/ + machine-readable summary crates/continuum-cli/tests/evidence/pr13-exit.json. Twenty-two scenarios drive every stable §13.4 command through cli::run itself (real argv → Scan parser → encoded frame → LocalPair → real Daemon serving workspace/intent/task/verification/context/evidence/observe; debug/repair registered-unserved), the union of the check_verdict/evidence_show/context_expand fixtures duplicated locally per house rule. Every --format json document and --format text body is retained under a stable artifact ID (pr13-<nn>-<command>--<scenario>.<channel>.golden) and compared byte-exactly with no normalization; pretty is pinned as text + exactly one label line. Exit codes: all five classes reached by genuine scenarios — 0 across ten commands; 1 by the daemon's own StaleSnapshot (lineage really superseded via dx03 attack-6 recipe through the CLI), its IdempotencyKeyReused (real generated-key collision), its UnsupportedSemanticFeature (explain/debug/repair over real frames), and a parse refusal; 2 by NullTransport (the transport bin/continuum.rs actually runs); 3 by the engine's own Die Hard refutation; 4 by its typed ResourceExhausted inconclusiveness under a real 4-state budget (check result AND check await). INV-003: contract::divergence empty between the two channels of every pinned scenario. INV-005: two independently provisioned daemons render byte-identical artifacts; only timestamps anywhere are the fixture's declared now; no nondeterministic field found (no FINDING to record). Anti-vacuity/INV-004: single-byte flip of any of the 42 goldens is detected by the same comparison the pinning test uses; a changed value and an invented key in a real terminal body fail the projection check by name; a dropped line fails the byte comparison; the check distinguishes all 380 cross-scenario pairs; PR13_EXIT_BLESS=1 regeneration rewrites then always panics so new bytes are always reviewed, never self-certified. The summary file is itself under test (rows, matrix, residuals asserted against the live run). RESIDUAL bn-jmx97: scenario pr13-06 pins the generated idempotency-key content collision (second verification.start, different body, same generated key → IdempotencyKeyReused) as current behaviour, annotated in suite/summary/START_HERE — pinned, not certified; the golden fails visibly when the derivation fix lands. DIVERGENCE from brief recorded: START_HERE PR 13 section still labels bn-3rqvm/bn-1g7e4/bn-ybh1z '(… open)' (lines ~303-305 and ~343-344) although all three are done per bones — stale prose from bn-3tz60's annotation era; left untouched as it is those bones' delivery text, lead may want a doc refresh. OBSERVATION (daemon-side, pre-existing, no bone filed): Daemon::refuse uses one generic detail string ('the request body is not the shape this operation declares') for every decode-stage refusal including UnsupportedSemanticFeature on unserved operations — the CLI renders it faithfully; wording precision belongs to continuumd if anyone cares. Verification: just check exit 0 from workspace root (fmt, clippy -D warnings, full workspace tests incl. the 9 new, boundaries, covenant, governance, dossier, Lean). START_HERE Exit line annotated (delivered: bn-2hmk — …), generate_traceability.py regenerated (PR-13/PR-13-EXIT now delivered; active 670→668). Not merged, not pushed, bone left open for the lead."}	blake3:pRUGpxURCIF4csepBuDkkDTpehNAMAp1jEOmEfK5Y7A
1785883792060548	continuum-dev	itc:v3:AWKSTzM5JJnJPkQAAAAAQar23VW6voAAAAEylws		item.comment	bn-2hmk	{"body":"Lead: merged @ epoch 43efd7fdb4d2. PR-13 exit delivered as an independent evidence layer: 22 scenarios through cli::run itself (real argv → parser → frame → LocalPair → one provisioned daemon), 42 golden artifacts under stable IDs compared byte-exact with NO normalization, all five exit classes reached by genuine scenarios (Die Hard refutation=3, typed ResourceExhausted inconclusive under a real 4-state budget=4, daemon's own StaleSnapshot/IdempotencyKeyReused/UnsupportedSemanticFeature + parse refusal=1, NullTransport fault=2). contract::divergence empty per pinned scenario (INV-003); two independent daemon provisionings byte-identical (INV-005 — no nondeterministic field found); anti-vacuity byte-flip + named projection-check mutations + 380/380 cross-scenario distinguishability; PR13_EXIT_BLESS always panics so new bytes are always reviewed (INV-004). bn-jmx97 residual PINNED not certified (pr13-06 retains the key collision and will fail visibly when the fix lands — correct). Flagged stale START_HERE prose (bn-3rqvm/bn-1g7e4/bn-ybh1z labeled open though done) noted for lead doc-refresh. Closing."}	blake3:1Wd9kN5WuJjxirQYMyWzirlvyo5IDMyIy1BwJVRliNA
