1785884604390231	continuum-dev	itc:v3:AWKSTzM5JJnJPkQAAAAAQar23VW6voAAAAEypgs		item.comment	bn-2ryko	{"body":"Both bullets resolved. Summary below; workspace bn-2ryko committed (f96720a on top of epoch 0352fa167a61), just check exit 0, not merged/pushed.\n\n## 1. RFC 0032 Validated-edge sentence — already fixed, no edit made\n\nChecked notes/plan/rfcs/0032-repair-transaction-protocol.md against RFC 0030's governing sentence (RFC 0030 \"Reuse-edge classes\" table, Validated row, line 87: \"the output is accompanied by a witness an independent checker accepts *for this input digest*\" / \"reuse only after the witness is re-checked\"; and RFC 0030 correction 6, line 350, which names RFC 0032's bullet directly: \"RFC 0032's bullet carries the same error and MUST be revised to match — this RFC does not edit it\").\n\nThe bone description (from bn-3hkk, filed against an earlier RFC 0032 draft) says RFC 0032 \"restates plan §8.6's error verbatim.\" That is no longer true. When RFC 0032 was expanded under bn-3i38 (commit fab324a, after bn-3hkk but apparently before this bone was picked up), its author independently applied the fix:\n\n- Cost-governance bullet (lines 249-254) already reads: \"a **conservative** disjointness judgement licenses a `Conservative` reuse edge; it licenses a `Validated` edge **only** when the disjointness itself carries a witness an independent checker accepts *for this input digest*...\" — correct per RFC 0030.\n- The RFC's own corrections ledger already carries correction 1 (line 330): \"A conservative disjointness judgement licenses a `Conservative` edge, not a `Validated` one,\" citing \"RFC 0030, correction 6\" by name and stating the same normative rule RFC 0030 states.\n\nThis already satisfies the bone's ask (numbered correction, house style, cites RFC 0030's governing text) with correct wording throughout the RFC (cost-governance bullet, corrections ledger, F9 flag at line 368, and the acceptance-criteria bullet at line 405 are all mutually consistent). Making a second edit would be redundant/risk contradicting an existing correction number. No edit made to RFC 0032.\n\nDivergence recorded: bone description's premise about RFC 0032's current state is stale; followed the current text per the task's own rule (\"If anything in the bone description turns out wrong against the current texts, follow the texts\").\n\nNot touched per the bone's fence: plan §8.6 itself still reads \"...reuse prior results as `Validated` edges...\" (notes/plan/plan.md:1090). This is the same error RFC 0030 correction 6 already addresses (\"RFC governs plan §8.6\" — RFC corrects plan without editing plan prose, per house convention). No new correction needed there; flagging only because the bone's rule asked me to record rather than edit if I believed §8.6 needed correcting — it does, but RFC 0030 already covers it and plan prose is out of scope for this bone.\n\n## 2. docs/42 quarantine scoping — edited\n\nRFC 0030's governing sentence: \"Quarantine\" section, notes/plan/rfcs/0030-incremental-semantic-query-engine.md:252 — \"The quarantine unit is the triple `(reuse-edge class, function_id, function_version)`. Quarantining a class *globally across all queries* is not the rule...\" (also stated as downgrade rule 1, line 100, and correction 7, line 352, which names plan §9.5/G5's \"quarantines the reuse class\" abbreviation directly — the same phrase docs/42 used).\n\nSearching notes/plan/docs/42_INCREMENTAL_VERIFICATION.md for \"quarantines the reuse class\" found two verbatim instances of the same imprecise claim (not one — the bone named line 105, but the identical phrase recurs at line 140 in the section that elaborates the same rule). Tightened both, smallest edit in each case:\n\n- Line 105 (Auditability classes bullet). Before: \"Any disagreement quarantines the reuse class and emits a minimal invalidation counterexample.\" After: \"Any disagreement quarantines the `(reuse-edge class, function_id, function_version)` triple (RFC 0030, \\\"Quarantine\\\") and emits a minimal invalidation counterexample.\"\n- Line 140 (Parity mismatches are engine defects). Before: \"An equality-auditable disagreement quarantines the reuse class and emits a minimal invalidation counterexample.\" After: \"An equality-auditable disagreement quarantines the `(reuse-edge class, function_id, function_version)` triple (RFC 0030, \\\"Quarantine\\\") and emits a minimal invalidation counterexample.\"\n\nLeft untouched: line 144's rhetorical \"why is this reuse class quarantined\" — it's an explainability question, not a scope claim, and isn't the literal search phrase; editing it wasn't required by the smallest-edit rule. docs/42's own Corrections table (line 191) quotes the pre-widening historical text (\"...quarantines the reuse class and emits a minimal invalidation counterexample and stopped there\") as a record of what plan §4.7 corrected docs/42 to add (the defect_* requirement); that quote is a historical citation of superseded prose (same convention RFC 0032 uses for its own \"previous revision\" quotes) and doesn't need updating to match the new wording.\n\nNo renumbering anywhere; no plan-prose edits; RFC 0032 and RFC 0030 untouched."}	blake3:sJB8X5hsJkzWA0taJEPRauafkrcs2eedOUI8V6NQP_E
1785884648439325	continuum-dev	itc:v3:AWKSTzM5JJnJPkQAAAAAQar23VW6voAAAAEypws		item.comment	bn-2ryko	{"body":"Lead: merged @ epoch acbae1145a28. Item 2 delivered: BOTH docs/42 instances (lines 105, 140 — bone named only one) tightened to the (reuse-edge class, function_id, function_version) triple citing RFC 0030's Quarantine sentence. Item 1 correctly declined: bone premise was stale — RFC 0032's bn-3i38 expansion already carries the fixed text + numbered correction 1 citing RFC 0030 correction 6; a redundant edit would have been noise. plan §8.6's residual original-error noted-not-edited, already addressed by RFC 0030 correction 6 (RFC beats plan). Closing."}	blake3:cp5EJtOcmexgdN8oXUR1OB63aOWTvrIapwKj1LfUbQw
