1785884684341922	continuum-dev	itc:v3:AWKSTzM5JJnJPkQAAAAAQar23VW6voAAAAEyqQs		item.comment	bn-3usqn	{"body":"Both dossier defects fixed in workspace bn-3usqn (commit efb558d). just check exits 0 (dossier validator status=pass; fmt/lint/test/boundaries/covenant/governance/lean all green).\n\n## 1. ObservationCoverage (docs/03 §2/§3)\n\nSearch evidence (whole dossier + notes/plan/schemas/ + code):\n- `grep -rn \"ObservationCoverage\" .` (workspace root, all file types) found exactly one prior hit outside docs/03 itself: `notes/plan/plan.typ:3831` — a Typst typesetting-render of docs/03 that `notes/plan/tools/validate_dossier.py`'s `_is_excluded_from_retired_scan` explicitly treats as a generated, non-authoritative render (\"Generated renders (e.g. Typst output of the markdown sources)... the markdown sources themselves are scanned\"); left untouched, same as the precedent in bn-14dqx (plan.typ staleness is its own tracked issue, dossier validator checks plan.md/docs, not plan.typ).\n- No hit in `notes/plan/schemas/` (no schema defines or references an ObservationCoverage-shaped enum).\n- No hit in any RFC, ADR, or other docs/*.md.\n- `crates/continuum-value/src/assurance.rs` (PR-1/IMPL-03, bn-2es0) already carried a doc comment reaching the identical conclusion: struct names it, §3 tabulates none, no other dossier source enumerates it, inventing levels would be exactly the guessing INV-008 forbids.\n\nConclusion: nothing normative backs the field. Struck it (INV-003: schemas decide, no invented levels).\n\nBefore (docs/03 §2):\n```rust\n    linkage: ImplementationLinkage,\n    observation: ObservationCoverage,\n\n    assumptions: Vec<Assumption>,\n```\nAfter:\n```rust\n    linkage: ImplementationLinkage,\n\n    assumptions: Vec<Assumption>,\n```\nplus a one-line note added after the code block: \"`ObservationCoverage` is struck from this struct: no source in this dossier, `notes/plan/schemas/`, or `continuum-value`'s assurance vocabulary (`crates/continuum-value/src/assurance.rs`) enumerates its levels, and §3 below tabulates only the four dimensions retained above; INV-003 leaves inventing levels to whichever source defines the field next.\"\n\nAssociated fix: `crates/continuum-value/src/assurance.rs`'s matching comment (lines 104-108) said \"The conceptual `AssuranceClaim` struct names it\" in present tense — now false. Updated it to past tense, recording that docs/03 has since struck the field rather than enumerate it (bn-3usqn). No behavior/API change, comment only.\n\n## 2. RFC 0010 Verdict block\n\nConfirmed contradiction: RFC 0010's \"## Verdict\" block listed six items (Established, Refuted, Inconclusive, Unsupported, ResourceExhausted, EngineError) as if all were verdicts. `notes/plan/schemas/assurance-result.schema.json` and `evidence-graph-node.schema.json` both give `verdict`/`status` exactly three members (established|refuted|inconclusive) plus a required `inconclusive_reason` (six members: Unsupported, ResourceExhausted, EngineError, InsufficientTelemetry, AbstractionAmbiguity, IncompleteProofSearch) whenever the verdict is inconclusive — matching plan §11.4's INV-008 list verbatim. RFC 0026 (correction 16) and RFC 0028 already treat these three as reasons, not verdicts, so RFC 0010 was the outlier.\n\nBefore:\n```text\n## Verdict\n\nEstablished\nRefuted\nInconclusive\nUnsupported\nResourceExhausted\nEngineError\n\n`Established` is meaningful only together with evidence and scope.\n```\nAfter:\n```text\n## Verdict\n\nEstablished\nRefuted\nInconclusive\n\n`Established` is meaningful only together with evidence and scope. `Unsupported`,\n`ResourceExhausted`, and `EngineError` are not verdicts: they are three of the six\ntyped `inconclusive_reason` values `Inconclusive` carries per INV-008 and plan\n§11.4 (correction 1).\n```\nRFC 0010 had no \"Corrections recorded\" ledger, so added one (RFC 0031/0037 house format: \"Per plan §25... The corrections in force:\" + numbered bold-title entries with Normative:/Direction:), placed before \"## Rejected alternatives\" matching where 0031/0037 place it. Correction 1 documents the reclassification with citations to both schemas and plan §11.4.\n\nNo renumbering anywhere; no other bones/schemas touched. Claims released next."}	blake3:tL6TFI6MG1ik3VQVBrfhY_MKsRzmISByhwPkJ0emMHE
1785884774253336	continuum-dev	itc:v3:AWKSTzM5JJnJPkQAAAAAQar23VW6voAAAAEyqgs		item.comment	bn-3usqn	{"body":"Lead: merged @ epoch 892d100d5982. ObservationCoverage STRUCK from docs/03 §2's AssuranceClaim on search evidence (no enumeration anywhere in dossier/schemas/code; only mentions were the excluded plan.typ render and assurance.rs's own gap-documenting comment, now updated to record the strike) — correct INV-003 outcome: a field no schema backs is not conceptual surface. RFC 0010 verdict block trimmed to the schema's three verdicts; Unsupported/ResourceExhausted/EngineError reclassified as inconclusive_reason values via new correction 1 in a fresh house-format ledger — the INV-008 typed-inconclusiveness boundary now consistent across RFC 0010/0026/0028, both schemas, and plan §11.4. Closing."}	blake3:3HFyozmqCKwxLiHTo-F4l6ai0o1L-DYFLWGV-CsVXj4
