1785885050421048	continuum-dev	itc:v3:AWKSTzM5JJnJPkQAAAAAQar23VW6voAAAAEyrAs		item.comment	bn-jmx97	{"body":"Resolution: BRANCH 2 of the decision frame — RATIFIED the current shape (cli-idem-{operation}-{counter} + documented --idempotency-key override as the cross-invocation replay channel). Workspace bn-jmx97, commit 88a310f, just check exit 0. No behaviour change, no golden changed.\n\nDIVERGENCE FROM THE BRIEF/BONE TEXT, recorded per instruction: the CLI's single production dependency edge is continuumd, NOT continuum-intent. crates/continuum-cli/Cargo.toml [dependencies] carries exactly `continuumd`; continuum-intent is dev-only fixture material. So branch 1's premise (\"reachable through the existing edge continuum-cli -> continuum-intent\") had no edge to travel.\n\nWHY BRANCH 1 IS NOT HONEST through the edge that does exist (continuumd):\n- The ID5 canonical ENCODING is reachable and already used as designed: continuumd::codec is the wire's own rule encoding.canonical_form implementation (\"This is the project's canonical-JSON discipline, not a second one\" — codec/json.rs), byte-deterministic per ID5.\n- No content DIGEST is reachable: daemon::identity::Blake3Identity is public but uncallable from the CLI — ContentIdentifier::identify is spelled in continuum-workspace types (ArtifactClass/ArtifactHandle) continuumd does not re-export; daemon::identity::HashedCorrelation is callable but is contractually rule audit.correlation's function of request IDENTITY alone (request_id, actor) — laundering body bytes through RequestId's grammar is the side-door use the frame excludes; nothing else public in codec/transport/protocol hashes bytes.\n- Even continuum-intent ships no hasher: identity.rs's CanonicalIdentity is pub(crate) (the identity IS the canonical bytes, ADR-0013), and the nine public identities' digest<H: ContentHasher>() accessors require naming continuum_value::identity::Blake3Hasher — i.e. a continuum-value edge regardless. \"continuum-intent's canonical hashing\" is really continuum-value's ContentHasher/Digest256 seam (dependency-rationale.toml says so verbatim).\n- The hashless variant (key = the canonical request bytes themselves) is deterministic and injective but was declined on the workspace's own terms: every content-derived wire token here is a digest token, never the preimage (ADR-0013: hashes index and partition); the key is user-visible surface (evidence show renders idempotency_key verbatim — pr13-14 golden), so request-sized keys leak whole bodies into rendered output; and it roughly doubles every generated-key mutation frame.\n\nBRANCH 3 FINDING (recorded, not acted on): the only honest path to a compact content-derived key is a NEW production edge continuum-cli -> continuum-value (Blake3Hasher/Digest256::to_token — the exact seam continuumd's Blake3Identity composes and continuum-intent reuses). Not added, per pre-authorization; routing is the lead's.\n\nWHY THE RATIFIED SHAPE IS CORRECT, not merely tolerable (the retry-vs-distinct-intent question, answered):\n- Every CLI command speaks exactly one mutation per invocation, as call one, so across invocations the generated key is a function of the operation name alone. A genuine retry (same command, same inputs) presents the same key AND the same canonical request = rule idempotency.replay's replay arm: the recorded first outcome, verbatim. INV-005's \"two invocations building the same request from the same inputs derive the same key\" ALREADY HOLDS for the CLI's real usage.\n- The residual is exactly: same operation, different body, no explicit key, persistent daemon -> the daemon's loud typed IdempotencyKeyReused naming the flag — never a silent wrong answer.\n- Content-derivation would hard-code \"same content = same request\", silently collapsing a deliberately repeated identical mutation into a replay — a statement rule idempotency.replay reserves to the caller. And the daemon already answers content-level idempotency at the layer that owns it: verification.start derives task_* from request content (identical resubmission under ANY key resolves to the same campaign — cached-result lane, daemon/verification.rs), ws_* snapshots are Blake3 identities. A client-side content key would restate, in an adapter, an idempotency the daemon owns.\n\nRECORDED WHERE: full grounds on wire::Connection::with_idempotency_key (the minting site's doc). Annotation flips, minimal and truthful (pinned-defect -> ratified regression guard): pr13_exit_evidence.rs header (\"Ratified behaviour, pinned as a regression guard\"), scenario-06 comment, summary-test comment; tests/evidence/pr13-exit.json residuals[0].note + scenario-06 note (asserted fields bone/pinned_by unchanged and still true); snapshot_family.rs bn-3rqvm pin-test doc (assertions untouched — behaviour stands); START_HERE bn-2hmk Exit annotation (\"ratified rather than fixed\"). generate_traceability.py run, PLAN_REQUIREMENTS.json regenerated. pr13-06 golden unchanged by design: the pinned refusal IS the ratified behaviour; it now guards against the derivation changing without revisiting this ratification."}	blake3:mf_ofrPo70cCdHxtZE3okpsTbmU2VibJ9H8ovll1MVA
1785885104964499	continuum-dev	itc:v3:AWKSTzM5JJnJPkQAAAAAQar23VW6voAAAAEyrQs		item.comment	bn-jmx97	{"body":"Lead: merged @ epoch d101f2ee630f. RATIFICATION ACCEPTED (branch 2): cli-idem-{operation}-{counter} + --idempotency-key stands as the cross-invocation replay channel, grounds documented on wire::Connection::with_idempotency_key. Brief divergence confirmed correct: the CLI's single production edge is continuumd (intent is dev-only) — my brief and the original bone description were both wrong about continuum-intent. Branch 1 honestly refused: canonical ENCODING is reachable through continuumd as designed but no content DIGEST is (Blake3Identity uncallable, HashedCorrelation contractually audit-only, raw-preimage keys rightly declined — keys surface in evidence show and ADR-0013 tokens are digests never preimages). Substance of the ratification: one mutation per invocation makes a same-inputs retry a true RFC 0026 replay; different-content collision is the daemon's loud typed IdempotencyKeyReused; content-level idempotency is already answered authoritatively by content-addressed handles. Branch 3 finding RECORDED as the routed disposition: if content-derived keys are ever demanded, the honest path is a new edge to continuum-value's ContentHasher/Digest256 seam — that decision lives with the lead at that time, discoverable via this bone; no speculative edge added now. Pin flips all deliberate (pinned-defect → ratified-regression-guard), asserted fields unchanged. Closing."}	blake3:g9xunOnE-ItNCB7J1-uGHvMPJGYLoQRC9Z9yvmMxWug
1785885105004864	continuum-dev	itc:v3:AWKSTzM5JJnJPkQAAAAAQar23VW6voAAAAEyrgs		item.move	bn-jmx97	{"state":"done"}	blake3:eQmcVxbfA_CLOFGoZ0Gt7mmqfx3w60sPujCRIOaAcKM
1785885757268365	continuum-dev	itc:v3:AWKSTzM5JJnJPkQAAAAAQar23VW6voAAAAEyrws		item.comment	bn-8mlg	{"body":"PR-12/IMPL-02 delivered in workspace bn-8mlg (commit 62ba1d4): crates/continuum-semantic-diff/src/properties.rs + tests/pr12_impl02_property_ast_edit_evidence.rs (16 evidence tests; 204 crate tests; just check exit 0).\n\nWHAT: RFC 0031 'properties' classification over Claim/ClaimSet keyed by id, closed over change_policy::Relation. Membership added/removed by key alone (renames never matched by expression). Meaning axis: kind/observer moved with expression fixed = incomparable (RFC verbatim); moved WITH the expression = unknown — the RFC scopes its incomparable rule to 'with an unchanged expression' and states no combined rule, so the compound edit folds into the governing non-affirmative relation exactly as assumptions.rs (bn-7vg7) resolved its identical silence, and the oracle is NEVER consulted across a meaning change (tested: a kind flip riding a decidable strengthening classifies unknown, never strengthened). Content axis: unchanged on ID2 encoding equality (ast+fragment, source excluded); unequal encodings reach the oracle only when both sides declare Finite (S3 license) — non-Finite, moved-fragment, and absent-fragment cases all fail closed to unknown (absent denotes the contract's declared fragment, which a two-ClaimSet classifier is never given).\n\nTHE ORACLE (the 'solver-based implication only where sound and bounded' line): properties::finite_formula_relation — nine individually meaning-preserving derivation rules (invertible and-right/or-left first, then conjunct-projection/disjunct-selection, then not/always/eventually/quantifier congruences over N5 level-named binders), each affirming only entailments valid in every interpretation, which discharges S2's Finite obligation a fortiori for what it proves. Bounded: IMPLICATION_STEP_BUDGET=4096 steps per direction, compile-time constant (raising it is a classifier-version change under RFC 0030); exhaustion fails closed, demonstrated by the same one-disjunct extension deciding weakened at 8 atoms and unknown at 400. A failed search refutes nothing, so incomparable never flows from content anywhere in the crate. Declined with reasons: le/lt literal arithmetic (no sort table — ast.rs's own N6 ground), always=>eventually (trace-model facts unfixed), instantiation (empty domains), tautology completeness (S2).\n\nON THE BRIEF'S ORACLE QUESTION: yes, IMPL-02 genuinely provides a Finite-fragment inclusion oracle — partial (sound underapproximation via universal entailment, not bounded-universe enumeration, which a two-formula classifier without a model cannot do), sound, bounded. Per instruction assumptions.rs is UNTOUCHED. Upgrade path for a follow-up bone: (1) assumptions.rs — its expressions are PropertyExpressions carrying fragment, so classify_pair's unequal-encodings arm can adopt the identical fragment license + finite_formula_relation call with NO dualize (its doc already records none is called for); its dangerous direction (strengthened) is then affirmed only with a derived witness. Note its module-doc sentence 'No Finite-fragment inclusion oracle exists... at the time of this writing' is now historical — self-dating, left as-is per the do-not-rewire instruction; refresh it in the same follow-up. (2) fairness.rs — its same-key condition arm now delegates to properties::formula_relation (the structural core; ZERO behavior change, pinned by new test a_condition_edit_the_oracle_could_decide_still_classifies_unknown, which will fail loudly when the upgrade lands); the full upgrade needs the contract's declared fragment threaded into classify_fairness (fairness items carry no fragment member), then finite_formula_relation + the existing dualize.\n\nFLAGS for the RFC lead (recorded in module doc, not silently resolved): (a) RFC 0031 '### properties' states 'strengthened iff behaviors(after) ⊆ behaviors(before), weakened iff behaviors(before) ⊆ behaviors(after)' — both iffs are simultaneously satisfied by a proven equivalence whose encodings differ, R2 forbids unchanged there, and the lattice has no equivalent token; the module fails closed to unknown on correction 16's one-record-one-direction reasoning (unreachable through CPNF-1 ClaimSets since N4 sorts the junction shapes that reach it; pinned on the raw-formula surface). Candidate correction. (b) The compound kind/observer+expression case above is unstated text — same shape as the assumptions silence bn-7vg7 flagged. (c) requested_assurance: RFC 0031's admissibility table makes expression directions inadmissible below bounded; this classifier's directions are witnessed at bounded+ but the clamp for weaker requested levels belongs to whatever assembles the diff artifact (no family classifier takes the level) — documented boundary, same as unsupported/scope.fragments.\n\nEVIDENCE highlights: the plan §5.1 properties attack in its most literal costume — appending the complementary 'v1 != v2' disjunct to the corpus fixture's Agreement claim, arriving in valid CPNF-1 through the front door — classifies an affirmed weakened and closes into PolicyTable::verdict BLOCK under the fixture's own locked verb (plus review under the gaming table's verb); strengthened mirror; double-negation disguise rejected at the artifact layer (N9 FalseNormalForm) and dissolved at the API layer (S1); vacuous-conjunct games never silent (alone: strengthened, a true non-strict inclusion; over a weakening: unknown — never unchanged); rename+weaken = removed+added; undecidable-therefore-closed beside the decided cases; anti-vacuity mutants both directions. START_HERE bullet annotated in workspace copy, traceability regenerated. Not merged, not pushed, bone left open for the lead."}	blake3:wW0-wptOljzNeBzRf5YvWTNdS84RCuHIjMmMnb5m5mw
1785885841333282	continuum-dev	itc:v3:AWKSTzM5JJnJPkQAAAAAQar23VW6voAAAAEysAs		item.comment	bn-8mlg	{"body":"Lead: merged @ epoch 0b6e17652f44. properties.rs = the crate's ONE formula authority: id-keyed membership; meaning axis (kind/observer flip with fixed expression → incomparable per RFC verbatim, compound move → unknown with the oracle never consulted across a meaning change); content axis → ID2-equality unchanged, else the S3-licensed sound bounded implication oracle — nine meaning-preserving derivation rules, 4096-step budget per direction, fail-closed exhaustion, both-directions collision refused to unknown. fairness.rs condition arm now DELEGATES to properties::formula_relation with a zero-behavior-change pin — the family's no-second-comparator rule held by construction. Evidence closes plan §5.1's complementary-disjunct attack into PolicyTable::verdict block under the fixture's own locked verb, with strengthened mirror, disguise sweeps, decided/undecidable/budget-boundary cases, mutants both directions. 204 crate tests. Three flags routed by lead: (a) equivalence-with-unequal-encodings has no token — candidate RFC 0031 correction; (b) compound-move textual silence (same shape bn-7vg7 flagged); (c) requested_assurance clamp belongs to the artifact assembler. Oracle question ANSWERED YES — assumptions.rs/fairness.rs upgrade paths recorded for routing. Closing."}	blake3:vHZRFwkxzLzWOvgWEfYDdc-ox0moAfv6qotbbaI5D1Q
