1785886803712220	continuum-dev	itc:v3:AWKSTzM5JJnJPkQAAAAAQar23VW6voAAAAEyuws		item.comment	bn-28ur	{"body":"Audit-first delivery (size s). Workspace: .maw/workspaces/bn-28ur. Commit 97742be.\n\nAUDIT — asked vs already-true vs added\n| Bone asked | Already true (citation) | Added here |\n|---|---|---|\n| Validator runs (`uv run --with jsonschema python tools/validate_dossier.py`) | Yes, exactly this invocation: `Justfile` `dossier` recipe (`cd notes/plan && uv run --with jsonschema python3 tools/validate_dossier.py`), chained into `check: fmt-check lint test boundaries covenant governance dossier lean`. `.edict.toml` names `just check` as `check_command`. | Nothing — recipe untouched per brief (\"do NOT restructure existing recipes\"). |\n| Regenerate validation-results.json + MANIFEST via generate_manifest.py, \"in the canonical order\" | The order (traceability -> validate -> manifest) is already documented, in `notes/plan/VALIDATION_REPORT.md` \"Reproduction\". But that same file states explicitly this is a **lead-loop/manual** convention, not a CI/per-commit gate step: \"It is not regenerated per-commit or by CI; it is regenerated by whoever closes the bone that changed the checked state.\" `generate_manifest.py` exists and runs, but its outputs (`MANIFEST.md`, `SHA256SUMS.txt`) were deliberately deleted from the repo in commit 74d23aa (\"docs: rm manifest and SHA256SUMS.txt\"), before implementation began, and are not read by `validate_dossier.py`, `just check`, or any other gate — confirmed by grep, no reference outside VALIDATION_REPORT.md's reproduction snippet and two plan-review critique docs. | Recorded as an honest residual, not built out: CI runs the validator only, not manifest/results-file regeneration, matching the dossier's own already-committed text. **Divergence from the brief**, recorded per instructions: the brief describes validation-results.json/MANIFEST regen as part of what CI runs; the current dossier text (written today, bn-2688c) says the opposite. I followed the text. |\n| One-commit reconciliation rule (§22) stated | Yes, normatively, in both directions already: plan.md §22 (\"`docs/52` and this section are reconciled in both directions in one commit... the dossier validator enforces bullet-for-bullet correspondence\") and docs/52's own header (\"Reconciled bullet-for-bullet with `plan.md` §22; the two are updated together\"). Mechanically enforced today by `check_gate_scheme_correspondence` in validate_dossier.py (bidirectional, >=0.6 token-overlap bullet matching, both directions checked as failures). | The corollary for bone-scoping was NOT previously written anywhere: \"each phase exit-gate bone includes its dossier updates\" as part of its own delivery, not a follow-up. Added a \"One-commit reconciliation rule (plan §22)\" section to `notes/plan/VALIDATION_REPORT.md` (already the process-documentation home for this tool family; freshly rewritten today by bn-2688c to serve exactly that role) stating both halves plainly. |\n| CI config in repo | None existed: no `.github/`, `.gitlab-ci.yml`, `.circleci/`, `Jenkinsfile`, `azure-pipelines.yml`, `.drone.yml` anywhere (verified by find across the tree). | Added `.github/workflows/check.yml`: runs `just check` unchanged on push-to-main and PRs-into-main. Documents its toolchain assumptions inline (rustup preinstalled + rust-toolchain.toml pin; mise via jdx/mise-action for just/uv/elan-init per mise.toml + README's three-line bootstrap; stdlib-only Python for the governance/boundary/covenant checkers). Also runs one CI-only extra step: `check_revision_delta.py --base origin/main --require-base` — this exact invocation is already named as CI's job in that checker's own docstring and in the Justfile's `governance` recipe comment (\"CI adds `--require-base`...\"); `just check`'s bare governance recipe (which skips gracefully with no base, by design, for local/shallow-clone runs) is untouched. |\n\nVerification: `just check` exit 0 from workspace root (fmt/clippy/tests/boundaries/covenant/governance/dossier/lean all green, Lean axiom manifest clean, 19/19 Lean jobs built), both before and after the edits, and again after commit. Dossier validator re-run standalone after each edit (validator-caution instruction) — stayed green throughout, \"status\": \"pass\" each time. New workflow YAML parsed and step list verified with PyYAML (one quoting bug found and fixed: a `name:` value containing an unquoted \"mise.toml: \" colon-space broke the parser — quoted the string). Sanity-ran the CI-only revision-delta invocation locally against the actual diff: \"status\": \"pass\", no violations.\n\nOperational caveat worth naming (not fixed here, out of scope per brief — no new process invented): plan_bones_traceability in validate_dossier.py compares notes/PLAN_REQUIREMENTS.json/PLAN_BONE_TRACEABILITY.md byte-for-byte against live .bones state (traceability.py::validate_checked_traceability). Any bone transition on trunk (not just merges) stales that snapshot until tools/generate_traceability.py reruns — already a known lead-loop pitfall (per-wave regen convention). Wiring the validator into CI means this becomes a mechanical, on-every-push failure mode instead of only surfacing when a human runs just check by hand — arguably the point of this bone, but worth the lead's awareness the first time CI goes red on a routine bone-state-only trunk push.\n\nAcceptance criterion re-read: \"Validator green in CI on every merge; a PR that flips a DX row without updating §0.3 (or edits §25 without its predicate) fails CI\" — satisfied directly, since g0_matrix_counts/program_status (§0.3 derivation) and spec_debt (§25 predicate) are existing validator checks now wired into CI via the unchanged dossier recipe; nothing new needed to be built for this criterion beyond CI existing at all.\n\nClaims released; not merged/closed per protocol — leaving for lead review/merge."}	blake3:MIdaf6vGHcL_R7PImPxCEJxtB94U2foymugv0vy_svk
1785886849163382	continuum-dev	itc:v3:AWKSTzM5JJnJPkQAAAAAQar23VW6voAAAAEyvAs		item.comment	bn-28ur	{"body":"Lead: merged @ epoch 647c386c0aa6. Audit-first delivery accepted: validator-in-gate and the §22↔docs/52 one-commit rule were ALREADY true (cited), so the bone's real gap was (1) the repo's first CI config — .github/workflows/check.yml running unmodified just check plus the CI-only strict check_revision_delta.py --base origin/main --require-base lane the tool's own docstring prescribes, and (2) the bone-scoping corollary (each phase exit-gate bone includes its own dossier updates) now stated in VALIDATION_REPORT.md. generate_manifest.py residual honestly recorded rather than wired to nothing (its outputs were deliberately deleted pre-implementation and read by nothing — following the current dossier text over the bone's stale phrasing was correct). Closing."}	blake3:YoTI5vm_1_9IHF2NQiRttod8cn7QjQk2r2Yv4_JJyhc
