1785887774231255	continuum-dev	itc:v3:AWKSTzM5JJnJPkQAAAAAQar23VW6voAAAAEyvgs		item.comment	bn-3cgt	{"body":"G0-DX-02 falsification campaign executed against the PRODUCTION classifier family. Workspace bn-3cgt, commit 74fef4c. just check exit 0 (fmt, clippy, tests, boundaries, covenant, governance, dossier, lean).\n\nDELIVERED: crates/continuum-semantic-diff/tests/dx02_falsification.rs — 28 tests: 19 attacks, 4 controls, 1 boundary probe, 2 campaign mutants. Every scenario is a genuine before/after Intent Contract pair over the two real corpus fixtures (replicated-register-contract.json, die-hard-contract.json), decoded via IntentContract::decode (the front door), classified by the production family (equality identity shortcut; properties w/ bounded implication oracle; assumptions; bounds; observers; faults; fairness; assurance), closed into PolicyTable::verdict under each fixture's OWN policy table, AgentAccept path, verdict computed against the BEFORE table per RFC 0037 P7. Machine-readable evidence (attack ids -> classifications -> verdicts) pinned byte-stable at tests/golden/dx02_falsification_evidence.txt. All required classifications were fixed from the governing texts before the campaign ran; every scenario passed on the first run — no expectation was fitted to code behavior.\n\nATTACK TABLE (all caught; none closed allow):\n- weaken property: complementary-disjunct (plan 5.1) -> properties:weakened -> block, both corpora (A01, A16); rename+weaken -> removed+added -> block (A02); split-the-claim -> removed+added -> block (A17)\n- strengthen assumptions: add favorable -> added -> review under review-verb (A03), added -> block under locked (A18); in-place narrowing -> unknown (fail-closed, no assumptions oracle yet) -> review (A04)\n- reduce bounds: nodes 3->2 -> contracted -> block (A05); values 6->5 -> contracted -> block (A19); mixed-movement disguise -> incomparable -> review, never allow (A06)\n- hide observer events (plan 19.5): drop family -> coarsened -> review (A07); same-size swap -> incomparable -> review (A08); rename+rebind compound -> observers removed+added + properties incomparable -> block (A09)\n- remove faults: drop crash -> removed -> block (A10)\n- plus: assurance validated->bounded -> downgraded -> block (A11); fairness added (schedules away the bug) -> review (A12); self-unlock rider (rewrite policy AND weaken, one revision) -> block via P7 (A13)\n\nCONTROLS (the named baseline, all allow with zero reasons): ordinary source guard repair, a real patch pair touching zero contract bytes -> fifteen unchanged via the production identity shortcut -> allow (C01); plus name-metadata edit (C02), claim source prose rewrite (C03), reformatting/key-reorder (C04) — ID2 exclusions and canonical-parse normalization exactly. No attack can board the shortcut: every attack row asserts Equality::Distinct first.\n\nMUTANTS (campaign anti-vacuity): fail-open closure (unclassified change read as unchanged) turns A15 into allow — fail-closed rule is load-bearing; verdict against the AFTER table turns A13 into allow — P7 is load-bearing.\n\nFINDINGS — two recorded BOUNDARIES, not defects, owners named in the test module doc and the matrix row: (1) governance-only rewrite (policy.properties locked->unlocked, nothing else) classifies fifteen unchanged / allow at this family's grain — policy is not one of the fifteen diff fields; identity still moves (shortcut refuses) and RFC 0037 ID3 routes governance edits through intent.lock, a daemon obligation (PR 5); pinned as DX02-B14; the one-revision unlock-and-weaken compound is blocked outright (A13). (2) Eight of fifteen fields (abstraction_maps, completion_policy, non_vacuity, nondeterminism, optimization, scope, security_policy, trust_boundaries) have no production classifier — an attack through trust_boundaries (mark storage effect opaque, plan 5.1's sixth move) is caught as unknown/review by RFC 0031's fail-closed rule, not as expanded/block; affirmative classifiers there are later PR-12 work. Honest scope: the wire intent_changes[]/diff_* assembler does not exist; the campaign implements RFC 0031's two normative closure rules (R2 canonical-encoding equality; fail-closed unknown) in harness code — every affirmative relation comes from a production classifier, never the harness. Also noted: assumptions has no direction oracle, so in-place strengthening is unknown/review rather than strengthened (its module doc records the gap); the direction-carrying oracle exists only for properties, where A01/A16 get affirmed weakened with a recomputable witness.\n\nROW: G0_SPIKE_MATRIX.md DX-02 flipped to Evidence (reference implementation) with campaign detail in Evidence and boundaries in Decision; count-neutral for plan 0.3 (status prefix unchanged class); dossier validator passes; traceability regenerated in-workspace (registry was stale from trunk bone-state moves; regen included in commit). src/ untouched (bn-21dd precedent); no existing test edited. Pass condition holds at production grain: all five named axes classified as intent changes; ordinary guard repair is not. Not merged; workspace left for lead review."}	blake3:2O3q2bBzxCfssTXyGHD4VJ_CilUOFVWQzxmx5LT6WO4
1785887833181404	continuum-dev	itc:v3:AWKSTzM5JJnJPkQAAAAAQar23VW6voAAAAEyvws		item.comment	bn-3cgt	{"body":"Lead: merged @ epoch 0318730499f1. G0-DX-02 ANSWERED YES at production grain: 28 tests (19 attacks, 4 controls, boundary probe, 2 campaign mutants), every scenario a real before/after contract pair over the fixtures' OWN policies through IntentContract::decode → full family → PolicyTable::verdict, expectations pre-registered from the RFCs, all passed first run. All five named axes catch; disguises refused incl. §5.1 complementary disjunct, §19.5 event hiding, rename+rebind compound, and the self-unlock rider (P7 shown load-bearing by after-table mutant). Guard-repair control: fifteen unchanged via the production identity shortcut → allow, zero reasons — and no attack can board the shortcut. Two boundaries pinned with owners: DX02-B14 governance-only rewrite routes to daemon ID3/intent.lock (PR 5), and the eight not-yet-affirmative fields shown guarded by fail-closed unknown/review with a fail-open mutant proving the guard load-bearing. DX-02 row → Evidence (reference implementation), count-neutral for §0.3. Closing."}	blake3:Qjyax_sC14iKBIxvS9tWOPYI1tn01JvPD8-qggY67W4
