1785887916035449	continuum-dev	itc:v3:AWKSTzM5JJnJPkQAAAAAQar23VW6voAAAAEyxAs		item.comment	bn-cho5	{"body":"Lead: merged @ epoch cc6cb4fe5a90. PHASE-A-DEL-03 delivered on all three criteria: (1) schedule-as-data sweeps at both grains — 1,680-schedule CAS two-phase convergence/coalescing + 560-schedule INV-017 visibility monotonicity in continuum-workspace; dispatch-lane commutation, cancel/duplicate-start spliced at every position, and bn-3dr's nine crash boundaries × every lifecycle position recovering Clean to byte-identical records in continuumd — composing with g1/dx13/dx14, not duplicating. (2) just sanitizers recipe (ASan+TSan, -Zbuild-std, --locked) correctly OUTSIDE just check per the pinned-toolchain rule, and ACTUALLY RUN: both armed canaries caught, 106 suites/1,708 tests, zero findings; residuals honestly recorded (nightly dated-pin convention, doctests excluded, TSan meaningful only on threaded store suites, CI lane = documented invocation). (3) mutation campaign: lost-update/orphan-worker/half-publication each injected as mutant re-implementations src-untouched, each caught by its NAMED check with reason asserted, faithful control green, fail-closed summary. Loom DECLINED with the right argument — dispatch holds &mut, phases reified as values, an external dev-dep would have been decorative. Closing."}	blake3:oaYJgoSAxs3YOqL4gqtjJ6KmS5EPEYd-hY7XGP8g3zw
1785887916076813	continuum-dev	itc:v3:AWKSTzM5JJnJPkQAAAAAQar23VW6voAAAAEyxQs		item.move	bn-cho5	{"state":"done"}	blake3:00I3hyOiAn2nfB4fKHFbMTpHRnXhslc-GsK8mC58t2s
1785889578027426	continuum-dev	itc:v3:AWKSTzM5JJnJPkQAAAAAQar23VW6voAAAAEyxgs		item.comment	bn-3jtr	{"body":"PR-12 exit delivered (workspace bn-3jtr, commit bd46c1b, just check exit 0): crates/continuum-semantic-diff/tests/pr12_exit_evidence.rs (21 tests) + retained artifact tests/golden/pr12_exit_evidence.txt — the independent exit layer over bn-3cgt's campaign; none of its tests touched, src/ untouched.\n\nQUANTIFIER CLOSED. The authoritative G0 gaming-patch set is the G0-DX-02 row of notes/plan/notes/G0_SPIKE_MATRIX.md — the one dossier row whose pass condition IS the exit sentence ('all classified as intent changes; ordinary code guard repair is not', asserted verbatim by the exit file). The move list is DERIVED at test time from the row's own required-experiment text (weaken property / strengthen assumptions / reduce bounds / hide observer events / remove faults) and verified member-by-member against the campaign's byte-pinned evidence artifact: 5/5 covered (A01/A02/A16/A17; A03/A18; A05/A06/A19; A07/A08/A09; A10), no attack row anywhere closes allow, every attack carries a produced classification named by a P6 reason, and the guard-repair baseline closes a clean allow. A doctored dossier row (sixth move 'erase history') fails the closure loudly — a future dossier addition cannot silently widen the quantifier past the evidence.\n\nTHE SENTENCE LIVE (INV-004, not self-certifying): one canonical patch per derived move re-executed independently through the production classifiers (the local closure harness contributes only R2 unchanged and fail-closed unknown — the two directions that cannot manufacture a pass), each refused the identity shortcut and closed into the BEFORE contract's own policy table on AgentAccept per P7: weakened/block, added/review, contracted/block, coarsened/review, removed/block. Negative half at exit grain: a real source patch pair, zero contract bytes, boards the production identity shortcut to fifteen unchanged and a zero-reason allow — same closure, same fixture, same acceptance path as the attacks. Live outcomes assert row-for-row agreement with the campaign artifact (6 twins), so the independent layer and the retained evidence cannot drift apart silently.\n\nANTI-VACUITY both directions: a blind-classifier mutant (weakened->unchanged) flips the live attack to allow and is REJECTED by the exit's own per-patch check; a flag-everything mutant (unchanged->unknown on the repair) flips the negative half and is rejected; corrupted campaign artifacts (flipped attack verdict / blanked classification / flagged guard-repair control) are rejected by the same closure function the real artifact passes. Golden regeneration is explicit and always red (PR12_EXIT_BLESS=1).\n\nADJACENT SETS closed by enumeration, each derived from its own text and pinned so an edit fails loudly: docs/50 intent attacks 6/6 covered; plan 5.1 8/8 — the one campaign gap, 'mapping two concrete values to one abstract value', is now covered LIVE at fail-closed grain (abstraction_maps: unknown -> review under the fixture's own verb; no affirmative classifier overclaimed — the campaign's eight-field boundary, exercised on a field DX02-A15 did not reach); plan 19.5 pinned and partitioned total: 7 Intent-Contract-patch members covered, 8 members are not Intent Contract patches (instrumentation/budget/grader/receipt/cache/prompt) and fall outside PR-12-EXIT's quantifier, owned by docs/50's other classes and their gates.\n\nSTART_HERE: PR-12 Exit line annotated (delivered: bn-3jtr — substance), traceability regenerated: PR-12-EXIT and PR-12 -> satisfied, 661 active. Note bn-1r9 (PR-12 goal) still has open children bn-181aj (docs) and bn-2nwpg (oracle wiring) — close-out is the lead's call; bn-2ofd depends on this bone.\n\nPHASE-A-DEL-06 DELIBERATELY NOT ANNOTATED — routing needed before this bone closes. 'Semantic diff v0' (plan §21 Phase A) is not fully delivered by PR-12's exit: RFC 0031 defines the engine as 'classifies every change, computes the evidence impact set, and produces the policy verdict', carried by the diff_* artifact, and the crate lib doc names both halves as 'not here'. Remaining, with NO carrier bone under req:pr-12 today: (1) the wire intent_changes[]/diff_* artifact assembly across all fifteen protected fields (schemas/semantic-diff.schema.json; includes RFC 0031's program-side semantic_changes[] seven axes) — every classifier module doc defers the R2/fail-closed closure rules to this assembler, which today exist only as harness code in the dx02 campaign and this exit file; (2) the impact-set computation (RFC 0031 'Impact set'). Also open under req:pr-12: bn-2nwpg (assumptions/fairness Finite-oracle wiring — until it lands, in-place assumption strengthening fail-closes to unknown/review rather than affirming strengthened; recorded in the campaign and the exit artifact) and bn-181aj (RFC 0031 text dispositions). The req:phase-a-del-06 label should ride to whichever successor carries the assembler + impact set."}	blake3:O_Zl8VGbGHPXcfmM55xe_VlfbOt5Vp-HcorYgmMSeHM
1785889632193552	continuum-dev	itc:v3:AWKSTzM5JJnJPkQAAAAAQar23VW6voAAAAEyxws		item.create	bn-7ek41	{"description":"The two remaining halves of semantic diff v0 (PHASE-A-DEL-06), identified at bn-3jtr's exit close as unboned: (1) the wire artifact assembler — RFC 0031's intent_changes[]/diff_* artifact shape assembled across all fifteen fields from the landed classifier family (equality shortcut + the seven field modules + properties), including correction 14's unchanged-shortcut wire behavior and the per-unit locator/requested_assurance clamp flags recorded in bn-8mlg's comment (clamp belongs HERE, not to any field classifier); (2) impact-set computation. Both close over the family's classifications — no second classification authority. Successor carrier for req:phase-a-del-06 per the label re-cover rule. Related open bones: bn-2nwpg (assumptions oracle wiring), bn-181aj (RFC 0031 text dispositions — its equivalence-token question is wire-visible and may interact with the assembler's vocabulary; check before freezing assembler tokens).","kind":"task","labels":["req:pr-12","req:phase-a-del-06","implementation"],"size":"m","title":"PR-12: wire intent_changes[]/diff_* artifact assembler and impact-set computation"}	blake3:lnDpgCSyDhe5rayeTyo3txuNKA18VAbBblc0PGeBLjg
