1785890338478601	continuum-dev	itc:v3:AWKSTzM5JJnJPkQAAAAAQar23VW6voAAAAEy0Qs		item.comment	bn-181aj	{"body":"Three RFC 0031 textual dispositions delivered as corrections 17-19 (appended, no renumbering) plus flag F6, in workspace bn-181aj (commit 6027310). All from `notes/plan/rfcs/0031-semantic-and-intent-diff.md`.\n\n(1) EQUIVALENCE-WITHOUT-TOKEN (bn-8mlg). properties'/assumptions' rule states a direction \"`strengthened` iff behaviors(after)⊆behaviors(before), `weakened` iff behaviors(before)⊆behaviors(after)\" — both `iff`s can hold together on a proven equivalence whose canonical encodings differ (CPNF-1 is sound but incomplete, S1/S2). A record carries one relation; the lattice has no `equivalent` token; R2 forbids `unchanged` off anything but encoding equality. CHOICE: (a) blessed `unknown` as the deliberate interim answer (correction 17), not (b) minted a token. REASONING: argued from the RFC's own privileged-change-detection goal — a proven equivalence is never itself the dangerous direction in either field's order (an equivalent property/assumption is exactly as restrictive as before), so failing closed to `unknown` never under-reports a weakening or strengthening; it costs a review on a pair that provably needed none, the same price S2 already charges every undecided pair. Minting `equivalent` is wire-visible (relation set is closed, \"Versioning and revision\" — needs a major schema_version bump) and NOT mine to implement here: recorded as F6 for the next protocol-minor bundle (bn-3jrtz), explicitly framed as additive-later (narrows an existing `unknown` arm, doesn't change what any current record means). BEFORE: `properties`/`assumptions` sections were silent on the both-satisfied case. AFTER: both sections state the resolution inline (\"(correction 17)\"); `properties.rs`'s `finite_formula_relation` already implements and tests it (the `(true,true) => Unknown` arm, test `a_pair_proved_in_both_directions_fails_closed_to_unknown`) — no code changed, text now matches landed behavior.\n\n(2) ASSUMPTIONS GAMING-TABLE ROW (bn-7vg7). The \"Completeness guarantee\" table mapped only plan §5.1's eight bullets; none is a bare assumption edit (its fairness bullet names `fairness`, not `assumptions`), even though the section's own opening paragraph names \"assumption strengthening\" as a G3 dimension and docs/50 lists \"strengthen assumptions\" as its own attack class. CHOICE: added a ninth row, mirroring the `properties` row's single-relation shape: \"narrow an assumption's expression to admit fewer environments | `assumptions` | `strengthened` | `review`\" (correction 18). REASONING: sourced from docs/50 + the RFC's own `assumptions` section rather than plan §5.1 (updated the table's intro sentence to say so, since the original \"eight moves of plan §5.1\" framing no longer covers all rows); verb `review` matches `assumptions`' base verb row — no directional verb, same set as `fairness` (`continuum_intent::change_policy::PolicyField::verbs`, both `BASE`). Cross-checked against `crates/continuum-semantic-diff/tests/dx02_falsification.rs`'s DX02-A03 (add a favorable assumption → `assumptions: added`, `review`) and DX02-A04 (strengthen in place → `assumptions: unknown` today, fail-closed pending the oracle, `review`) — the row states the RFC's normative target relation (`strengthened`), consistent with every other table row documenting the lattice's rule rather than today's implementation completeness (e.g. `abstraction_maps`/`merged` despite that field's own open decidability question). BEFORE/AFTER: table gained one row + corrected intro sentence; `assumptions.rs`'s module doc already called the omission an editorial gap in prose — text now closes it structurally.\n\n(3) COMPOUND-MOVE SILENCE (bn-8mlg + bn-7vg7 independently). `properties` states `kind`/`observer` moving `incomparable` only \"with an unchanged expression\"; `assumptions` states `classification`/`fidelity_profile` moving `incomparable` only \"with an unchanged expression\" too — neither states the compound case (that axis AND expression moving together). CHOICE: ratified the landed resolution — `unknown`, not `incomparable` (correction 19). REASONING: the content axis's decision procedure answers a question about one unit's meaning under one FIXED kind/observer/classification/fidelity_profile; once that axis has also moved, the two sides no longer share the meaning a direction would be decided over, so the procedure (oracle or plain equality) is never consulted across the boundary. Same safe polarity as (1): `unknown` is non-affirmative and fails closed identically to `incomparable` under P2, so this costs nothing the fail-closed rule doesn't already spend and never lets a compound edit find a spuriously affirmative direction. Explicitly distinguished from `fairness`'s kind+condition compound (correction 16), which resolves differently (removed+added) because `kind` is part of THAT field's unit key — properties'/assumptions' moved axes are not part of either unit's key, so it stays one unit, one record. BEFORE/AFTER: both sections now state the compound rule inline; `properties.rs` (test `a_meaning_change_never_lets_the_oracle_affirm_a_direction`) and `assumptions.rs` (test `a_content_change_alongside_a_declaredness_change_still_classifies_unknown`) already implement and test it — no code changed.\n\nCONSISTENCY WITH bn-2nwpg: bn-2nwpg (concurrent, in flight) upgrades assumptions.rs's single-axis content case to consult the oracle; the compound-move rule (3) and both modules' fail-closed boundaries are untouched by that work, since a compound move never reaches the single-axis decision procedure under rule (3) — text avoids asserting \"assumptions never decides a direction\" and instead scopes every claim to the specific case each correction addresses, verified true under both the current and post-bn-2nwpg states.\n\nVERIFICATION: `just check` exit 0 in workspace (fmt, clippy -D warnings, full test suite, boundaries, kernel covenant, governance, dossier validator — including its RFC-prose gate — Lean, all green). Only file touched: the RFC. No code, no schema, no other doc. Committed (6027310), not merged, not pushed. Claims released after this comment."}	blake3:v19acIpZYLhXzy8Kg_qaQNHQTPa43Z48lTaOg5PWbzo
1785890384353368	continuum-dev	itc:v3:AWKSTzM5JJnJPkQAAAAAQar23VW6voAAAAEy0gs		item.comment	bn-181aj	{"body":"Lead: merged @ epoch c03426c05861. Corrections 17-19 accepted: (17) proven-equivalence-with-unequal-encodings blessed unknown on the correct polarity argument — equivalence is never the dangerous direction, unknown triggers review, no under-report possible; equivalent-token alternative recorded as F6 for the bn-3jrtz protocol bundle, matching properties.rs's landed (true,true)→Unknown arm with zero code change. (18) ninth completeness-table row for assumptions (narrow-to-admit-fewer-environments | strengthened | review), sourced from docs/50 and cross-checked against DX02-A03/A04. (19) compound-move rule ratified as unknown-not-incomparable with the oracle never consulted across a meaning/declaredness change, correctly distinguished from fairness's kind+condition compound (correction 16, kind is in that field's unit key), and worded to stay true post-bn-2nwpg. bn-7ek41 (assembler) is now unblocked on the token question: F6 is the bundle's, assembler vocabulary freezes on the current tokens. Closing."}	blake3:o4L2qWRYomLoJneGWMD1VIrSMAA2pSBdHG98rlbEtuU
1785890384385554	continuum-dev	itc:v3:AWKSTzM5JJnJPkQAAAAAQar23VW6voAAAAEy0ws		item.move	bn-181aj	{"state":"done"}	blake3:q1GC0KcuvKkgv8S5ugj5WFSQYrbVp7JgNKDFEYwifTk
1785890866243634	continuum-dev	itc:v3:AWKSTzM5JJnJPkQAAAAAQar23VW6voAAAAEy1As		item.comment	bn-2nwpg	{"body":"bn-2nwpg delivered in workspace bn-2nwpg (commit 6a5c467): assumptions.rs content axis wired to the bn-8mlg Finite implication oracle; fairness delegation audited. 147 semantic-diff tests (136 lib + new 11-test evidence file), just check exit 0 in workspace. Not merged, not pushed.\n\nPOLARITY DERIVATION (the crux, from the texts): the oracle's relation is consumed DIRECTLY — no dualize. (1) RFC 0031 assumptions: 'The relation is computed on expression exactly as for claims — the same order, on the same normal form'; what differs is 'Direction and policy valence' — which direction is dangerous — never the mechanism. 'An assumption strengthened admits fewer environments' and a formula strengthened admits fewer behaviors: same sign term for term. (2) The antitone marker RFC 0031 writes for fairness[].condition ('the enabling predicate occupies an ANTITONE position... weakening the condition strengthens the constraint') appears nowhere in the assumptions text; an assumption's expression is not a guard on when something else applies, it IS the thing the direction is stated over. (3) Fairness's dual is anchored on a null extremum ('null means unconditional... the weakest condition, hence the strongest constraint') supplied by RFC 0037's absence≡null family — which correction 15 enumerates (bounds.values, bounds.depth, fairness[].condition, extended to scope.abstraction_level) and which contains NO assumptions[].expression entry: expression is a REQUIRED schema member with no null form (pinned against the live schema), so the weakest-formula/strongest-unit inversion that forces fairness's dual has no anchor in this field. Wrong polarity would classify a real in-place strengthening as weakened — the family's dangerous-direction failure — so it is pinned, not argued: disguise sweeps prove strengthened across five CPNF shapes, and a dualizing mutant is proven wrong in BOTH directions on the real corpus.\n\nWHAT UPGRADED: exactly the single-axis decidable case. classify_pair now mirrors properties' two-axis shape (declaredness where meaning stands); the declaredness-fixed unequal-encodings arm calls properties::expression_relation — bn-8mlg's license arm promoted to pub(crate) and shared verbatim so the S3 Finite license is written once and cannot drift (no second comparator, per the family rule). A decidable Finite-to-Finite edit now classifies affirmed strengthened/weakened with a recomputable derivation witness.\n\nWHAT STAYED CLOSED (all preserved, all tested): meaning-axis rules verbatim (equal+equal=unchanged, declaredness-moved+equal=incomparable); expression+declaredness compound stays unknown with the oracle NEVER consulted across a declaredness move (bn-7vg7's recorded resolution preserved for bn-181aj to ratify; pinned non-vacuously — the riding pair is asserted oracle-decidable); non-Finite/moved/absent fragment unknown (absent = the contract's declared fragment, never given to a pairwise classifier); undecidable and budget-exhausted unknown (8-atom decides, 400-atom exhausts, through classify_assumptions); both-directions collision refused to unknown by inheritance from finite_formula_relation (assumptions' PropertyExpressions only hold normalized ASTs, so the arm is unreachable through this module's inputs exactly as through properties').\n\nFAIRNESS AUDIT: delegation polarity confirmed RFC-correct, not just unchanged. Two unequal declared conditions classify unknown and that IS the RFC's answer (S3: no fragment member on fairness items, no scope.fragments given, so no license — not an implementation shortfall); the null-extremum arms already pin RFC 0031's verbatim 'C → null classifies strengthened' end to end; NEW pin audit_the_dualize_table_is_rfc_0031s_verbatim_duality_and_nothing_else proves the dualize table every future oracle answer must cross is the RFC's sentence exactly (weakened<->strengthened swap, incomparable/unknown pass through). bn-8mlg's zero-behavior pin left intact and loud.\n\nFLIPPED PINS: none — checked deliberately. DX02-A04 and impl03's content-edit sweep are all atom renames the oracle cannot relate in either direction, so their pinned unknown/review expectations hold unchanged for the S2 reason (a failed derivation refutes nothing); their now-false 'no oracle exists' PROSE was amended with bn-2nwpg citations, assertions untouched, never loosened. pr12_exit_evidence's assumption attacks are membership adds — unaffected.\n\nEVIDENCE (tests/pr12_assumption_oracle_wiring_evidence.rs): the plan 5.1/5.3 assumption-strengthening move in its most literal costume — dropping NetworkNoForgery's NOT occurs(Deliver) escape disjunct, arriving in valid CPNF-1 through the front door — classifies an AFFIRMED strengthened where bn-7vg7 pinned unknown, and closes into PolicyTable::verdict review under the fixture's own verb (P6 naming the record) and BLOCK under Die Hard's locked verb via a conjunct insertion kept in N4 order; weakened mirror on the same real expression; rename disguise = removed+added never a direction; reclassification rider = unknown; source costume cannot soften an affirmed direction; undecidable and budget boundaries closed into review; license-ignoring (fail-open on Symbolic) and dualizing mutants both proven wrong. Docs: assumptions.rs's 'no oracle exists' section replaced with the license/derivation sections; properties.rs authority paragraph, lib.rs, START_HERE bn-7vg7/bn-8mlg annotations amended minimally and truthfully; traceability regenerated (661 active, counts unchanged)."}	blake3:QokuKJuccCN9uStpJ4cy6AzMIlWnsTpkuSoykvgSSp0
1785890890806047	continuum-dev	itc:v3:AWKSTzM5JJnJPkQAAAAAQar23VW6voAAAAEy1Qs		item.comment	bn-34je	{"body":"INV-001 evidence delivered: crates/continuum-intent/tests/inv001_protected_intent_evidence.rs (20 tests, 6 modules, all green), commit f0594e5 in-workspace (bn-34je). Zero src/ changes, zero existing tests touched, zero new dependency edges (cross-crate citations are include_str!/fs over tracked files — the inv008/inv014 device).\n\nSCOPING NOTE (brief-vs-texts, recorded per bn-n9a1's precedent): the brief called the six-verb sentence 'INV-001's text'. The texts say otherwise: plan §2's INV-001 is the two-sentence contract ('Ordinary tasks may not mutate intent. Intent changes require a new Intent Contract, semantic diff, policy decision, and invalidation of dependent evidence.'); the six-verb spelling is AGENTS.md's joint INV-001/INV-011 summary. Not a contradiction — the map is keyed to the six verbs (the operational grain the enforcement is built at) and both texts are pinned with anti-drift checks.\n\nVERB -> SITE MAP (each row: classifier at production grain + policy site live in-crate + campaign rows cited)\n- weakening a property -> properties/weakened -> semantic-diff properties.rs (implication oracle) -> fixture 'locked' -> BLOCK (DX02-A01/A02/A16/A17)\n- strengthening an assumption -> assumptions/strengthened -> assumptions.rs (no inclusion oracle: in-place fails closed to unknown) -> 'review' + named reviewer -> REVIEW (DX02-A03/A04/A18)\n- shrinking a bound -> bounds/contracted -> bounds.rs -> 'no-decrease' -> BLOCK (DX02-A05/A06/A19)\n- hiding an event -> observers/coarsened -> observers.rs -> 'review' + named reviewer -> REVIEW (DX02-A07/A08/A09)\n- removing a fault -> faults/removed -> faults.rs -> 'no-removal' -> BLOCK (DX02-A10)\n- downgrading assurance -> assurance/downgraded -> assurance.rs (correction-13 carve-out) -> 'no-downgrade' -> BLOCK (DX02-A11)\nAll six closed LIVE into PolicyTable::verdict under the replicated-register fixture's own policy table on BOTH acceptance paths — never allow, P6 naming exactly the attacked field/relation/verb/reviewers. Fail-closed unknown forbids allow on all six (block under locked); correction 13's assurance x incomparable exclusion asserted directly with the other 14 fields admitting it (bn-2sngz cited).\n\nTHE FOUR REQUIRED ELEMENTS, SITED\n1. 'a new Intent Contract' — LIVE here: bound shrink and governance-only respell both move the ID1/ID2 preimage (the DX02-B14 identity half asserted live); ID2 metadata (name, expression.source) never does; re-assembly control equal.\n2. 'semantic diff' — LIVE at classifier grain, CITED not re-run (bn-1eqt style): dx02 campaign (19 attacks over all six verbs, 'All nineteen attacks were caught' pinned, both campaign mutants pinned, every map row id present in campaign AND golden artifact) + pr12 exit (quantifier closure, blind-classifier mutant, BLESS-always-panics all pinned); eight-module family checked bidirectionally against the real src directory. The WIRE lane is an absence (below).\n3. 'policy decision' — LIVE here: PolicyTable::verdict P1-P6 (change_policy_contract.rs's clause-by-clause suite cited, not duplicated; this file binds the six verbs to it), admits_relation incl. correction 13, W6 via is_admissible_on.\n4. 'invalidation of dependent evidence' — discharged today BY IDENTITY, not by a walk: revisions mint a new in_*, evidence/tasks bind intent by identity only (daemon/task.rs pin), so prior evidence is never re-served for a revised intent. The EXPLICIT lane (plan §4.2's sentence, pinned) has typed vocabulary (INVALIDATES edge in continuum-evidence, pinned) and NO producer — absence pinned to go red ('nvalidat' absent from daemon/intent.rs).\n\nPRIVILEGE HALF (WHO) — LIVE, cited via source tripwires: intent.accept/reject/lock @privileged @audit_recorded in the registry, propose_revision at revise-intent and deliberately NOT privileged (docs/49's 'revise intent: proposal only' row pinned verbatim + RFC 0027 reading pinned in the daemon module doc); T3 decided in admission.rs from profile.privileged_operations; intent.lock's weaken-refusal and propose's locked-field refusal pinned as live; D1 first-intent-wins ('converge on the *first* intent', 'A re-create cannot re-govern a snapshot', 'There is no un-seal operation') pinned — the DX-03 fix wave's INV-001 ratification.\n\nGAPS (typed absences, INV-008 spirit, each a tripwire that fires when the producer lands)\na. Daemon propose/diff classification lane: refuses UnsupportedSemanticFeature, never guesses. bn-1604's owed rationale-recheck VERIFIED NOT YET DUE: protocol/shared.rs declares 'rationale: String required;' and daemon/intent.rs still contains no 'rationale' token — both pinned; either breaking = recheck due.\nb. P7 accept-time recomputation: no producer AND no exploit — source sweep proves put_intent reachable only from state.rs (definition) + intent.rs (lock successor), so no wire path mints a Proposed record; 'AcceptancePath' appears in zero continuumd sources.\nc. Explicit invalidation producer (element 4 above).\nd. INV-011 reclassification: continuum-repair still the PR-1/IMPL-01 scaffold, zero pub items, its own 'reclassified and blocked rather than merged' sentence pinned.\ne. Assumptions inclusion oracle: in-place strengthening classifies unknown (fail-closed review, never allow) — the module's own recorded gap, cited via DX02-A04.\n\nMUTANTS: sentence extraction (dropped verb -> 5 not 6, unrelated text -> None); blind classifier (unchanged swap -> allow/zero reasons -> rejected by the file's own never-a-repair predicate, per-row); campaign tripwire (gutted DX02-A10 reported by id); daemon tripwire (stripped locked-refusal detected; planted AcceptancePath reported).\n\nANNOTATE-VS-DECLINE: ANNOTATED, per bn-n9a1's rule (annotate when the obligation is structurally dischargeable today with gaps that are ABSENCES stated inline; decline when substance hasn't arrived). Reasoning: 'ordinary tasks may not mutate intent' is satisfied structurally (immutable contracts, revise-intent authority floor, privileged trio, first-intent-wins); three of the four process elements are live (contract identity, classifier-grain diff via the landed dx02/pr12 campaigns, policy verdict); the fourth is discharged by content identity with the explicit producer a pinned absence; the remaining gaps (a-e) are all no-producer absences that cannot violate the invariant while nothing produces them, each pinned to fail loudly. This is INV-008's shape (annotated with 2/5 kinds unlanded), not INV-014's (substance not arrived). A reviewer weighing it differently can strip the tag and regen.\n\nGATES: fmt --check clean; clippy --workspace --all-targets --locked -D warnings clean; cargo test -p continuum-intent --test inv001_protected_intent_evidence 20/20; full just check (fmt, lint, workspace tests, boundaries, covenant, governance x6, dossier, lean build + empty axiom manifest) exit 0. plan.md INV-001 heading annotated (delivered: bn-34je); just traceability regenerated (INV-001 active -> satisfied, one status flip, diff tight); validation-results.json untouched; no .bones/ touched; commit f0594e5 in-workspace only.\n\nCONCERNS: (1) The daemon-boundary and campaign citations are source-text tripwires, not re-dispatches — a behavior change that preserves the pinned strings would not be caught here; the owning suites (daemon_operations.rs, dx02, pr12) remain the behavioral guards and just check still runs them. (2) The verb map's policy column is the replicated-register fixture's table; Die Hard's stricter table (assumptions locked) is exercised by the cited campaign rows (DX02-A18), not re-closed here. (3) Absence pins b and d are substring sweeps over real directory walks — loud on landing, but a producer landing under a different spelling than 'AcceptancePath'/'put_intent' would need pin maintenance; flagged in the file's module doc.\n\nNot closing bn-34je per instructions."}	blake3:jGrSn0dkvXcOs9KgXRZTgv23OWD-cVRuM5U9oWGH05o
1785890916218876	continuum-dev	itc:v3:AWKSTzM5JJnJPkQAAAAAQar23VW6voAAAAEy1gs		item.comment	bn-2nwpg	{"body":"Lead: merged @ epoch 42b09f53db84. Polarity adjudication ACCEPTED — my brief suggested dualization; the worker followed the text instead: RFC 0031's 'exactly as for claims — the same order' governs, the antitone marker is fairness-condition-scoped, and the correction-15 extremum family has no assumptions[].expression entry (pinned against the live schema). Proven not assumed: dualizing mutant wrong in BOTH directions on the real corpus. expression_relation promoted pub(crate) so the S3 license is written once — the one-comparator rule held. Decidable single-axis Finite edits now affirm strengthened/weakened (NetworkNoForgery escape-disjunct drop → strengthened → review under its own verb, block under locked — the upgrade observable and safe); compound/unlicensed/undecidable/budget/both-directions all still fail closed with non-vacuous pins. Fairness audit went beyond unchanged to RFC-correct, with the dualize-table pin carrying the RFC's sentence verbatim. Zero flipped pins — DX02-A04/impl03 hold for the S2 reason, stale prose amended assertions-untouched. 147 crate tests. Closing."}	blake3:k85M8S6XTRMLj-rBhBmvQq7yom4aJ-eS15PsKJByRL4
