1785891757424682	continuum-dev	itc:v3:AWKSTzM5JJnJPkQAAAAAQar23VW6voAAAAEy4As		item.comment	bn-37gu	{"body":"EARLY SCOPE ASSESSMENT (per the honest-scope rule): which of the three G0-DX-01 pass-condition legs are dischargeable today at production grain.\n\nThe landed surface, read: crates/continuum-context (all six PR-11 IMPL bullets), crates/continuumd/src/daemon/context.rs (context.expand live; context.compile refused UnsupportedSemanticFeature — \"RFC 0028's ten-stage compiler is not wired anywhere in this workspace\"), crates/continuum-engine-reference (real transition semantics, exploration, checking, shortest witness), RFC 0028, START_HERE PR-11 section + exit sentence.\n\nLEG-BY-LEG:\n\n1. Causal core replay-preserving — PARTIAL. The replay CHECK is dischargeable at production grain: RFC 0028 \"Validation\" makes the checker independent of the compiler by design, and continuum-engine-reference's own Model::is_enabled/action_successors decide whether a core replays step for step while checking::check decides whether the failure reproduces. The core SELECTION has no producer: stage 2 (backward causal slicing) is part of the unbuilt ten-stage compiler. The campaign will implement stage-2 dynamic dependence slicing in harness code over the model's own declared read/write sets (production expr AST via BoolExpr::variables/IntExpr::variables), declared as harness grain, with drop-a-causal-event controls showing the production replay comparison can fail.\n\n2. >=10x context reduction — PARTIAL. The counting rule is production (RFC 0028 correction 17: measured bytes = the whole published canonical encoding, checkable via pack::budget_bytes_of and the least-fixed-point reading), and every fragment (SelectedItem/Manifest/Target/Verdict/Assurance/ReplayRef canonical JSON) is production. Whole-pack ASSEMBLY of the root document is declined by every landed bullet, so the 17-key assembly is harness grain. Baseline will be conservative: min(canonical JSON of the full trace, engine's own witness-format rendering).\n\n3. Exact expansion handles — PRODUCTION, end to end: parent pack registered through DaemonState::put_context_pack (the out-of-band surface a deployment uses), context.expand through Daemon::dispatch, ExpansionHandle::derive over the ID5 canonical question, the promise derivable from the omission record alone vs the returned ctx_*, and the child's selected[] vs the exact omitted items — plus the BudgetPacker branch under a ceiling.\n\nTRACE PRODUCER EXISTS: the 200+ event noisy durability failure can be synthesized through the real engine — a declared RFC-0007-vocabulary storage model (submit/ack-before-flush/power-loss, plus independent noise actors and a benign second writer with durability-vocabulary names as red herrings) driven by a declared deterministic schedule through Model::successors (the dx10 declared-schedule precedent), with the refuted invariant decided by production explore+check over the complete state space and corroborated by witness::shortest.\n\nMISSING PRODUCERS, NAMED (residual routing): (a) the ten-stage compiler (context.compile; stages 1-8 must provide candidate-set construction and backward causal slicing licensing CausallyClosed/ReplayPreserving, with auditable intermediates per RFC 0030 compared artifact 5); (b) whole-pack root assembly (no landed bullet claims it; reconciles ctx_* question identity with store content identity); (c) the crashpack producer (\"nothing in this workspace builds a crashpack\"), so the pack's replay field names a class-checked crash_* handle with no artifact behind it. Residual routes to bn-3m65 (PR-11 exit) and the compiler's own future bone.\n\nProceeding: full campaign at this grain in crates/continuumd/tests/dx01_falsification.rs (engine + context + daemon are all continuumd dev-deps), dx02 house style — pre-registered expectations, load-bearing controls, byte-stable golden evidence artifact, src/ untouched."}	blake3:1fpIAOgCho5So8KOMP05usFeytKwfnRztdXT-WTvqa0
1785892459369523	continuum-dev	itc:v3:AWKSTzM5JJnJPkQAAAAAQar23VW6voAAAAEy4Qs		item.comment	bn-3990	{"body":"G0-DX-12 falsification COMPLETE — pass condition holds at production grain; no unauthorized channel landed.\n\nWHAT RAN: crates/continuumd/tests/dx12_falsification.rs (16 tests, all green, un-ignored). Four swarm roles as identities+capability profiles driven as principals over the real daemon wire (Daemon::dispatch only): planner (agent:planner, revise-intent level, NO privileged op = docs/49 proposal-only cell), repairer (agent:repairer, execute+production-trace, the adversary), prover (agent:prover, execute+production-trace), reviewer (service:reviewer, promote + privileged intent.accept/reject/lock AND the daemon's verification service via EvidenceFamily::verifying_as). src/ untouched (bn-21dd precedent).\n\nCHANNELS (enumerated from RFC 0027/0037/0038 + IDL, not invented) — every one refused by a typed authority check AND left the record unchanged (a graph/registry fingerprint is read before and after each attack):\n- A1 producer intent.accept -> CapabilityDenied (T1 and T3)\n- A2 planner has the level, not the privilege, accepts -> CapabilityDenied (RFC 0027 \"privilege is not a level\"; the T3-isolating channel)\n- A3 producer intent.lock -> CapabilityDenied (T3)\n- A4 planner proposes onto a LOCKED field -> IntentMutationDenied (daemon enforces the lock, RFC 0037 P4; admission passes, so this is the daemon itself, not the capability layer)\n- A5 producer intent.reject -> CapabilityDenied\n- B1 non-service principal mints CHECKED_BY edge -> CapabilityDenied (RFC 0038 Authority: checker is a service: actor; repairer AND planner both refused at the scheme, not the ladder)\n- B2 promotion forgery -> no status field on observe.ingest; producer append lands proposed; expected_status is the CAS guard not the write; a verify writes the SERVICE's re-derivation (observed) and no higher, never the caller's; Validated guard -> StatusConflict (INV-004)\n- B3 self-certification: reviewer service verifies/links its own production -> InsufficientEvidence, before the artifact is read (control: prover's node verifies+links)\n- B4 edge retargeting: misfiled/retargeted node -> CertificateRejected (re-derivation, RFC 0038 D2/D4; control: node under its own identity verifies)\n- B5 authorized-edge replay to smuggle content: identical replay converges on ONE edge (provenance outside the identity, D4); different-content replay mints a DISTINCT visible attributed edge, never a silent rewrite (edge_id IS the content of what it asserts, D2); original edge bytes unchanged\n- C1 intent-status via evidence writes: the whole evidence workflow around a stable accepted contract leaves it byte-identical — evidence graph and intent registry are separate stores, no evidence.*/observe.* op writes an intent status; the channel a naive design leaves open does not exist\n\nBASELINE/CONTROLS (as load-bearing as the attacks): authorized accept by reviewer moves proposal->Accepted; authorized lock mints a superseding successor; ordinary evidence work (ingest->verify->link) flows clean end to end. Every isolating attack carries a control satisfying only that gate.\n\nANTI-VACUITY (the harness can fail): mutant_granting_the_planner_the_accept_privilege_lands_the_unauthorized_accept — same actor/level, one privileged op added, A2's accept now LANDS; mutant_a_service_actor_lands_the_check_edge_the_agent_could_not — B1's identical link from a service: actor lands. A fail-open authority check flips the verdict, so the campaign is not vacuous.\n\nROW: G0-DX-12 -> \"Evidence (reference implementation)\" (Evidence + Decision cells rewritten in house style; traceability regenerated -> req:g0-dx-12 satisfied; plan section 0.3 evidence set unchanged since DX-12 was already startswith-Evidence). Scope disclosed honestly: single-threaded dispatch = the linearized-per-claim write model RFC 0038 fixes, NO concurrency claim (concurrency is DX-13, evidenced in continuum-workspace). Classifier-grain weakening (weaken property/strengthen assumptions/reduce bounds/hide observers/remove faults) is DX-02's axis — cited (bn-3cgt dx02_falsification.rs), not re-run. One recorded boundary, not a defect: intent.propose_revision returns UnsupportedSemanticFeature for an UNLOCKED-field change (RFC 0031 classifier is later PR-12 daemon work), but a LOCKED-field change is refused IntentMutationDenied first (A4), so the lock — not the unshipped classifier — holds the stable intent stable. This closes RFC 0038's own \"Acceptance\" (parallel swarm, adversarial false consensus) at the authority dimension.\n\nPHASE-A-DEL-04/09 (both labels ride on this bone) — NEITHER annotated delivered, per annotate-vs-decline (substance not fully arrived). DEL-04 \"evidence graph\": DX-12 discharges its swarm-authority ACCEPTANCE, but the graph's remaining Phase A substance is disclosed unbuilt — evidence.subscribe event channel (typed-refused today), the whiteboard compiler, and the full RFC 0038 query set (proof/repair frontier, semantic duplicates, task generation). DEL-09 \"agent protocol spike parity\": DX-12 provides multi-agent wire-parity evidence for the four roles, but full agent-protocol/MCP surface parity is broader. LEAD ACTION AT CLOSE: re-cover req:phase-a-del-04 (other carrier bn-3rqvm is closed) and req:phase-a-del-09 (solely on this bone) to active successors, or traceability fails uncovered.\n\nCommitted in-workspace @33520f4; just check exit 0 (fmt/lint/test/boundaries/covenant/governance/dossier/lean all green). NOT merged/closed."}	blake3:qBHqwJkJiFORSmYE38ymz1RI0ZbsY0ajYD_pGUs-YoQ
