1785893149388845	continuum-dev	itc:v3:AWKSTzM5JJnJPkQAAAAAQar23VW6voAAAAEy5gs		item.comment	bn-37gu	{"body":"CAMPAIGN COMPLETE — G0-DX-01 executed at production grain where production exists, declared harness grain where the producer is missing, no attack landed. Delivered in workspace bn-37gu (committed, just check exit 0; NOT merged): crates/continuumd/tests/dx01_falsification.rs (12 tests, all green, default suite) + golden evidence artifact crates/continuumd/tests/golden/dx01_falsification_evidence.txt + G0_SPIKE_MATRIX.md DX-01 row update + regenerated traceability/validation.\n\nLEG-BY-LEG GRAIN TABLE (as declared in the file BEFORE any number):\n- Leg 1, causal core replay-preserving: PARTIAL. Check = production (Model::action_successors decides replay step for step; checking::check/evaluate_predicate decide refutation — RFC 0028 \"Validation\" makes checkers compiler-independent by design). Selection = harness (stage-2 dynamic dependence slicing over the model's declared read/write sets via the production expr AST), because the ten-stage compiler is unbuilt.\n- Leg 2, >=10x reduction: PARTIAL. Counting = production (RFC 0028 correction 17: recorded size == published canonical length, read back through pack::budget_bytes_of; every fragment is the production rendering; INV-007 conservation through the production ClosedAccounting). Assembly = harness (no landed root-pack writer; the 17-key join applies the packer's own least-fixed-point measurement reading).\n- Leg 3, exact expansion handles: PRODUCTION end to end (DaemonState::put_context_pack registration, Daemon::dispatch, ExpansionHandle::derive).\n\nMEASUREMENTS (pinned in the golden artifact):\n- Trace: 225 events (221 noise incl. red-herring names telemetry_flush/scrub_write_verify/a correct replica writer), produced through the real engine under a declared schedule; complete exploration = 5,248 states; engine verdict refuted; witness::shortest == the 4-event core (begin_txn, submit_write, ack_before_flush, power_loss) — independent production corroboration of the slice.\n- Leg 1: core replays and reproduces the refutation (client_acked=1, wal_durable=0, wal_buffered=0); causal closure witnessed by demanded-sub-state agreement at every core step; all four drop-one mutants fail their pre-registered way (two disabled steps, two lost refutations — both failure modes exercised); reordered core disabled; textual-relevance control (RFC 0028 C2's named exclusion) admits 67 noise events, misses begin_txn+power_loss, fails strict replay, and does not refute even forgivingly.\n- Leg 2: pack 2,791 B vs graded raw 48,764 B = 17.47x PASS. Sensitivity published (dx10 pattern): engine positional Display 4.92x, positional JSON 4.50x, delta log 3.93x, action-name log 1.44x — the 10x sign flips only under stripped encodings no landed producer emits; pack header is 1,498 of 2,791 B (redesign-actionable).\n- Leg 3: promised ctx_* (derived from the published omission record ALONE) == returned ctx_*; expansion returns exactly the 248 omitted transition items byte for byte under an empty residual manifest; second idempotency key -> same handle, byte-identical pack; budget branch keeps the promise (recoverable_by == same handle, conservation exact, typed BudgetExhausted below the minimal child); promise check shown able to fail (tampered record derives a different handle; hostile anchor/undefined relation/unheld pack land on three distinct typed refusals).\n\nROW STATUS: Evidence (reference implementation) — per the dx02/dx03/dx14 precedent (Status prefix exact, scope stated plainly in the Evidence/Decision cells). The Decision cell names the missing producer in its first sentence.\n\nRESIDUAL, ROUTED: (1) the ten-stage compiler (context.compile refused UnsupportedSemanticFeature) — must provide candidate-set construction + stage-2 slicing licensing CausallyClosed/ReplayPreserving with auditable intermediates (RFC 0030 compared artifact 5); (2) root-pack assembly (reconcile ctx_* question identity with store content identity); (3) crashpack producer + intent-registry resolution (the pack's replay/intent are class-checked handles with no artifacts behind them). All owned by bn-3m65 (PR-11 exit — its sentence is this experiment run BY the compiler) and the compiler's own bone. Typed-vocabulary absences recorded: EventRole is the causal-core split so slice-irrelevant events are accounted as their concrete per-variable transitions; no landed trace serializer, so the graded baseline is defined in the file with every hostile reading's ratio beside it.\n\nTEXTS vs BRIEF: no divergence found. §0.3 left untouched deliberately — it defers statuses to the matrix (\"Statuses live in notes/G0_SPIKE_MATRIX.md, from which these counts derive\"), and the dx02/dx03/dx13/dx14 upgrades established that its Phase A \"carry spike evidence\" sentence stays as the historical record. Dossier validator: status pass, g0_matrix_counts {evidence: 6, open_freeze_blocking: 1, rehomed: 8}."}	blake3:dSF1EgKPH37itC0yjyZM_CUVRZAO2Fcfyn8Q8e6thiY
1785893149430515	continuum-dev	itc:v3:AWKSTzM5JJnJPkQAAAAAQar23VW6voAAAAEy5ws		item.comment	bn-3m65	{"body":"Routing note from bn-37gu (G0-DX-01 falsification, delivered): the DX-01 campaign ran the 200+ event durability experiment at the deepest landed grain — crates/continuumd/tests/dx01_falsification.rs, evidence pinned at tests/golden/dx01_falsification_evidence.txt. What this exit bone still owes is the experiment run BY the compiler: RFC 0028's ten-stage pipeline is the named missing producer (context.compile is refused; stage-2 causal slicing and root-pack assembly ran as declared harness code in the campaign). The campaign's model, schedule, slice, and baselines are reusable as this exit's fixture; its leg-by-leg grain table and residual routing are in the DX-01 matrix row's Decision cell and the bn-37gu bone comments."}	blake3:qBf07-Yeu1_mAICcMEDoJ43bKdOT364hBjS5FEKvpls
