1785893525391056	continuum-dev	itc:v3:AWKSTzM5JJnJPkQAAAAAQar23VW6voAAAAEy6gs		item.comment	bn-7ek41	{"body":"PR-12 wire assembler + impact set delivered in workspace bn-7ek41 (commit f3c6a7a; just check exit 0): crates/continuum-semantic-diff/src/{artifact,impact}.rs + tests/pr12_wire_assembler_and_impact_evidence.rs (15 tests) + retained golden tests/golden/pr12_wire_artifact.json. 2860 workspace tests green.\n\nARTIFACT SHAPE (schemas decide): artifact.rs assembles the one diff_* shape against the live semantic-diff.schema.json — schema_id/epoch consts, five validated identities (DiffId/SnapshotId newtypes pattern-checked; IntentId reused; handles are inputs, never derived — ADR-0013, minting is the daemon's), classifier{intent-diff-0.1.0, cpnf-1} (F3), requested_assurance (F2), per-unit unit locators (F1), semantic_changes[] (typed seven-axis input; advisory, never touches the verdict), impact, policy. Emission rule resolved one way for canonicality: unchanged records omitted; the verdict input carries what the wire omits (P1-complete, equality.rs's promised split honored — shortcut = zero wire records, fifteen verdict records). Correction 14 pinned at byte grain: equal canonical identities produce literally \"intent_changes\":[] in the bytes, decided on preimage bytes not handle strings. Verdict = PolicyTable::verdict against the BEFORE contract's table+reviewers (P7, harness precedent), AcceptancePath a parameter; policy.reasons = P6 set rendered via VerdictReason Display, deduped/sorted (uniqueItems). NO SECOND AUTHORITY: family records consumed as-is; the eight classifier-less fields get the exit-blessed R2/fail-closed closure made production, at the schema's OWN locator grain (scope by sub-field, abstraction_maps by role, nondeterminism by site, optimization/non_vacuity by member, security_policy by component) since the schema REQUIRES unit on those fields — equal canonical content unchanged, anything else unknown, no membership direction ever minted (the exit's abstraction_maps:unknown boundary held). assurance folds BOTH halves per its module doc: the change_to triple + evidence_class_changes membership records.\n\nCLAMP (bn-8mlg flag c, mine): below bounded, expression-derived directions report unknown on wire AND verdict (the two must agree — the schema's fail-closed allOf reads wire relations). Clamped set = directions resting on a formula comparison: properties/assumptions strengthened/weakened (only directional source is the Finite oracle = bounded-class evidence, admissible bounded+ per the RFC table), plus fairness same-key directions where BOTH sides declare a condition (unreachable today — no license reaches classify_fairness — stated now so the recorded fairness-oracle upgrade cannot silently open a below-bounded direction). NOT clamped: the table's nine encoding-decidable relations, and by the same sentence's own concept the two fairness shapes that never consult a formula's language — kind swap (definitional) and condition declaredness move (C to null, presence alone) — both pinned by test (a weak-to-strong swap survives at observed). Evidence: the same Agreement weakening reports weakened at bounded/validated/proved and unknown at observed/sampled, block either way under the fixture's locked verb; assumptions mirror via bn-2nwpg's own mutation.\n\nUNSUPPORTED (assembler-owned, every classifier's recorded fence): any declared expression fragment of a properties/assumptions unit, on any side it exists, outside after.scope.fragments forces unsupported — the MUST is unconditional so it reaches unchanged pairs (narrowing converts to fail-closed, never allowed); an undeclared fragment denotes the contract's declared set (W3), always in scope. Fragment attribution (SHOULD): emitted when every side the unit exists on declares the same one. Evidence: dropping Finite from the corpus scope forces all six Finite units unsupported + scope/fragments unknown, closing block; baseline anti-vacuity: zero unsupported with the fragment declared.\n\nIMPACT SET (RFC 0031 'Impact set', scope implemented not invented): compute_impact partitions the caller-supplied naming scope into invalidated/reused/unknown — pairwise disjoint and total by construction (severity fold invalidated > unknown > reused, deterministic trigger order). RFC 0030's closed sets restated locally token-for-token (DependencyReason x9, ReuseEdgeClass x4, independence tri-state) because continuum-incremental is a PR-23 scaffold with no types — the module doc records the two-renderings rule for when PR 23 lands. Triggers: (1) properties changed = the query-key rule, keyed_to_before_intent invalidated unless a Validated checker witness licenses reuse (both facts on EvidenceRecord since no reason token expresses a key change, per RFC 0030's own table); (2) mapped reasons per the RFC table including the correspondence program axis; (3) no-reason fields (faults/completion_policy/nondeterminism/trust_boundaries/security_policy/optimization/non_vacuity) yield independence Unknown for EVERY in-scope artifact (the load-bearing row — a witnessed independence on another reason still lands unknown, tested). Non-affirmative field relations count as changed. Promotion-facing reuse licensing: Exact/Validated need a witness (unwitnessed strong-class independence is ill-formed and fails to unknown), Conservative is its own named justification (the 'conservatively rebuilt' distinction lives in the typed Dispositions per INV-003; the wire arrays are the rendering), Experimental never reaches reused ('MUST NOT support promotion') and fails to unknown with cause. A duplicate evidence identity refuses the whole artifact.\n\nEVIDENCE: real-corpus end-to-end (Agreement complementary-disjunct + nodes 3-to-2 riding together) into schema-valid canonical bytes byte-pinned (PR12_ARTIFACT_BLESS always red) into block with P6 reasons naming both, all three impact sets populated; independently cross-validated with the real jsonschema library (golden + corrected example both pass). The in-test conformance checker is DERIVED from the live schema bytes (required lists, enums, protected const, the 11-field unit rule, patterns, the fail-closed allOf all navigated out of the document; an unrecognized pattern is an error, never a skip) and proven non-vacuous against six doctored artifacts. Nine-scenario battery all schema-valid + round-trip + policy.decision equals the typed verdict (the wire-surface MUST). Rename disguise = removed+added with both locators. An allowed revision (evidence-class removal; no-downgrade does not deny removed) still invalidates lemma-dependent evidence — the impact set is not the verdict. INV-005: byte-identical under evidence/semantic-changes input permutation.\n\nRECORDED DIVERGENCES/FLAGS (schema-sweep SD-08 candidates, in module docs, not silently resolved): (a) the schema's unit comment says assurance has 'no sub-unit to name' but RFC 0031 classifies accepted_evidence_classes by membership per class — those records carry the class token as unit (schema-legal: unit is a defined property on every record; dropping it would leave the class identity with no typed home, the INV-003 failure F1 was paid to end); (b) a collapsed fairness kind-change record is rendered with the after-side key (strong:A) since kind:action cannot name a swapped pair in one token — the before side is derivable from the relation under correction 16's clean-swap scope; (c) F5-shaped locator collisions on security_policy dedupe to one record. SMALL CROSS-CRATE TOUCHES: continuum-intent/assurance_policy now pub-uses the assurance vocabulary it already returns from public accessors (the assembler names AssuranceLevel through the crate that hands it out, no new continuum-value edge); the inv001 module-list tripwire updated for the two non-classifier modules with a comment saying why they may never enter the classifier column.\n\nDEL-06: START_HERE PR-12 (the IMPL-05 bullet's remain-open tail) annotated delivered; plan section 21 'semantic diff v0' annotated sibling-style, scoped honestly (library-level engine per RFC 0031; daemon DiffHandle endpoints ride their protocol PRs); traceability regenerated — PHASE-A-DEL-06 satisfied, 659 active. Not merged, not pushed, bone left open for the lead."}	blake3:PYOyMXENl40Arvrza7tWPJ_DQ_n07bmjotcAljfQORM
1785893605868080	continuum-dev	itc:v3:AWKSTzM5JJnJPkQAAAAAQar23VW6voAAAAEy6ws		item.comment	bn-7ek41	{"body":"Lead: merged @ epoch 2f3045763f07 (759 intent+semantic-diff tests re-verified post-rebase). SEMANTIC DIFF v0 COMPLETE — PHASE-A-DEL-06 satisfied. Assembler accepted: one diff_* shape pinned against the live schema, handles as inputs never derived (minting is the daemon's per ADR-0013), correction 14's literal empty intent_changes[] asserted at byte grain with the shortcut decided on preimage bytes; family records consumed as-is with the eight classifier-less fields made production at the schema's own locator grain, unchanged/unknown only, no direction ever minted. Clamp exactly per bn-8mlg flag (c): expression-derived directions → unknown below bounded on wire AND verdict, encoding-decidable directions exempt and pinned. Fragment-scope unsupported unconditional, reaching unchanged pairs — narrowing never converts to allow. Impact set exactly RFC 0031's section, RFC 0030 closed sets token-for-token with the two-renderings rule documented against the empty PR-23 scaffold, Experimental/unwitnessed strong-class independence failing to unknown. Conformance checker DERIVED from live schema bytes, non-vacuous against six doctored artifacts, cross-validated with real jsonschema. Three flags noted as SD-08 candidates in module docs (assurance unit token, fairness kind-swap locator, cross-crate pub use). Closing."}	blake3:o4jPnNfLK8TyQgtYflure5lPx2BquF_i53eDu5Runak
