1785901782858159	continuum-dev	itc:v3:AWKSTzM5JJnJPkQAAAAAQar23VW6voAAAAEy8ws		item.comment	bn-3m65	{"body":"ADJUDICATION (a): the PR-11 exit CLOSES AT THE DECLARED GRAINS bn-37gu established — the word 'compiles' does not demand the ten-stage compiler as producer first — with the compiler as the exit's NAMED owed producer and a live grain guard so the close cannot linger silently once a compiler lands.\n\nTEXTUAL BASIS, four legs:\n(1) RFC 0028 'Validation': 'the checkers are independent of the compiler that made the claim — INV-004's discipline applied here', and C6: a promotion-relevant consumer 'MUST re-run the checker rather than read the field'. In this program replay-preservation is established by the checker over the artifact, never conferred by the producer's pedigree — so every predicate the exit sentence asserts (replay-preserving core, substantial reduction, exact expansion handles) is checker-established at PRODUCTION grain in the dx01 campaign: the production engine's replay check + checking::check + witness::shortest independently equal to the 4-event core; the packer's own counting rule (correction 17); Daemon::dispatch end to end. Only the verb's production wiring is missing, and it is a named absence, not a silent one.\n(2) The exit-precedent conventions: a PR exit is the PR's own completion claim, read over its delivered surface with the boundary named at the point it is crossed. PR-5 closed with the CBOR half of every golden vector explicitly owed; PR-8 closed with the crashpack producer absent ('the field exists, the producer does not') and the 96 corroborated one layer down under RFC 0026 F16; PR-6's 'every instrumented phase' closed over the wire-reachable set. Same shape here: grain declared in the Exit annotation itself, residual named in it.\n(3) PR-11's own scope defines 'compiler v0' and every bullet of it is delivered — several ARE compiler stages in substance (BudgetPacker = stage 10 with the RFC's packing MUSTs as tests; closed accounting = the manifest-reconciliation validation row; expansion wire-live), RFC 0028 itself blesses 'plain causal slice + expansion, stage 9 disabled' as a runnable configuration, and no bullet claims stages 1-9 ('the compiler itself ... is unbuilt' is their own landed text). The completion claim over those bullets demands the integration demonstration, which bn-37gu delivered adversarially.\n(4) The controlling instance: the G0-DX-01 row — this sentence in the matrix's own words, under the heavier consequence ('redesign evidence model') — was accepted at exactly these grains with the compiler named in the Decision cell's first sentence. No text holds the PR exit to a stricter standard than the kill-criteria row it instantiates. The one compiler-demanding text — the row's routing parenthetical 'whose sentence is this row's experiment run by the compiler' — is bn-37gu's routing gloss, routed to this bone for adjudication; no normative text (START_HERE PR-11, RFC 0028, plan section 21/25) conditions the exit on the pipeline, and plan section 25 frames the case consumer-side ('Agent receives a 200-event failing run through a 4-event Context Pack').\n\nDELIVERED in workspace bn-3m65 (committed, just check exit 0; NOT merged):\n- crates/continuumd/tests/pr11_exit_evidence.rs (5 tests, default suite) + golden tests/golden/pr11_exit_evidence.txt (bless always red, PR11_EXIT_BLESS=1): the independent exit layer over the bn-37gu campaign, touching none of its tests and none of src/. Every leg RE-DERIVED from the campaign artifact's bytes rather than its recorded flags: ratio recomputed from the byte counts (48,764/2,791 = 17.47x, graded at the row's 10x), witness-equals-core from the two membership lines, INV-007 conservation (258 = 10 + 248), the promise from the two handles; the grain declarations and missing-producer naming are REQUIRED by the closure — an artifact that stops declaring harness grain or stops naming the compiler is rejected, so the declared-grain close can never quietly become a production-grain claim.\n- Anti-vacuity: eight doctored artifacts each rejected by the same closure the genuine artifact passes (undercounted case, flipped verdict, control off its pre-registered failure, lying ratio, consistent sub-10x, broken promise, deleted harness declaration, deleted compiler naming), each matched to its own rejection arm.\n- Grain guard, live: context.compile dispatched against a real daemon, refused UnsupportedSemanticFeature with no payload — pinned so a landed compiler turns this exit layer red and forces the re-run at production grain.\n- The sentence closed against the dossier, not restated: START_HERE's PR-11 Exit line (verbatim sentence + delivered annotation + residual named), the G0-DX-01 row's experiment and pass condition, and the campaign artifact's own header held to one another.\n- START_HERE Exit line annotated (delivered: bn-3m65 — grains declared in the annotation itself, numbers, precedents, residual); traceability regenerated: PR-11-EXIT -> satisfied, PR-11 -> satisfied; dossier validator status pass.\n\nRESIDUAL (unchanged from bn-37gu's routing, now carried by the Exit annotation and the exit artifact): the ten-stage compiler — candidate-set construction, stage-2 backward causal slicing licensing CausallyClosed/ReplayPreserving, auditable intermediates (RFC 0030 compared artifact 5) — plus root-pack assembly (ctx_* question identity vs store content identity), the crashpack producer, and intent-registry resolution. Recommended compiler-bone shape: stages 1-8 over the evidence graph with per-stage auditable intermediates, context.compile wired through daemon::context ('when the compiler lands it will write through the same surface' is that module's own text), whole-pack assembly + publication decision, and the production-grain re-run of DX-01's experiment as its own exit; stage 9 explicitly deferrable per RFC 0028's fallback configuration. Size: L."}	blake3:xa6kbENmvSj6LZdsyVglSJL2sNx4dwTSSU8wskboP6U
1785901852968119	continuum-dev	itc:v3:AWKSTzM5JJnJPkQAAAAAQar23VW6voAAAAEy9As		item.create	bn-8g9uj	{"description":"The named residual from PR-11's exit (bn-3m65, adjudication (a)) and the DX-01 row: RFC 0028's ten-stage compiler is the missing producer — context.compile is refused UnsupportedSemanticFeature and root pack assembly is a test harness. bn-3m65's bone comment records the recommended shape: stages 1-8 with auditable intermediates (BudgetPacker already = stage 10 in substance, closed accounting = the manifest-reconciliation validation row; RFC 0028 blesses slice+expansion with stage 9 disabled as runnable), context.compile daemon wiring, production root assembly, and G0-DX-01 re-run at production grain as its exit. The pr11_exit_evidence.rs grain guard pins context.compile's refusal LIVE — landing the compiler flips that exit red by design, forcing the production re-run. This bone is the staging/scoping carrier: at pickup, split into child bones per stage group (the full build is L-class and must not be one leaf).","kind":"task","labels":["req:pr-11","implementation"],"size":"m","title":"Context Pack compiler v0: stage the build (stages 1-8, context.compile wiring, root assembly)"}	blake3:3xRJYG-wY_gc5cu1SnSVM1P_VUnv3pDwyUxBcCpR5k8
1785901853011430	continuum-dev	itc:v3:AWKSTzM5JJnJPkQAAAAAQar23VW6voAAAAEy9Qs		item.comment	bn-3m65	{"body":"Lead: merged @ epoch 13d5729819fb. Adjudication (a) RATIFIED — the four-legged argument is exactly right: RFC 0028's own Validation section makes every checker compiler-independent (INV-004/C6), the PR-5/PR-8 exit precedents close true-at-delivered-grain sentences with the boundary named, several delivered bullets ARE compiler stages in substance, and the DX-01 row accepted the same sentence under the heavier consequence. The live grain guard is the right falsification-discipline move: a landed compiler flips this exit red and forces the production re-run — the exit cannot silently outlive its own grain. Exit layer re-derives every leg from artifact bytes (17.47× recomputed, conservation 258=10+248), rejects eight doctored artifacts incl. grain-hiding and compiler-unnaming ones. PR 11 FULLY EXITED. Compiler staging bone created carrying the recommended shape with req:pr-11. Closing."}	blake3:got24Vv0MfkeiFNqCvkGfRJDws7SCOX8NnLgV9i_u8M
