1785904989520312	continuum-dev	itc:v3:AWKSTzM5JJnJPkQAAAAAQar23VW6voAAAAEyigw		item.comment	bn-33iv	{"body":"R14 risk checkpoint complete. All five controls (docs/08_RISK_REGISTER.md:211-224, identical on this bone) verified against the live repository, in-workspace at .maw/workspaces/bn-33iv/ (committed b5f827a). Full citation-dense evidence: notes/plan/notes/R14_ALIEN_MATH_THEATER_EVIDENCE.md. Checkpoint added no source code — R14's failure mode is claims outrunning evidence, so verification here is citation, not delivery.\n\nCONTROL -> EVIDENCE\n\n1. Research labels — LIVE. Every alien-math claim (C014-C017, docs/18_CLAIMS_MATRIX.md:32-35) is HYPOTHESIS, never a stronger word; research/07-alien-mathematics.md opens \"none of these ideas are product claims\" and closes with a 9-item governance list ending \"no effect on stable semantics until an ADR promotes it.\" Direct recursive grep for sheaf|homology|cohomolog|HDA|category.theor across README.md, notes/plan/README.md, and crates/** (source code): zero hits — no shipped capability claims exist to mislabel. tools/governance/check_claim_governance.py mechanically scans README + 55 docs + plan.md for bare uncontrolled claim verbs; self-test 13/13 fixtures caught, real run: 58 documents scanned, 0 violations.\n\n2. Baseline and threshold — LIVE. plan.md §24.5: \"Every HYPOTHESIS-class capability... is owned by a research lane with a baseline, a quantitative promotion threshold, a kill criterion, and a named fallback.\" tools/validate_dossier.py's check_register_rows() mechanically enforces a kill/defer/draft marker per row AND register<->research-note quote-id identity (marked quotes must match verbatim). Live run: register_rows: {rows: 21, ratified_quotes_checked: 6}. Sheaf-based-composition row cites docs/31's promote/kill pair with fallback \"monolithic composition proofs\" as its named baseline.\n\n3. No correctness claim from heuristic topology — LIVE, with an honest scope note. INV-004 (delivered bn-11yx/bn-24i/bn-3sypm/bn-bou09): the four continuum-kernel-* crates are the sole verdict authority, composed behind continuum-certificate, whose Cargo.toml declares nothing but those four crates. INV-008 (delivered bn-n9a1) adds the four-kernel vocabulary sweep: crates/continuum-kernel-core/tests/inv008_unsupported_vs_rejected_evidence.rs::positive_is_verified_is_the_only_boolean_projection_in_every_kernel_crate pins that no second boolean escape hatch exists anywhere in the trusted checking base. Structural confinement: tools/check_kernel_covenant.py KCOV-06 enforces the four kernel crates admit ZERO dependencies (ADMITTED_KERNEL_DEPENDENCIES is the empty frozenset) — mechanically, not by convention, nothing heuristic or topological can reach a verdict. Both check_kernel_covenant.py and check_crate_boundaries.py self-tests + real runs pass clean in this checkpoint's run. Gap stated plainly: the only shipped \"heuristic\" surface is OmissionReason::HeuristicCutoff (continuum-context, RFC 0028 context-pack omission bookkeeping, not a verdict type) and zero sheaf/homology/topology code exists anywhere in crates/** today — so the confinement guarantee is currently exercised vacuously. That is the correct state for Phase A, but it means the guarantee has not yet been tested against a real topological implementation attempt.\n\n4. Kill criteria — LIVE. research/07 states an explicit kill condition per core alien-math idea (directed topology, sheaves, homology, category theory); docs/31_FALSIFICATION_AND_KILL_CRITERIA.md restates two with numeric promote/kill pairs; ADR-0020 is the binding decision record and explicitly rejects the R14 failure mode by name in its alternatives section: \"Use mathematical vocabulary only for marketing: explicitly rejected.\" Mechanically enforced by the same check_register_rows() marker rule (§24.5 rows) and check_adr_process.py (ADR-0020's 9 required sections, including validation/rollback, structurally present).\n\n5. Publish negative results — PARTIAL, honest gap. ADR-0020: \"Negative results are acceptable outputs.\" docs/18's REFUTED claim state mandates \"explicitly document the negative result.\" docs/12 §9 names \"sheaf/cubical experimental results, including negative findings\" as an intended publication output. But no §24.5 lane has reached a kill decision in Phase A yet, so there is no live REFUTED row and no mechanical validator that checks \"a fired kill criterion actually produced a published negative result\" — this control rests entirely on document policy, unexercised. Flagged in the evidence doc for a future checkpoint pass once any lane fires.\n\nDIVERGENCE FROM BRIEF: docs/08_RISK_REGISTER.md's R14 row (and all 21 rows in that file, R01-R21) carries no \"(delivered: ...)\" evidence-annotation convention anywhere, unlike plan.md's INV-NNN invariant list. Left the register row untouched per its own (absent) convention rather than inventing one; evidence recorded on this bone and in the dedicated note instead.\n\njust check: exit 0 (fmt, lint, full test suite, boundaries, kernel covenant, governance, dossier, Lean — all green; dossier register_rows and program_status confirmed live in the run). Left in doing; no merge/push/close performed. Claims to be released now."}	blake3:FTeyVDK6t7_0OddXLSNMKWZFO7gmEpTDcqU-WNlbrqc
1785905037606805	continuum-dev	itc:v3:AWKSTzM5JJnJPkQAAAAAQar23VW6voAAAAEyiww		item.comment	bn-33iv	{"body":"Lead: merged @ epoch 363ce8812f28. R14 checkpoint accepted — all three required controls verified LIVE with mechanical evidence (claim-governance checker 0 violations over 58 docs, register_rows reproduced 21/6, kernel-covenant KCOV-06 zero-dependency enforcement), plus the two honest scope notes that make this a real checkpoint rather than a rubber stamp: the topology-confinement guarantee is structurally sound but currently VACUOUS (only OmissionReason::HeuristicCutoff exists, a non-verdict type — the guarantee gets real content when frontier code lands), and publish-negative-results is policy-live but instance-empty (no Phase A kill has fired). Register-row divergence correctly recorded: docs/08 carries no delivered-annotation convention, so the row stays untouched rather than inventing one. Closing."}	blake3:hDGMaW-niBxg8JXkPQheADoDRxdidnliqrW3nn5hqs0
