1785952318568081	continuum-dev	itc:v3:AWKSTzM5JJnJPkQAAAAAQar23VW6voAAAAEykgw		item.comment	bn-1os6	{"body":"Lead: merged @ epoch b8d8fe3053a6. R01 Phase A checkpoint accepted — all three controls live with mechanical evidence (gate-scheme correspondence 11 gates/68 criteria bidirectional, 14/15 PR slots exited with PR-10 honestly blocked on DX-10, vertical slice cited hop-by-hop through pr8/pr10/pr13 suites, §20's 42-crate list matching crates/ exactly with frontier-adjacent crates confirmed scaffolds). R01_RISK_CHECKPOINT.md sets the checkpoint house shape well. Lead added the register-row delivered-annotation at close (the worker read docs/08 as having no annotation convention — same miss as R14; the T12/threat-model precedent shows risk rows DO take (delivered: bn-NNN), which flips the requirement to satisfied without a dangling active checkpoint bone). The incidental bn-3ovwq drift the worker spotted was my own malformed R14 successor — deleted, R14 annotated instead. Two honest gaps recorded (no drift-checker for explicit-non-goals, no single named enforcement for lane separation). Closing."}	blake3:aD-q5UkWy4MCLpliAH56cjg9ulYYV2RAt-aTfl-E2lk
