1785952479893077	continuum-dev	itc:v3:AWKSTzM5JJnJPkQAAAAAQar23VW6voAAAAEylgw		item.comment	bn-ulhg3	{"body":"Lead: merged @ epoch 03dc26ea72ec. MCP Refusal now carries data: Option<RefusalData>, resolved through the codec's own decode_error_data — typed CertificateRejection relayed verbatim (bn-dtg61 boundary intact, no second shape table, single continuumd edge preserved). Decode tolerance is the right posture: undeclared codes arrive as RefusalData::Undeclared(Opaque) preserved verbatim per RFC 0026's 3.4 'carry the canonical value verbatim, never guess' — and the recorded divergence-in-station is exactly the kind of honesty I want: the CLI hard-errors on the same input (version-locked to its daemon) while this external client must tolerate it. Evidence drives a real kernel rejection (trailing-byte CONTCERT) through evidence.verify over the client's own wire, held equal to the daemon's in-process typed outcome, forward-compat via a hand-built F11 retry-after frame, anti-vacuity by reintroducing the drop. F19's shape now reaches typed callers, not just the CLI. Closing."}	blake3:9FdUg-cLIyugH7U6pJN5fPn2itJWMDKjqB_79WA_obk
