1785953888354367	continuum-dev	itc:v3:AWKSTzM5JJnJPkQAAAAAQar23VW6voAAAAEyoww		item.comment	bn-3mjd	{"body":"INV-015 evidence delivered: crates/continuumd/tests/inv015_agent_least_authority_evidence.rs (28 tests, all green). Heading annotated `(delivered: bn-3mjd — …)`; traceability regenerated (INV-015 row active→satisfied). Zero src/ changes, zero existing tests touched, zero new dependency edges (every cross-crate citation is include_str! over tracked files — the inv008/inv014 device). Committed in-workspace @ 28928ba; NOT merged/pushed/closed.\n\nCONTRACT → CLAUSE → SITE MAP (each row: live enforcement site + direct test or freshness-tripwire citation)\n- \"alter evidence status\" → daemon/evidence.rs: Promotion has private fields + no public constructor, and the producer family lives in daemon/observe.rs (a DIFFERENT module), so producer code can name the type and never build one — bn-24i's compile-time device, which IS INV-015's first clause. Plus a LIVE registry sweep here proving no @mutation request carries a caller-supplied status field (the one status-named field anywhere is evidence.verify's expected_status, the CAS guard — what the caller believes, never what's written). Cited: a_producers_append_lands_at_the_lattices_bottom, the_status_written_is_what_the_checker_established_not_what_the_caller_named, no_operation_in_either_family_removes_or_edits_an_appended_node, a_verification_service_may_not_promote_a_claim_it_produced_itself.\n- \"sign receipts\" → evidence.link: checker is the admitted capability's actor (no checker request field), must be a service: scheme, self-cert refused before the receipt is read (RFC 0038 D3). Cited: only_a_service_actor_may_append_a_check_edge, a_checker_may_not_record_a_check_of_its_own_production. GAP: cryptographic signing (plan §18.6, docs/09 lifecycle) has NO producer — daemon stores an acceptance signature verbatim and verifies nothing; live source-walk pins the absence (no verify_signature/keypair token in any continuumd source).\n- \"access ungranted production traces\" → daemon/admission.rs R-4: observe.ingest requires DataGrant::ProductionTrace beyond execute, decided by required_grant() before any family runs — asserted LIVE off the production predicate (exactly one op requires a grant, and it's the trace grant). Denied is a zero-bit unit struct (X1), precedes the index (X3), reveals no existence (X2) — size_of asserted 0 here + cited byte-identical dispatch tests. GAP: §18.4 capture-time contract (salted commitments, per-artifact encryption, retention clock) has NO producer; the redaction half IS live (typed stubs + INV-007 omissions) and cited.\n- \"execute unrestricted host effects\" → structural: closed 73-op registry, NO capability namespace (RFC 0026 corr. 20: \"no operation in this protocol can widen the authority of the connection that invokes it\"); ReferenceStore::mint/revoke have no wire caller — live walk over every continuumd source finds zero .mint(/.revoke( callers. GAP: every host-effect crate (continuum-effects-{network,process,storage,time}, continuum-forge, continuum-proof-client, continuum-security) is a zero-pub-item PR-1/IMPL-01 scaffold — pinned to go red the moment any grows a public item.\n- cross-cutting \"no ambient authority / never by default\" → the @privileged perimeter is EXACTLY the five governance verbs (intent.accept/lock/reject, repair.promote/reject) and nothing else — asserted exhaustively as data (nothing did this before; a consistent sixth privileged op would have passed every existing gate). Each is @audit_recorded (docs/49 \"logs attempted privileged operations\"). Absent profile = fail-closed (\"grants nothing rather than everything\"), delegation only narrows — pinned at admission.rs + cited dispatch tests.\n\ndocs/49 authority rows: bn-34je's INV-001 suite already pins \"revise intent: proposal only\" verbatim — CITED via freshness tripwire, not re-derived (per the brief). The three INV-015-own rows (promote evidence yes/checker; production secrets no/default; arbitrary network/host exec no across every agent column) pinned here.\n\ndocs/49 WORKER-ISOLATION AUDIT (eight controls, as anti-drift data checked against docs/49's own bullet list): ZERO of the eight have a worker-scoped producer — no worker execution environment exists in this workspace, so nothing mounts/allowlists/kills a worker. Four have a live daemon/task-grain COUSIN one layer up (resource limits→budget ledger; output size/schema→INV-003 closure [schema half live, size half declared-only, see below]; cancellation→dx14 task.cancel matrix [hard-kill fallback presumes a process, none exists]; audit trace→obligation.rs audit_required + dispatcher denial audit). Four have none (pinned image/toolchain, read-only mount, no-ambient-credentials, network-disabled/allowlisted) — the repo's toolchain pins and INV-005's no-ambient-time/entropy are recorded as ADJACENT disciplines that deliberately claim NO row, because they govern the repo/daemon, not a worker mount. Extra live gap sweep: ServerLimits.max_result_bytes is declared on the handshake and read by no daemon/ source (size-limit half of control six is declared-not-enforced).\n\nANNOTATE-vs-DECLINE DECISION: ANNOTATE (delivered, with gaps stated inline), per the bn-n9a1 rule. Reasoning on the capability-half-live vs isolation-half-declared split the brief flagged: INV-015's contract is a set of four PROHIBITIONS (\"agents cannot…\"), and every one is enforced today at the surface where an agent can actually act — the native protocol. The capability half is fully live: status writes are a private-constructor witness in a foreign module, receipt edges are service-gated + no-self-cert, trace access is a pre-index data-grant with a zero-bit denial, and host effects/administration have no wire verb at all. That is the whole of what an agent CAN reach. The isolation half being largely declared-no-producer does NOT leave a prohibition unmet, because there is no worker execution environment for an agent to escape from — the controls guard a surface that does not exist yet, so their absence is a typed ABSENCE (INV-008 shape), not an unmet obligation. This is the bn-n9a1 side of the bn-n9a1-vs-bn-dw81 line (annotate when the obligation is structurally dischargeable today and the remaining gaps are absences stated inline), NOT the bn-dw81/INV-014 side (decline when the substance itself — e.g. Phase-D proof receipts — has not arrived). The honest guarantee that the isolation gap is not silently load-bearing is pinned from plan §24.5's own frontier row: autonomous promotion stays DISABLED until the Phase B G3 red-team corpus — including \"one escape attempt against each of the eight worker-isolation controls of docs/49\" — clears in full, human-approved promotion the standing fallback. The corpus is a Phase B deliverable and does not exist today; the file states this rather than overclaiming, and every gap row is a live tripwire that flips this map red when its producer lands.\n\nGATES: cargo fmt --all --check clean; clippy --workspace --all-targets --locked -D warnings clean (zero warnings); targeted 28/28 + cargo test --workspace --locked green; full `just check` exit 0 (boundaries, kernel covenant, governance ×5, dossier — status pass, program_status ready — Lean build + axiom manifest). validation-results.json regen tight (only the INV-015 row flipped active→satisfied). No .bones/ touched in-workspace.\n\nNot closing bn-3mjd per instructions."}	blake3:KSHiZd-AGF5Aj7DFzbzyUWOMPVaUbQ6nEy4M5igecz8
1785953984918385	continuum-dev	itc:v3:AWKSTzM5JJnJPkQAAAAAQar23VW6voAAAAEypAw		item.comment	bn-kh8b	{"body":"INV-007 evidence delivered: crates/continuumd/tests/inv007_omission_transparency_evidence.rs (5 tests, all green), commit 41cfe16 in-workspace (bn-kh8b). Zero src/ changes anywhere in the workspace.\n\nSHAPE OF THE BONE. INV-007's substance was not built here — it was already substantially live, per the brief. This file is mostly a facet-to-site-to-test MAP, citing the owning suites via freshness tripwires (bn-1eqt's device) rather than re-running them, plus one piece of genuinely new evidence at the one grain nothing else exercised.\n\nFACET -> SITE -> TEST MAP (full table is in the file's own module doc; summarized here)\n- closed five-member OmissionReason, schema order, unrepresentable conditionals -> continuum-context::omission -> omission::the_reason_set_is_exactly_the_schema_enum, ::every_record_declares_its_retrievability (cited)\n- kind closed to the selection vocabulary at the schema itself (F13, bn-3jrtz) -> context-pack.schema.json $defs.selection_kind -> omission::the_schema_closes_omission_kind_to_the_selection_vocabulary + mutant ::a_reopened_free_string_kind_is_caught (cited)\n- closed accounting is a CONSTRUCTOR property (candidates = selection + Sigma manifest counts), not arithmetic a caller could get wrong -> continuum-context::accounting::Accounting::close -> accounting::the_counting_equation_holds_for_every_closed_accounting, ::an_undispositioned_candidate_cannot_be_closed (cited)\n- ClosedAccounting::reconcile is an INDEPENDENT check over the two published halves -> accounting::a_shrunk_manifest_count_fails_reconciliation, ::an_inflated_manifest_count_fails_reconciliation (anti-vacuity mutants, cited)\n- expansion handles are content-derived (ID5 canonical encoding of parent+relation+anchor+depth), not ledger-minted -> continuum-context::expansion::ExpansionHandle::derive -> daemon_context_operations::the_handle_the_manifest_promised_is_the_handle_the_expansion_returns, ::one_question_is_one_pack_whatever_the_idempotency_key_says (cited)\n- a packed child is an ANSWER (ok + budget omission); BudgetExhausted only below the minimal child (bn-38p2) -> continuum-context::budget::BudgetPacker -> daemon_context_budget::an_over_budget_expansion_publishes_a_smaller_child_and_says_what_the_ceiling_cost, ::a_ceiling_below_the_minimal_child_publishes_nothing (cited)\n- measured content_budget.bytes is a least self-consistent fixed point -> continuum-context::pack::ChildPack::to_json -> pack::the_recorded_size_is_the_least_self_consistent_one (cited)\n- wire manifest agrees with the pack's own manifest record for record; no arm of context.expand answers manifest-free -> daemon::context::expand/project -> daemon_context_operations::the_envelope_manifest_agrees_with_the_packs_manifest_record_for_record, ::a_purged_anchor_expands_to_a_success_carrying_the_stub_and_the_redaction_record, ::depth_moves_items_between_the_pack_and_the_manifest_and_changes_no_total (cited)\n- context.compile is a typed refusal (UnsupportedSemanticFeature), never a manifest-free fake success -> daemon::context::ContextFamily::handle -> daemon_context_operations::context_compile_decodes_and_is_refused_with_the_typed_reason (cited)\n- MeterSet's declared-x-unmetered cell: a charge is REFUSED, not silently recorded (bn-1gc) -> continuum-task::budget -> budget::charging_an_unmetered_dimension_is_refused_rather_than_invented, ::a_declared_ceiling_with_no_meter_is_named_rather_than_silently_passed (cited)\n- the daemon's own omission list is DERIVED from the meter set, not a hand-written array (bn-23j7s deleted verification::unenforced in favor of this) -> daemon::budget::omissions_of -> pr6_impl02_budget_evidence::the_omission_manifest_is_derived_from_the_meter_set, ::a_ceiling_nothing_meters_is_recorded_and_named_on_the_answer, ::budget_exhausted_on_the_wire_is_never_a_silent_dead_end (cited)\n- a redaction is never just an error: it also names itself in omissions[] -> daemon::evidence::redact_evidence -> daemon_evidence::a_redacted_reference_reads_back_as_the_typed_stub_and_names_its_omission, ::verifying_over_a_redacted_reference_returns_the_structural_result_and_the_redaction (cited)\n- INV-016 interaction: ContextExpandRequest.anchor is closed-vocabulary equality against the pack's own advertised anchors, never parsed as prose -> daemon::context::ContextPackRecord::resolves -> inv016_untrusted_source_evidence (cited)\n- the CLI's own manifest render is non-suppressible (no --quiet-omissions; every format always carries the omissions key) -> continuum-cli::render, ::explain -> textual freshness tripwires (continuumd has no dependency edge to continuum-cli to dispatch through -- continuum-cli depends on continuumd, never the reverse, per tools/check_crate_boundaries.py)\n- the >=10x-reduction / exact-handle / accounting-refuses-undercounts acceptance criterion, over a real 200+ event durability failure -> dx01_falsification.rs (bn-37gu) -> leg2_the_pack_is_ten_times_smaller_under_the_packers_own_counting_rule, a04_the_production_accounting_refuses_every_undercount_on_this_dataset, leg3_the_promised_handle_is_the_returned_handle_and_the_expansion_is_exact, leg3b_the_budget_branch_keeps_the_promise (cited)\n- NEW HERE: the wire field itself cannot be dropped from a real answer -> wire::the_omissions_field_cannot_be_dropped_from_a_real_wire_answer\n\n38 citation rows total, each a (facet, tracked-file-path, byte-exact marker) triple, verified against the real files before writing (every marker was grepped out of the actual source, not typed from memory) and re-verified live by citations::every_citation_still_holds, with its own anti-vacuity test (a marker that cannot be present is confirmed reported missing) and a table well-formedness test. A citation going stale -- a cited test renamed, a cited file rewritten, a cited sentence reworded -- fails this file the next time it runs."}	blake3:0JEwUyPtwK5socUeZaXoP-20Blz6BAM7KuMA03HHVu4
1785953988339311	continuum-dev	itc:v3:AWKSTzM5JJnJPkQAAAAAQar23VW6voAAAAEypQw		item.comment	bn-kh8b	{"body":"bn-kh8b, part 2 of 3 (continues the delivery note above).\n\nNEW EVIDENCE (the file's one non-cited leg). wire::a_real_success_and_a_real_refusal_each_carry_a_typed_omissions_list dispatches a real context.expand success (non-empty manifest: the `far` group is still outstanding one hop beyond a depth-1 expansion, reason slice-irrelevant, recoverable_by Present) and a real malformed-anchor refusal (empty manifest, but still a real Vec, never absent) from one minimal fixture -- the compact cross-status contrast no single existing suite states in one place. wire::the_omissions_field_cannot_be_dropped_from_a_real_wire_answer is the mutant: takes that SAME real success envelope, round-trips it byte for byte as a baseline, then textually strips `\"omissions\":[...]` from its own canonical-JSON bytes (a bracket-depth-matching helper, not an assumption about what's inside the array) and asserts `from_bytes::<ResultEnvelope>` refuses with `CodecError::MissingField { declared_by: \"ResultEnvelope\", field: \"omissions\" }` -- the same single-field-drop device codec_canonical_form.rs's presence_is_three_valued_in_both_directions uses for `intent`, applied here to the field INV-007 is about, over a REAL dispatch-produced answer rather than a hand-built one. This proves the \"never absent\" half of INV-007's discipline structurally, at the wire's own boundary, independent of which operation family emitted the answer.\n\nHONEST GAPS (typed absences, not violations -- stated in the file's own module doc, per bn-n9a1's rule: an unbuilt producer cannot violate a disclosure invariant while nothing it would have disclosed exists)\n1. The ten-stage compiler is unwired -- context.compile refuses UnsupportedSemanticFeature rather than faking a compiled pack. dx01_falsification.rs (PR-11's own acceptance-criterion campaign) states its honest grain up front: replay-check/counting-rule/expansion run at production grain, candidate-set construction and stage-2 causal slicing are harness code standing in for the compiler. This is INV-008's typed-refusal territory reaching into INV-007's, not an INV-007 gap by itself.\n2. Whole-pack root assembly / store publication is declined, by name, in daemon::context's own module doc -- a pack travels on the wire and is not separately content-addressed in the reference store. The manifest still travels (INV-007's text only obligates naming the omission and how to retrieve it), so this bounds pack *storage*, not disclosure.\n3. The crashpack producer is absent (dx01's residual item 3): a pack's `replay` field names a class-checked handle with no artifact behind it. The manifest makes no claim that `replay` resolves -- a typed, honestly-unproduced field, not a place content is dropped without a record.\n4. continuum-benchmark::shell deliberately SUMMARIZES the manifest to a count plus a named retrieval command rather than inlining every record, and says so in its own module doc (\"the one place the projection is genuinely lossy,\" with the reasoning: a terminal is not a place to print a structured list nobody asked for). It still names what was omitted (the count) and how to retrieve it (the command) -- INV-007's text at a coarser grain, a documented style divergence, not a substance gap. Also worth recording: AgentView::ceiling_enforced in that same crate actually CONSUMES the manifest to answer a real falsification-harness policy question, so the manifest is load-bearing there, not decorative.\n5. The MeterSet undeclared x unmetered cell is silent, correctly -- a dimension nobody declared and nothing meters owes no omission record, because it was never in the request's scope. Recorded because it can look like a silent drop to a reader who hasn't seen the 2x2 table; it's the one cell of four that isn't a disclosure obligation at all."}	blake3:zKR_eRQSAQTGUXjiK8yxbjN-uJM6ESpg6v3bYBDf0FE
1785953991314912	continuum-dev	itc:v3:AWKSTzM5JJnJPkQAAAAAQar23VW6voAAAAEypgw		item.comment	bn-kh8b	{"body":"bn-kh8b, part 3 of 3 (continues the delivery note above).\n\nANNOTATE-VS-DECLINE (bn-n9a1's rule: annotate when the obligation is structurally dischargeable today with gaps stated as inline ABSENCES; decline when substance hasn't arrived). ANNOTATED. Reasoning: INV-007's text (\"names what was omitted and how to retrieve it... never silently drops content... a typed, disclosed fact\") is satisfied structurally and richly: the manifest is a required wire field on every answer (never absent, proven here by direct codec mutation); the closed vocabulary and closed accounting make omission a constructor property rather than a check that could be skipped; the packer's own boundary keeps the manifest reserved ahead of the selection under a shrinking budget; the MeterSet discipline extends the same property to budget dimensions outside context packs entirely; and the PR-11 acceptance-criterion campaign (dx01_falsification.rs) proves the whole chain over a real 200+ event failure. Every gap is an unbuilt-producer absence (compiler, store publication, crashpack) or a documented style choice (benchmark shell's summarization) -- none is a live code path that drops content without a typed record. This is INV-001/INV-008's shape, not INV-014's (where substance itself hadn't arrived) or bn-dw81's INV-014 non-annotation (a genuine documented deferral). A reviewer weighing the compiler's absence more heavily can strip the tag and regen -- the map states exactly where that producer would need to land and what would then need re-checking (item 1 above, echoing dx01's own residual list).\n\nREGEN / GATES. plan.md INV-007 heading annotated. `python3 notes/plan/tools/generate_traceability.py` run in-workspace: invariant category 9 active/9 satisfied -> 8 active/10 satisfied, registry 649 active -> 648 active, a one-status-flip diff (confirmed via git diff -- PLAN_REQUIREMENTS.json changes exactly the INV-007 entry's status+summary, PLAN_BONE_TRACEABILITY.md changes exactly the invariant row + the two aggregate counts). validate_dossier.py: status pass, program_status ready. validation-results.json untouched (confirmed absent from git status). No .bones/ touched. Gates from workspace root, all exit 0: cargo fmt --all --check; cargo clippy -p continuumd --all-targets --locked -- -D warnings (zero warnings); cargo test -p continuumd --test inv007_omission_transparency_evidence (5/5); cargo test --workspace --locked (full suite green, 227 \"test result: ok\" blocks, 0 failed); full `just check` (fmt, lint, workspace tests, boundaries, kernel covenant, governance x6, dossier, Lean build + empty axiom manifest) exit 0. Commit 41cfe16, in-workspace only, not merged, not pushed, not closed per instructions.\n\nCONCERNS FOR THE LEAD.\n1. The citation table is a freshness tripwire over TEXT, not a re-dispatch -- a behavior change that preserves the pinned strings (e.g. a test renamed back to something containing the same substring, or a doc-comment sentence kept verbatim while the code under it changed) would not be caught here. The owning suites remain the behavioral guards, and `just check`/`cargo test --workspace` still run all of them every time.\n2. Two CLI-layer rows (continuum-cli::render, continuum-benchmark::shell) are cited textually rather than dispatched, because continuumd has no dependency edge to either crate (they depend on continuumd, never the reverse). If a future bone wants those live-checked, the test would need to live in continuum-cli or continuum-benchmark instead, importing continuumd -- the mirror of this file's own position.\n3. The new fixture (wire module) intentionally trims bn-28jj's original near+far pack to drop the redaction/irretrievable group -- it doesn't need it, and the redaction row is already directly cited (daemon_context_operations::a_purged_anchor_expands_to_a_success_carrying_the_stub_and_the_redaction_record). Flagging in case a reviewer expected this file's own fixture to exercise all rows of the typed-outcome table rather than citing most of them.\n4. Item 1 in the gaps list (compiler absence) is the one place this map and INV-008's map overlap; I read it as INV-008's territory containing INV-007's obligation for that specific facet (a typed refusal instead of a fake success), not as this bone needing to re-litigate INV-008. Recorded per the brief's \"adjudicate and record reasoning\" instruction in case a reviewer draws the line differently.\n\nClaims to be released after this comment. Not closing bn-kh8b per instructions."}	blake3:-H3KPW8SOlMH-M-TNENfSCGLKQPmbUXXw65ZPY3z2GE
1785954109815618	continuum-dev	itc:v3:AWKSTzM5JJnJPkQAAAAAQar23VW6voAAAAEypww		item.comment	bn-kh8b	{"body":"Lead: merged @ epoch f525cd9d6983. INV-007 ANNOTATED (delivered) — substance richly live from PR-11 (bn-28jj closed accounting, bn-38p2 packer, bn-3jrtz schema closure) and PR-6 (bn-1gc/bn-23j7s MeterSet), correctly cited-not-rebuilt via 38 byte-exact freshness-pinned citations (the bn-1eqt device, right choice since continuumd can't dispatch through to continuum-cli/benchmark — dependency runs the other way). The one genuinely new structural check is the best part: stripping omissions[] from a REAL Daemon::dispatch answer's own encoded bytes refuses to decode (CodecError::MissingField), proving wire-level non-droppability structurally rather than per-family. Four honest typed-absence gaps (unwired compiler, declined whole-pack publication, absent crashpack producer, benchmark shell summarization). §2 sweep now: 001/002/003/005/006/007/008/009/012/016 delivered (INV-015 in flight). Closing."}	blake3:frif_ccykP4XcmlqCk2a8lwtw8fTIPRpEJL6mEHL2uA
