1786291735864955	continuum-dev	itc:v3:AWKSTzM5JJnJPkQAAAAAQar23VW6voAAAAEyuAw		item.comment	bn-3l5la	{"body":"RFC flag bookkeeping complete. Workspace bn-3l5la, commit 0552dce, gate green (`maw exec bn-3l5la -- just check` full pipeline: fmt, clippy, tests, boundaries, governance, dossier validator \"status\": \"pass\" with spec_debt.open == [], `just lean` — 19/19 modules built, axiom manifest up to date).\n\nVERIFICATION METHOD: read bn-1lfek's actual landed commit (92a064c, the one reachable from HEAD — note eb6fe75/eece8b8 with the same bone id are an abandoned earlier attempt NOT on main, confirmed via `git merge-base --is-ancestor`) plus its full diff against every schema in notes/plan/schemas/, and cross-checked each flag's claimed payment against the concrete schema JSON before writing any annotation. This covered every flag in the acceptance list, well beyond the requested 2-3 spot-check minimum.\n\nMARKED PAID (phrase \"paid by the bn-1lfek schema sweep, 2026-07-31\" used verbatim, entries kept in place):\n- RFC 0028: F1 (`parent` lineage field), F3 (`compiler` block), F4 (`content_budget` required + `tokenizer_id` conditional requirement).\n- RFC 0031: F1 (`intent_changes[].unit`), F2 (`requested_assurance` closed 5-member enum), F3 (`classifier` block).\n- RFC 0032: F8 (`coverage` typed into 7 named groups), F9 (`reuse_provenance`), plus correction 10 (`promotion-receipt.example.json`'s `intent_diff`/`semantic_diff` now name the same `diff_demo1` identity).\n- RFC 0037: F4 (per-field policy-verb enums), F5 (`scope.fragments` minItems:1), F10 (registry `supersedes`/`superseded_by`), F11 (lowercase `unknown` in prose).\n\nPARTIAL / DEFERRED (as instructed):\n- RFC 0031 F4: annotated deferred. Schema-side half paid via `intent_changes[].unit` (unit identity no longer lives only in reason-string prose); the rest — typing the reason strings themselves — stays open because it needs a closed per-field reason vocabulary RFC 0031 hasn't minted.\n- RFC 0037 F3: only the schema half marked paid (`policy_reviewers` keys restricted to the fifteen policy keys via `propertyNames`, empty principal lists rejected via `minItems:1`). The other half — tying every `review`-verb field to a non-empty reviewer list — left open; it's a cross-object relation JSON Schema can't state and remains a checker rule.\n\nREQUIRED-PROPERTY COUNT: verified against `notes/plan/schemas/context-pack.schema.json`'s actual `required` array (17 entries after `content_budget` was added). RFC 0028's \"sixteen required properties\" sentence (the \"Required fields, reconciled with plan §6.2\" section) and the identical restatement in correction 7 were both corrected to \"seventeen\", `content_budget` added to the enumerated list, and moved out of the \"optional or conditional\" list (now three: `debugger_branch`, `redactions`, `inconclusive_reason`).\n\nLEFT UNTOUCHED, AS INSTRUCTED: RFC 0037 F1/F2/F6/F7/F8/F9 and RFC 0032 F1/F2/F3/F4/F5/F6 — confirmed still open/deferred in the live text, no edits made.\n\nDISCREPANCIES FOUND (neither marked paid nor left silently open — flagging here per the spot-check instruction):\n1. RFC 0028 F5 and F12 were EXCLUDED from my edits even though the acceptance list names them. Both already carry a \"— **PAID**\" annotation on trunk, added later by bn-3jrtz (protocol-3.4 bundle, commit a71c3cf, Aug 5 — after bn-1lfek's Jul 31 payment, and itself already closed/done). That existing text already attributes the payment to bn-1lfek in substance (e.g. F5: \"PAID (correction 2, bn-1lfek): ... recorded here at the 3.4 sweep (bn-3jrtz), which found the payment made but unmarked\"), just not in this bone's exact phrase. Re-annotating over another closed bone's settled bookkeeping risked a confusing double/conflicting record, so I left both as-is rather than edit them. Functionally the bookkeeping this bone exists to close is already done for F5/F12; only the phrasing differs from bn-3l5la's convention.\n2. `notes/plan/docs/41_REPAIR_TRANSACTIONS.md` (already edited by bn-1lfek, out of this bone's scope — I did not touch it) describes the RFC 0032 F8 `coverage` schema as a \"closed six-group object,\" but the live schema (`promotion-receipt.schema.json`) actually has seven groups (`replay`, `neighborhood`, `property_mutation`, `defect_mutants`, `refinement_coverage`, `certificate_rebuild`, `incremental_parity` — counted directly from the `properties` object). I did not use \"six\" anywhere in my RFC 0032 F8 annotation to avoid propagating the miscount; worth a follow-up bone if docs/41's number should be fixed.\n\nFiles touched (all in .maw/workspaces/bn-3l5la/): notes/plan/rfcs/0028-context-pack-format.md, notes/plan/rfcs/0031-semantic-and-intent-diff.md, notes/plan/rfcs/0032-repair-transaction-protocol.md, notes/plan/rfcs/0037-intent-contract.md. No CAUTION-flagged nested parentheses were introduced inside any paren annotation."}	blake3:f9oAbI8dw2rq4CBmu08_85BCWzDE3GFscHm8ydoPxzk
1786291778386431	continuum-dev	itc:v3:AWKSTzM5JJnJPkQAAAAAQar23VW6voAAAAEyuQw		item.comment	bn-3l5la	{"body":"Lead ratification: merged @ 7fb19eaec28a (workspace destroyed, snapshot retained). Review: diff exactly the four RFC files; 13 flags marked paid with the canonical phrasing, F3-schema-half/F4-deferred handled per spec, sixteen→seventeen count fixed against the live schema required array, deferred flags untouched. Both discrepancy calls accepted — leaving bn-3jrtz's settled F5/F12 record alone was right, and not repeating docs/41's six-vs-seven-group miscount was right; docs/41 count noted as possible future hygiene. Closing."}	blake3:D_cC6TgaxzJd5MoT-Zf9FK3AGYRsAUXXMbO11zhX1q0
