1786292623639021	continuum-dev	itc:v3:AWKSTzM5JJnJPkQAAAAAQar23VW6voAAAAEyzQw		item.comment	bn-2uh80	{"body":"bn-2uh80 (1/2) — ROWS ADDED. docs/31 residual thresholds merged into plan §24.5. Workspace bn-2uh80, commits 8ecd6d9 + 0fd02de (rebased onto epoch c6d6cd2), NOT merged/pushed.\n\nWHERE THE ROWS WENT. All four are APPENDED at the end of the §24.5 table, deliberately: notes/plan/tools/traceability.py numbers frontier requirements FR-NN by table ordinal, so inserting mid-table would have renamed FR-01..FR-21 and broken requirement identity. Appending kept every existing FR key and left the INV-015 evidence test's pins on the workbench-security row untouched.\n\nFR-22 \"Higher-dimensional / cubical reduction (INV-013, C015)\". Lane research/01, research/10; docs/31; docs/07 §7. Baseline: the optimal-DPOR and unfolding exploration of RFC 0004 on the same high-width workload, never raw interleaving — docs/31's own hypothesis is that cells beat *optimal* DPOR, and C015 grades on a preregistered benchmark. Promote: >=3x memory or time on at least two real protocol classes, with a preservation theorem for the property class, and no regression worse than 25% on dependent workloads. Kill: only synthetic grid benchmarks win, or counterexample explanations worsen materially. Fallback: conservative unreduced exploration; the cubical engine stays separately named, benchmarked and assurance-capped per ADR-0020. Status: DRAFT.\n\nFR-23 \"Semiring-valued analysis (§9, C034)\". Lane research/19; ADR-0030; docs/31. Baseline: each analysis's specialized hand-written traversal, on both code complexity and performance, per research/19's experiment and C034's \"specialized-baseline equivalence\". Promote: at least three production analyses share one generic acyclic dynamic-programming kernel, each within 15% of its specialized baseline. Kill: the algebra obscures numerical or game semantics, or introduces hot-path abstraction cost; also a kill — not a narrower promotion — if a result needs probability treated as an ordinary commutative semiring where nondeterminism or a scheduler adversary requires MDP or stochastic-game semantics, per research/19's probability warning and ADR-0030. Fallback: specialized per-analysis traversals with no shared algebra; results still state their algebra and conditions per ADR-0030. Status: DRAFT.\n\nFR-24 \"Assumption synthesis games (§14.3, C028)\". Lane research/15; docs/31. Baseline: the hand-written minimal assumptions C028 names, on the §7.2 liveness corpus subset. Promote: weaker, deployable assumptions or repairs on at least five liveness cases, with \"deployable\" bound to research/15's operational assumption type — all four interpretations present: logical formula, simulator adversary restriction, production monitor or SLO, and deployment mechanism or human procedure — so an assumption with no operational interpretation does not count toward the five; \"weaker\" is Pareto-minimality in research/15's assumption-strength lattice. The five are counted on synthesis output only, because research/15 ships counterstrategies first. Kill: grammars require hand-encoding the answer, or synthesized assumptions are operationally meaningless; also kill on parity/Streett state explosion, from research/15's risk list. Fallback: counterstrategies only; fairness assumptions stay hand-written and reviewer-approved, declared as assumptions rather than synthesized results. Status: DRAFT.\n\nFR-25 \"Automatic abstraction discovery (§14.4, §16)\". Lane research/24; docs/31; docs/07 §7. Baseline: human-authored abstraction variables and refinement maps, on total human PLUS compute cost over the same projects. Promote: proposed views and refinement maps survive independent checking and reduce that total cost on multiple projects, where \"independent checking\" is research/24's anti-overfitting set spelled out in full — held-out schedules and faults, semantic mutants, neighboring causal classes, stronger bounds, differential reference execution, and a simulation proof or a clearly bounded evidence class, with \"agreement on a finite trace set is not refinement\" carried over. Kill AS AN ASSURANCE FEATURE: results require manual semantic repair, in which case the capability is retained suggestion-only, promoted only with a receipt, and no assurance claim may depend on it. Fallback: suggestion-only proposals with a human-reviewed semantic diff and no assurance claim. Status: DRAFT AND QUALITATIVE IN EVERY SOURCE — the row says so in capitals, states that no number exists in docs/31, docs/07 §7, or research/24, and states that the register does not invent one on the lane's behalf.\n\nWHAT STAYED DRAFT. All four rows. None carries a quote-id marker, so the dossier's quote-identity check still sees exactly the 6 pre-existing ratified quotes (register_rows: rows 21 -> 25, ratified_quotes_checked 6 -> 6) and traceability.py classifies all four as status=active, never satisfied. Nothing was quantified or promoted on a lane owner's behalf, and no research note was edited."}	blake3:Lo9d4HK7-5M0AgOVeUteMRywWAM6NaXcZsKIXH3l9Gk
1786292652510877	continuum-dev	itc:v3:AWKSTzM5JJnJPkQAAAAAQar23VW6voAAAAEyzgw		item.comment	bn-2uh80	{"body":"bn-2uh80 (2/2) — RECONCILIATIONS, SIDE-WORK, GATE.\n\nRECONCILED DISAGREEMENTS, AND WHO WON.\n1. Cubical magnitude and corpus — docs/31 (\">=3x memory/time on at least two real protocol classes with a preservation theorem\") vs docs/07 §7 (\">=2x memory or representative reduction on 3/5 target benchmarks without regressions >25% elsewhere\"). DOCS/31 WINS on magnitude and on requiring the theorem: a reduction with no preservation proof cannot carry a property-scoped assurance claim (INV-013), and docs/07 omits the theorem entirely. DOCS/07'S NON-REGRESSION CLAUSE IS KEPT as an added conjunct, because it is a real falsifier docs/31 lacks. The residual \"two real protocol classes\" vs \"3 of 5 target benchmarks\" denominator split is named in the row as exactly what research/01 must settle at ratification — not silently picked.\n2. Cubical >=3x vs the existing exploration-reduction row's >=10x (FR-02, research/01) — NEITHER WINS. The row states they measure different things and neither absorbs the other: >=10x is the lane-level bar for property-scoped reduction against unreduced exploration; >=3x is a representation-level bar against an already-reduced DPOR/unfolding baseline. Without saying so the register would have read as self-contradicting.\n3. Semiring analysis count — docs/31 counts \"three production analyses\"; research/19 ENUMERATES FOUR kernels (reachability, shortest causal witness, equivalence-class-representative counting, minimal fault-set provenance) and ADR-0030 names five algebras. THE NOTE WINS ON SCOPE (a bare count names nothing measurable); DOCS/31 WINS ON THE NUMBER, read as a FLOOR over the note's enumeration rather than a cap. No kernel was dropped to make the count agree.\n4. Semiring margin — research/19 states only the qualitative \"promote only if the abstraction pays rent\". DOCS/31'S 15% WINS as the lane's only number; the row records that research/19 must fix the margin, the workload, and the code-complexity metric at ratification.\n5. Abstraction-discovery cost denominator — docs/31 says \"reduce human work\"; docs/07 §7 says \"total human+compute cost\". DOCS/07 WINS: a map that halves human effort while multiplying checking compute has not reduced cost. Docs/31's \"survive independent checking\" gate survives and is bound to research/24's anti-overfitting set.\n6. The reconciliation rule itself — §24.5 previously said \"where docs/31 and a research note disagree, the note is corrected and cited\", which reads as \"docs/31 always wins\" and would have forced case 3 to delete a kernel. The closing prose now states the rule precisely: it is about WHO HOLDS THE NUMBER — docs/31's quantity beats a note's silence or qualitative phrasing, and the note is corrected at ratification — and NOT about scope, where a note that enumerates what docs/31 merely counts is what the row cites. The same reading is extended to docs/07 §7, which is not a research note: the stricter bar wins and the clause the other document uniquely contributes is kept.\n\nSIDE-WORK THE GATE REQUIRED. Four new ACTIVE frontier requirements are uncovered and unwired by construction: traceability reported `uncovered=4, frontier_wiring_failures=1` until each row got a ratification task. Created, shaped exactly like the existing bn-3dg5b / bn-187wu / bn-k7s1i / bn-307pv ratification tasks — size s, leaf task, parent bn-2z3, labels req:fr-NN + req:phase-X + phase-x + plan-key:frontier-fr-NN + research:\n- bn-1w6fn — FR-22, phase-d, Phase B barrier (bn-3zt), blocks bn-twd9 (C015).\n- bn-1vaok — FR-23, phase-f, Phase D barrier (bn-1db), blocks bn-3ldj (C034).\n- bn-2wdhb — FR-24, phase-d, Phase B barrier (bn-3zt), blocks bn-3vo7 (C028).\n- bn-ycyi2 — FR-25, phase-e, Phase C barrier (bn-1fd), blocks bn-kg2 (Forge abstraction synthesis with finite-bound overfit guards).\nnotes/plan/tools/groom_execution_graph.py's lane_specs gained the four matching entries, so a future run of the authoring script is a no-op for them rather than a re-create. The script itself was NOT run — it does far more than this bone needs and its fixed point may have drifted.\n\nSOURCE POINTERS ADDED. docs/31 gained a closing \"Where lane status is decided\" section — appended at the end of the file specifically so R14_ALIEN_MATH_THEATER_EVIDENCE.md's `docs/31:14-25` line citation still resolves — and docs/07 §7 gained a paragraph after its table. Both say plan §24.5 is the lane authority and both name the reconciliations above. That is the \"ONE lane authority\" half of the bone.\n\nGATE. `maw exec bn-2uh80 -- just check` exit 0, run in full three times: before a prose rewrap, after it, and again after the rebase onto epoch c6d6cd2. Dossier: status pass, program_status ready, register_rows {rows: 25, ratified_quotes_checked: 6}. Traceability regenerated in-workspace; registry diff is 4 new FR entries plus line-number shifts for the §25-derived requirements, with FR-01..FR-21 keys, summaries, and metadata unchanged. Lean T0/T1 green, axiom manifest empty.\n\nFOR THE LEAD. (a) The rebase onto the newer epoch produced two conflicts: `.bones/events/2026-08.events` (resolved union — append-only and replay-order-independent per .bones/.gitattributes) and PLAN_BONE_TRACEABILITY.md (took epoch, then regenerated). Both re-verified by a full green gate afterwards. (b) The workspace commit includes 12 `.bones/events` lines — the four item.create events and their eight blocking links. The same events are in the trunk working copy from `bn create`; union merge dedupes. (c) Not merged, not pushed, bone not closed, workspace not destroyed."}	blake3:cFbdvt_gYTglK3PxFVqc4075HDfn-Z080feONKNQk34
1786292743112841	continuum-dev	itc:v3:AWKSTzM5JJnJPkQAAAAAQar23VW6voAAAAEyzww		item.comment	bn-2uh80	{"body":"Lead ratification: merged @ c0c60f8f5bc4 (workspace destroyed, snapshot retained). Review: four DRAFT rows FR-22..FR-25 appended — appending rather than inserting was exactly right, ordinal FR numbering makes a mid-table insert an identity-breaking change; INV-015's workbench-security pins untouched; docs/31 pointer appended end-of-file preserving R14's line citation. All six reconciliations accepted, notably scoping §24.5's note-correction rule so docs/31 holds numbers while research notes hold scope, and refusing to arbitrate FR-22-vs-FR-02 magnitudes that measure different things. Carrier bones bn-1w6fn/bn-1vaok/bn-2wdhb/bn-ycyi2 verified well-formed with lane_specs entries. Closing."}	blake3:rX2KiWZoJVsUD9RmjwguWC2-C7puzqO22d5U20yvXXE
