1786293334763959	continuum-dev	itc:v3:AWKSTzM5JJnJPkQAAAAAQar23VW6voAAAAEy2gw		item.create	bn-21vno	{"description":"Child 1 of bn-8g9uj (RFC 0028 ten-stage Context Pack compiler). Scope: the pipeline spine plus the earliest stage group — the redaction pre-pass, stage 1 (root selection), stage 2 (backward causal slicing).\n\nWhat this bone owns:\n\n- **The auditable-intermediate discipline.** \"Each stage MUST produce an auditable intermediate, and the intermediates MUST be retrievable for the parity audit's context-slice comparison (RFC 0030, compared artifact 5)\" — RFC 0028, \"Compiler pipeline\". A typed `Stage` vocabulary declared with all ten members (the crate's own `SelectionKind`/`ExpansionRelation` precedent: an enum missing members of a closed vocabulary cannot round-trip a conforming instance), a content-identified intermediate, and a gap-free ordered trail, so the later stage groups append to a spine rather than each inventing one.\n- **The closed thirteen-member guarantee vocabulary**, plus rule C1 (requested is not achieved): a guarantee is claimable only through a license the stage's own check produced, never by echoing a request. Rule C2 (`ReplayPreserving` implies `CausallyClosed` and a non-null `replay`) is stated here because stage 2 is where its precondition is licensed.\n- **The redaction pre-pass.** RFC 0028 correction 12 — \"Redaction precedes root selection, not merely slicing\": policy is applied before stage 1, a redacted root is refused rather than sliced from (\"a redacted root is not a root and slicing from one leaks the shape of what it dropped\"), and a redacted causal predecessor is accounted as an irretrievable `redaction` omission, not silently included and not silently dropped.\n- **Stage 1, root selection**, whose licence is exactly nothing: \"a bad root is a wrong pack, not an unsound one\".\n- **Stage 2, backward causal slicing**, licensing `CausallyClosed` and the precondition of `ReplayPreserving`. The causal order must be engine-independent: `continuum-context` may not import an engine (`tools/check_crate_boundaries.py`) and `continuum-cir` is a documented stub, so the input is a typed causal order this crate owns. The downward-closure check MUST be written independently of the slicer — RFC 0028 \"Validation\": \"the checkers are independent of the compiler that made the claim — INV-004's discipline applied here\".\n- Every disposition lands through `crate::accounting`, so INV-007's counting equation (\"candidate set = selection + Sum of manifest counts\") holds by construction rather than by a check somebody must remember to run.\n\nDeterminism: INV-005 — no clock, no entropy, no float, `BTree`-ordered everything. Tests must be positive, negative, and boundary, with mutants that the checks actually reject: a slice missing a causal predecessor, a redacted root, a cyclic \"causal order\", a root that is not a candidate, an empty slice.\n\nDeclined here and named rather than implied: stages 3-8 (their own children), stage 9 (RFC 0028 blesses \"plain causal slice + expansion, stage 9 disabled\" as a supported configuration and the register row's named fallback), stage 10 (`continuum-context::budget::BudgetPacker` is it in substance), whole-pack root assembly and `context.compile` wiring (the last child).","kind":"task","labels":["implementation","req:pr-11"],"parent":"bn-8g9uj","size":"m","title":"Context Pack compiler stages 1-2: pipeline spine, auditable intermediates, redaction pre-pass, root selection, backward causal slicing"}	blake3:R6HHVOmSfUdvysvbzo7jH8owlOfOkT4rmTLMjLTgAKk
1786293356591649	continuum-dev	itc:v3:AWKSTzM5JJnJPkQAAAAAQar23VW6voAAAAEy2ww		item.create	bn-1kj2n	{"description":"Child 2 of bn-8g9uj (RFC 0028 ten-stage Context Pack compiler), appended to child 1's stage spine. Depends on bn-21vno.\n\n- **Stage 3, property-automaton relevance filtering.** Input: the property automaton. Licenses `PropertyPreserving`, with stage 2. RFC 0028 \"Validation\" is decisive about the checker: \"An independent property monitor on `PropertyPreserving` — an implementation that reuses the compiler's own automaton has checked nothing.\" So the monitor that licenses the guarantee MUST NOT be the filter that produced the slice, and a test must show the monitor can disagree (a filter mutant whose slice the monitor rejects).\n- **Stage 4, static/dynamic dependence join.** Input: source correspondence. Licenses the *admissibility* of `source` and `model` items — not a guarantee of its own. INV-016 governs: \"Source is untrusted data and MUST NOT be interpolated into any description\"; `crate::source::SourceRef` and `crate::model::ModelActionRef` are the landed typed constructors and are the only way an item of those kinds may be built.\n- Each stage appends its auditable intermediate to child 1's trail (RFC 0030 compared artifact 5), and every candidate a stage drops is dispositioned through `crate::accounting`, so the counting equation stays closed across the whole pipeline rather than only within one stage.\n\nBoundary and negative cases this bone owes:\n- A slice containing no automaton-observed event at all — `PropertyPreserving` is not claimed, and the reason is typed.\n- **An abstraction-relevant hidden event.** RFC 0028, \"Selection and the causal core\": \"A compiler MUST NOT exclude an abstraction-relevant hidden event on the grounds that no observer publishes it: INV-013 scopes reduction to named observers and properties, and an event the abstraction depends on is in scope for the property.\" A stage-3 filter that drops one must be rejected by the monitor.\n- An item dropped because the compiler could not decide is `heuristic-cutoff`, never `slice-irrelevant` (RFC 0028, \"Omission manifest\") — the two reasons are distinguishable here for the first time and the distinction must be tested.\n\nDeterminism: INV-005 throughout, as child 1.","kind":"task","labels":["implementation","req:pr-11"],"parent":"bn-8g9uj","size":"m","title":"Context Pack compiler stages 3-4: property-automaton relevance filtering (PropertyPreserving) and static/dynamic dependence join"}	blake3:Smwwt7iA255GXITRnrBFliFt0wlybv3vdqU9twMu1MU
1786293370280578	continuum-dev	itc:v3:AWKSTzM5JJnJPkQAAAAAQar23VW6voAAAAEy3Aw		item.create	bn-imhw2	{"description":"Child 3 of bn-8g9uj (RFC 0028 ten-stage Context Pack compiler). Depends on bn-1kj2n.\n\n- **Stage 5, proof-dependency slicing** over the named obligations. Licenses `ProofRelevant`. Checker: the proof-slice check (RFC 0035, RFC 0012); failure mode: \"an item off the slice is a false relevance claim\". The proof-target pack profile (RFC 0028, \"Pack profiles\") \"MUST claim `ProofRelevant` or state why it cannot\" — the second branch is this bone's real work, since no proof service is landed.\n- **Stage 6, observer projection** over the intent's observers. Licenses scoping under INV-013 and, in RFC 0028's own words, \"never a guarantee by itself\" — a test must pin that stage 6 alone licenses nothing.\n- **Stage 7, abstraction/refinement correspondence mapping** over the plan section 16 correspondence graph. Licenses the concrete-to-abstract links selected items carry.\n\nThe load-bearing discipline of this group: **a stage whose input does not exist in this workspace refuses rather than degrades.** There is no landed proof-service artifact and no section 16 correspondence graph. RFC 0026 `rule errors.unsupported_surface` — an operation \"registered ahead of its producing subsystem MUST fail with the typed `UnsupportedSemanticFeature` rather than degrading, guessing, or returning an empty success\" — and INV-008's typed inconclusiveness together mean the stage MUST record a typed `unsupported` omission (and, where the absence makes the answer unusable, `verdict: inconclusive` with one of the six `InconclusiveReason` tokens per rule C1) and MUST NOT license its guarantee. That refusal, and its anti-vacuity mutant (a stage that quietly licenses `ProofRelevant` with no proof slice behind it), are the most important tests this bone owes.\n\nAlso here: `AbstractionAmbiguity` and `IncompleteProofSearch` get their first real producers, and the invariant/proof-target profiles' verdict rules (RFC 0028: such a pack \"MUST NOT default to `satisfied`\") become checkable.\n\nDeterminism: INV-005 throughout. Intermediates append to the child-1 trail; accounting stays closed.","kind":"task","labels":["implementation","req:pr-11"],"parent":"bn-8g9uj","size":"m","title":"Context Pack compiler stages 5-7: proof-dependency slicing (ProofRelevant), observer projection (INV-013), abstraction/refinement correspondence mapping"}	blake3:oGTWLsF9jegtq7Ui1psC2kXGTWZ0o7z1IKZp6tovxJM
1786293384320252	continuum-dev	itc:v3:AWKSTzM5JJnJPkQAAAAAQar23VW6voAAAAEy3Qw		item.create	bn-3ub6i	{"description":"Child 4 of bn-8g9uj (RFC 0028 ten-stage Context Pack compiler). Depends on bn-imhw2.\n\nStage 8 — \"minimal unsatisfied core / correction-set analysis\", input \"a solver artifact, where one exists\", licensing \"the minimality classes, each with its own transcript\".\n\n- The six transcript-checkable classes — `OneMinimal` (single-item removal transcript), `CardinalityMinimal` (exhaustive smaller-set search transcript within declared bounds), `CausallyMinimal`, `ValueMinimal`, `OwnerMinimal`, `FaultMinimal` — each licensed **only by its own transcript**. RFC 0028 rule C3: \"Minimality classes are independent claims. A pack MUST claim exactly the classes whose checks ran and passed, and a consumer MUST NOT infer one class from another on the wire.\" A test must show that running the one-removal check does not license any other class.\n- **`ExplanationMinimal` is not emittable here.** RFC 0028 correction 5: it \"requires the docs/48 preregistered study (plan section 21.1, G8) and MUST NOT be emitted from a minimizer transcript\". The refusal must be pinned by a test, since the type system will happily let a thirteenth member be claimed beside the twelve.\n- **`CardinalityMinimal` requires declared bounds** — \"an unbounded search cannot claim it\". A transcript with no bound declaration does not license the class.\n- RFC 0028's guarantee-violation mutant list names this stage's own: \"a minimality class with no transcript\" MUST be rejected. Add the neighbouring ones the stage can produce: a survivable single-item removal refuting `OneMinimal`, and a removal-minimized slice that is no longer downward closed (which would also break child 1's `CausallyClosed` — RFC 0028's Lean obligation 2, \"minimality soundness\", is the model-side statement of exactly this).\n- Rendering rule, enforced at the same place: \"`minimal` without a class is prohibited output in every rendering\" (rule C3, plan section 6.4).\n\nDeterminism: INV-005 throughout — the removal search order is declared, not discovered. Intermediates append to the child-1 trail; accounting stays closed.","kind":"task","labels":["implementation","req:pr-11"],"parent":"bn-8g9uj","size":"m","title":"Context Pack compiler stage 8: minimal unsatisfied core / correction-set analysis and the per-class minimality transcripts"}	blake3:oOXZ7gyd-5X7fsHPby3L7wR2UZREbSQkSqio_e0OXQg
1786293402903020	continuum-dev	itc:v3:AWKSTzM5JJnJPkQAAAAAQar23VW6voAAAAEy3gw		item.create	bn-1y4qc	{"description":"Child 5 of bn-8g9uj — the LAST child and the stage-group exit. Depends on bn-3ub6i.\n\nThree things land together, and they must land together:\n\n**1. Production root pack assembly.** The seventeen required properties of `context-pack.schema.json` written as one root document, with the four profiles' content constraints (failure, reachability, invariant, proof-target) and the deterministic ordering of the six list-valued fields (`rule ordering.deterministic`). This settles the decision `daemon::context` deliberately declined: \"A store handle is the content identity of the bytes (`ContentIdentifier::identify`), and a pack's `context_id` is the identity of its *question* — two spellings for one artifact unless something reconciles them, and reconciling them is a decision about pack assembly rather than about expansion ... leaves the store question to the bone that owns pack assembly.\" `crates/continuumd/tests/dx01_falsification.rs::assemble_root_pack` is the harness form being replaced.\n\n**2. `context.compile` wired through `daemon::context`.** That module says so itself: \"When the compiler lands it will write through the same surface, and nothing in this file changes.\" The `(\"context.compile\", ErrorCode::UnsupportedSemanticFeature)` entry in `daemon::context::FAULTS` and its refusal arm come out. The IDL binds the response: `context.compile` is `@mutation @task_starting` with `authority read` and verdict `EvaluationVerdictValue`; \"that verdict MUST equal the pack's `verdict`, and its `assurance_class` MUST equal the pack's `assurance.class`\" (RFC 0028, \"Wire surface\"). `Audience` selects rendering, never content: two requests differing only in `audience` MUST produce the same `ctx_*`.\n\n**3. G0-DX-01 re-run at production grain — and the exit guard that flips red by design.**\n\n`crates/continuumd/tests/pr11_exit_evidence.rs` pins `context.compile`'s refusal **LIVE**: \"Grain guard, live: `context.compile` dispatched against a real daemon, refused `UnsupportedSemanticFeature` with no payload — pinned so a landed compiler turns this exit layer red and forces the re-run at production grain\" (bn-3m65). **Landing the wiring in item 2 turns that test red.** That is the intended falsification trip-wire, not a regression: the PR-11 exit closed at *declared* grains with the compiler named as its owed producer, and the guard exists so the close cannot quietly outlive its grain.\n\nSo this bone MUST, in the same change: re-run G0-DX-01's experiment at production grain (the compiler as producer, not `causal_core`/`assemble_root_pack` harness code), update the exit artifact's grain declarations from \"harness\" to \"production\" with the compiler no longer named as missing, and re-bless `tests/golden/pr11_exit_evidence.txt` and `tests/golden/dx01_falsification_evidence.txt`. It MUST NOT weaken the guard: the exit closure that *rejects* an artifact for hiding its grain or for un-naming its missing producer stays exactly as it is — only the grain being declared changes. Every leg stays re-derived from the artifact's bytes (ratio recomputed from byte counts and graded at the row's 10x, witness-equals-core, INV-007 conservation, the expansion promise), and the eight doctored-artifact rejections stay live.\n\nAlso owed: the G0-DX-01 matrix row's Decision cell and the START_HERE PR-11 Exit annotation are updated to the production grain, and traceability is regenerated.","kind":"task","labels":["implementation","req:pr-11"],"parent":"bn-8g9uj","size":"m","title":"context.compile daemon wiring + production root pack assembly + G0-DX-01 re-run at production grain (PR-11 exit re-close)"}	blake3:yOqyJvqpHzPKa6eXJ4R5hzGbJizwbt8KhTJPjWWUVV4
