1786296813047263	continuum-dev	itc:v3:AWKSTzM5JJnJPkQAAAAAQar23VW6voAAAAEy_Aw		item.create	bn-1as8e	{"description":"Successor carrier for PHASE-A-DEL-04 after bn-2qa0u landed the whiteboard note format and the compiler as a crate-level surface.\n\nWhat bn-2qa0u delivered: notes/plan/schemas/whiteboard-note.schema.json (new normative schema, wired into validate_dossier.py SCHEMA_PAIRS + EXTERNAL_SCHEMA_PAIRS), RFC 0038 W1-W9 recording every plan §11.5 prose-to-schema decision, and crates/continuum-evidence/src/whiteboard.rs — note -> typed graph proposals (6 of 7 sections to node kinds, Experiment to a TaskProposal), the docs/44 six compilation rules each met by the shape of the format rather than a check, SUPPORTS as the only emitted edge kind, whole-note refusal. Explicitly NO wire operation.\n\nRemaining, with the reasoning:\n\n(1) The whiteboard WIRE surface. There is still no declared operation and no EvidenceQuery field. Registering one moves the IDL, plan §10.2 and RFC 0027's authority table together under rule conformance.registry_agreement and raises the protocol minor 3.4 -> 3.5 (rule versioning.compatible_change). RFC 0038's 'Not decided here: the wire' paragraph states the deferral. Open sub-questions a wire slice must answer: does compilation happen daemon-side (the daemon holds the graph the references resolve against) or client-side with only the resulting proposals crossing; and whether the note crosses as an Opaque naming whiteboard-note.schema.json or as a declared struct.\n\n(2) The reverse direction — docs/44's 'human-friendly whiteboard view': rendering evidence-graph state back into a note. bn-2qa0u's compiler is deliberately one-way (plan §11.5 and RFC 0038 both say note -> proposals). The view has no schema, no surface, and no decided semantics for which held nodes belong in which section.\n\n(3) The seven RFC 0038 'Queries' forms: missing obligations, conflicting candidates, proof frontier, repair frontier, semantic duplicates, provenance, task generation. crates/continuum-evidence/src/graph.rs ships the selection-and-traversal layer these are written in, plus EvidenceGraph::contradictions ('conflicting candidates'), and names the other six as not-delivered because they need artifact content the graph does not hold — a proof frontier needs proof obligations, semantic duplicates need semantic equality. They also have no wire representation. Inventing them over handles alone is the empty-success shape rule errors.unsupported_surface forbids. Any slice here should start by deciding whether these are wire operations at all or library queries over content a later PR supplies. Note that bn-2qa0u's TaskProposal is a partial down-payment on 'task generation': experiments become task proposals, but the graph-driven task generation of docs/44 ('close missing proof edge', 'find counterexample to candidate', ...) is untouched.\n\nScope from RFC 0038 + the IDL + plan §11.5 + docs/44. May split at pickup. Do NOT annotate PHASE-A-DEL-04 as delivered from this bone alone.","kind":"task","title":"Evidence graph remaining surface: whiteboard wire verb + view, the seven RFC 0038 semantic queries"}	blake3:X8xpKKNfJzahnZis7tddBRtNHfsCQUls4ANb7Edw_Xc
