1786296835199313	continuum-dev	itc:v3:AWKSTzM5JJnJPkQAAAAAQar23VW6voAAAAEy_ww		item.create	bn-sk44r	{"description":"Pre-existing, reproducible on main at affa890 with a clean tree — NOT introduced by any workspace.\n\n    python3 tools/governance/check_dependency_audit.py   # status: fail, 6 violations\n\nCargo.lock resolves blake3 1.8.6, cc 1.4.2, find-msvc-tools 0.1.10; tools/governance/dependency-audits.toml records 1.8.5, 1.4.0, 0.1.9. The checker fires two rules per crate: every-external-dependency-is-audited (the resolved version has no audit entry) and no-stale-entries (the recorded version is no longer resolved). check_t12_evidence.py fails through the same delegate ('cargo-vet/advisory scanning'), so 'just check' stops at the governance recipe for every worker.\n\nTwo candidate fixes, and they are NOT equivalent — this needs a decision, which is why it is a bone and not a drive-by:\n\n(a) the lockfile drifted by accident (a  without --locked) and should be restored to the audited versions; or\n(b) the bump is wanted, and the three crates need a real vet recorded in dependency-audits.toml with who/criteria/notes and a checksum matching Cargo.lock.\n\n(b) is a governance attestation about work someone must actually do (GOV-1-07, docs/09 T12); a worker filling it in to make its own gate green is the forged-attestation shape the manifest exists to prevent. Found while landing bn-2qa0u, which adds no dependency and leaves Cargo.lock byte-identical.","kind":"task","title":"just check is red on trunk: dependency-audits.toml lags Cargo.lock (blake3 1.8.6, cc 1.4.2, find-msvc-tools 0.1.10)"}	blake3:tSc1xdlWYaEN92BtL642eNK1FeERlQS7LKmLml8Vmx4
