1786299777726873	continuum-dev	itc:v3:AWKSTzM5JJnJPkQAAAAAQar23VW6voAAAAEylA0		item.comment	bn-imhw2	{"body":"[bn-imhw2 delivery 1/4] PER-STAGE DECISION, WITH THE EVIDENCE\n\nWorkspace bn-imhw2, commit 2fe4295, NOT merged, workspace not destroyed. 8 files, +4794/-29, all inside crates/continuum-context. Cargo.lock byte-identical (git diff --stat Cargo.lock empty); no dependency added; no schema, RFC or plan file edited.\n\nSTAGE 5 — proof-dependency slicing — TYPED REFUSAL. Evidence: plan §20 homes the proof lane in `continuum-proof-client`; that crate is a 22-line PR-1/IMPL-01 scaffold whose whole body is a `//!` doc comment and which has ZERO public items. `proof.slice` and `proof.goal` are registered operations in continuumd's IDL with no producing subsystem behind them — RFC 0026 `rule errors.unsupported_surface`'s literal case. So there is nothing here that can compute a proof dependency slice AND nothing that can run the proof-slice check RFC 0028's Validation section requires before `ProofRelevant` may be published. `ProofSlicing::refusal()` always returns a typed `StageRefusal`.\n\nSTAGE 6 — observer projection — IMPLEMENTED FOR REAL. This is the finding the split did not anticipate, and I verified it rather than assuming either way. `continuum-observer` IS a 19-line scaffold — but RFC 0028 names stage 6's input as \"**the intent's** observers\", and those are landed: `continuum_intent::observers::{ObserverSet, Observer, ObserverId, ProjectionKind}` is a complete PR-4/IMPL-03 field group (unit key, the four RFC 0031 projections, decode/encode, canonical identity, W1/W2), and `continuum-intent` is already one of continuum-context's three dependencies, so no new edge and no boundary change. The integration suite builds stage 6's premise out of exactly those types, so \"the input exists\" is evidenced by the file compiling, plus a source-text freshness pin on `continuum-intent/src/observers.rs`.\n\nSTAGE 7 — correspondence mapping — TYPED REFUSAL. Evidence: plan §16.1/§16.2 describe the input (typed concrete↔operational↔abstract↔observer↔Lean links, with get/put lenses, consistency relation, ambiguity conditions, generated obligations); plan §20 homes all of it in `continuum-refinement`, a 21-line scaffold with zero public items whose own doc comment names \"The correspondence graph, proof-oriented lenses… plan §16\". `correspondence.bind` is likewise a registered operation with no producer. A distinction I stated loudly in the module docs because the two share a word: `dependence::SourceCorrespondence` (stage 4, landed) is NOT this. Stage 4's is untrusted claims corroborated by execution attestation under INV-016; §16's is a typed lens with its own consistency relation and generated proof obligations. Stage 4 landing does not give stage 7 its input."}	blake3:cglB0ioB_5A_BBNeENhnLy8t2C_qQTBreI6Mg1Q3nQw
1786299798834640	continuum-dev	itc:v3:AWKSTzM5JJnJPkQAAAAAQar23VW6voAAAAEylQ0		item.comment	bn-imhw2	{"body":"[bn-imhw2 delivery 2/4] WHAT A REFUSAL COSTS, AND THE FIVE READINGS I HAD TO SETTLE\n\nsrc/unsupported.rs — the shared refusal vocabulary. `UnsupportedSurface` (2 members, declared in stage order so its derived Ord IS the precedence rule below), `AbsentProducer` (naming the plan §20 crate the tripwire reads — a closed enum, not a free string, so the refusal and its tripwire cannot drift), `SurfaceAbsence`, `StageRefusal`. A refusal costs exactly four things: the guarantee; an `unsupported` + `expandable:false` omission for every candidate only that stage could have decided; a typed `inconclusive_reason`; and an auditable intermediate recording that the stage RAN. It costs nothing else — the pipeline still runs end to end.\n\n(1) INV-008's SHAPE: \"no proof service in this deployment\" vs other absences. Two REACHABLE arms. `ProducerNotDeployed(AbsentProducer)` is a fact about the workspace no caller can change; `NothingNamed` is a fact about the QUESTION (no obligation / no subject named). The question's defect is decided FIRST, and the reason is principled rather than arbitrary: it is decidable WITHOUT consulting the absent producer — a slice \"of the named obligations\" over no obligations is vacuous whether or not a slicer exists, which is `monitor::Inapplicable::EmptyAlphabet`'s own reading. Both arms have identical consequences and are non-equal values with distinct trail notes; that is INV-008's point (the outcomes are distinguishable in the record, not treated differently).\n\n(2) WHICH VERDICT REASON WHEN BOTH STAGES REFUSE. A pack has one `inconclusive_reason`. The rule: the EARLIEST refusing stage names it, because a later stage's input would have been consumed over the earlier stage's output. It is a consequence of `UnsupportedSurface`'s declaration order feeding a BTreeMap, not a comparison anyone wrote. Stage 5 → `IncompleteProofSearch`, stage 7 → `AbstractionAmbiguity` — both get their FIRST producers here, and neither falls back to the generic `Unsupported` token (pinned).\n\n(3) STAGE 5's MANIFEST COLUMN IS `proof`, AND STAGE 7 HAS NONE. Stage 5 is the only stage that can put an item on a proof dependency slice, so with it refused an unpublished `proof` candidate has no deciding stage at all: `unsupported`, irretrievable. Stage 7 gets NO manifest cell, deliberately: the manifest partitions CANDIDATES and stage 7 drops none — what it costs is the concrete-to-abstract link, which `schema_epoch` 1 has no field for. Inventing a cell would make RFC 0028's counting equation false in the direction that looks like diligence, and would put a fact in the artifact contract the required-fields table has no home for. Recorded instead in three places a consumer reads: the trail, `Compilation::refusals()`, and the verdict's reason, plus `unmapped_correspondence()`.\n\n(4) NEITHER REFUSING STAGE NARROWS. Acting on behalf of a subsystem that does not exist is the \"guessing\" the rule prohibits, and a drop nothing decided could not be attributed to a deciding stage. Pinned by comparing the published selection with and without the stages configured.\n\n(5) EVERY STAGE-6 DROP IS `heuristic-cutoff`, NEVER `slice-irrelevant`. Stage 6 licenses SCOPING, not irrelevance. INV-013 justifies a reduction relative to \"named observers/properties **and fairness obligations**\"; stage 6 consults the first, stage 3 supplies the second, and the third has no producer in this workspace — so an item outside every named observer's scope is undecided, never disproved. This is bn-1kj2n's stage-4 reading (an uncorroborated claim is undecided, not disproved) pointed at the other justification source, and it is stated in compile.rs's ladder rather than inferred."}	blake3:pyCqIgn03WwiEbeNGw_TznF503VVlq6HNs4BrPr3gH0
1786299860944564	continuum-dev	itc:v3:AWKSTzM5JJnJPkQAAAAAQar23VW6voAAAAEylg0		item.comment	bn-imhw2	{"body":"[bn-imhw2 delivery 3/4] STAGE 6's SUBSTANCE AND THE TRIPWIRE DESIGNS\n\nSTAGE 6 DESIGN (src/observer.rs + src/scope.rs). The one thing missing between an observer's projections (sets of element-name strings) and a causal order's candidates (Name + SelectionKind) is the attribution, which is instrumentation and would live in `continuum-cir` (a stub). So it is a DECLARED input, `Observation{ProjectionKind, element}`, exactly as CausalOrder and PropertyAutomaton are. Three consequences, each a test:\n- A candidate with NO declaration is never dropped. INV-013 read literally: no justification, no reduction.\n- `ObserverFilter::retain` seeds from (protected ∪ unattributed ∪ in-scope) and RE-CLOSES, so the output stays downward closed and stage 6 cannot break stage 2's guarantee.\n- **Stage 6 cannot undo stage 3 — a theorem, not a coincidence.** Stage 3's output is the backward closure of the relevance set, so every member is either protected or an ancestor of something protected, and both are restored. That IS RFC 0028's \"a compiler MUST NOT exclude an abstraction-relevant hidden event on the grounds that no observer publishes it\", made structural. The load-bearing pair: WITHOUT the property, the same projection drops `e_flush` (no observer publishes it); WITH it, it may not.\n- Empty observer set / an order no named observer publishes → `ProjectionInapplicable::{NoNamedObserver, NoObservedCandidate}`, the monitor's two-arm precedent. Stage 6 then narrows NOTHING and says why — an empty observer set would otherwise \"justify\" dropping everything, which is justified by nothing.\n\nTHE INDEPENDENT CHECKER, AND WHAT IT DOES NOT LICENSE. `scope::ScopeAudit` is a different computation (the filter selects by seed+closure; the audit examines each dropped candidate individually against the observer set, the protected set and the attribution, then re-checks closure), in a different module, reading only (order, ScopeReduction). `ScopeReduction` is publicly constructible so hand-built reductions the filter cannot produce get an answer from the premise alone. `with_observer_projection(projection, audit)` takes both separately, so a stricter audit refuses. **Its affirmative verdict licenses NOTHING** — RFC 0028's Licenses column reads \"never a guarantee by itself\", so `ScopeVerdict::Justified` is an audit result, not a `License`, and `the_scope_audit_module_imports_only_the_premise_the_filter_also_reads` mechanically pins that scope.rs's production code contains no `License::issue`, no `use crate::guarantee`, no `ObserverFilter` and no `use crate::compile`.\n\nTRIPWIRE DESIGNS (all in tests/pr11_compiler_stages_5_7.rs; the INV-015 `boundary_the_host_effect_surface_has_not_arrived` device).\nT1 `tripwire_the_proof_service_and_the_correspondence_graph_have_no_producer` — include_str! of `continuum-proof-client/src/lib.rs` and `continuum-refinement/src/lib.rs`; asserts `pub_items()` is EMPTY on both and each still declares \"PR-1 / IMPL-01 scaffold\" and the responsibility the refusal cites. GOES RED the moment either crate grows a public item, forcing the refusals to be reconciled against a surface that now exists. Anti-vacuity `negative_the_producer_tripwire_is_not_vacuous`: `pub_items` is non-empty on this crate's own src/proof.rs, and the scaffold text with one `pub fn` spliced in is caught.\nT2 `tripwire_the_crate_licenses_exactly_two_guarantees_and_proof_relevance_is_not_one` — THE ANTI-VACUITY MUTANT THE BONE ASKED FOR. `License::issue` is pub(crate), so the only code that could mint `ProofRelevant` is this crate. The test scans EVERY `License::issue(` call site in the production half of all 27 source files (split at `#[cfg(test)]` — monitor.rs's precedent — with comment lines stripped, because guarantee.rs's module doc carries a compile_fail doctest whose whole point is such a line) and holds the result to a RECORDED INVENTORY: exactly [\"Guarantee::CausallyClosed\", \"Guarantee::PropertyPreserving\"]. A third call site, or a different guarantee at either, fails until the audit is redone. Anti-vacuity `negative_the_licence_inventory_is_not_vacuous`: compile.rs's production text with `set.claim(License::issue(Guarantee::ProofRelevant))` spliced in IS caught by the same scan, and a module with no call site yields nothing (so the scanner is not matching on the word \"Guarantee\").\nT3 `every_source_file_of_the_crate_is_recorded` — closes T2's loop with a runtime read_dir over src/: a NEW MODULE fails this test until it is added to the inventory, so the licence scan cannot silently stop covering the crate.\nT4 `tripwire_the_intents_observers_are_still_the_landed_field_group_stage_six_reads` — the positive-side freshness pin: five declarations of `continuum-intent/src/observers.rs`, so if stage 6's input moves or narrows, its \"the input is here\" reading is re-derived rather than assumed."}	blake3:6UWa9uyT10K7ycoUw6-HqT80WwBTQ3aE6X2kBPKhmPw
1786299897277182	continuum-dev	itc:v3:AWKSTzM5JJnJPkQAAAAAQar23VW6voAAAAEylw0		item.comment	bn-imhw2	{"body":"[bn-imhw2 delivery 4/4] TEST INVENTORY, GATE RESULTS, DELIBERATE EXCLUSIONS\n\nTEST INVENTORY — 58 new unit tests (296 in the crate, was 238) + 33 new integration tests from outside the crate.\nsrc/unsupported.rs (6): every refusal is `unsupported` + irretrievable and the two spellings agree; the two absences have distinct tokens AND are unequal values at one surface; each surface names its own inconclusive reason and neither is the generic `Unsupported`; each names its stage (5, 7) and its plan §20 crate; the surfaces sort into pipeline order (the precedence rule); all four trail notes distinct and token-shaped.\nsrc/proof.rs (6) + src/correspondence.rs (5): the refusal and its typed absence; the no-obligation / no-subject absence with identical consequences and a different record; stage 5 decides exactly the `proof` kind; every subject unmapped because nothing maps; canonical (shortlex) ordering; determinism.\nsrc/observer.rs (13): the scope is what a named observer publishes; observers reported by id; unattributed never dropped; a protected candidate survives; the filter re-closes; a narrowing stays downward closed; A COARSENED OBSERVER NARROWS THE SCOPE (the module's anti-vacuity); both Inapplicable arms; the four projection kinds do not cross (`events:pending` is not `state_projection:pending`); a candidate attributed twice refused; a slice from outside the order refused; determinism.\nsrc/scope.rs (11): the filter's own output is justified; THE AUDIT REJECTS HAND-BUILT REDUCTIONS THE FILTER CANNOT PRODUCE (observed-dropped / added / unclosed, plus the honest one still passing); protected-dropped reported as its OWN violation ahead of the observer check; the observer named in the violation; unattributed-dropped; the vacuous-reduction arm under an inapplicable projection, both directions; a stricter audit refuses; determinism.\nsrc/compile.rs (13 new): stage 5 refuses and declines proof relevance; the proof candidates are unsupported+irretrievable and the cell exists BECAUSE a stage ran and refused; a refusing stage records that it ran and narrows nothing; stage 7 invents no manifest cell; the earliest refusing stage names the verdict's reason; stage 6 licenses nothing while visibly narrowing; a stage-6 drop is heuristic-cutoff (exact (kind,reason)->count map); stage 6 cannot undo stage 3 with an APPLICABLE projection; the hidden event survives; attribution/subject from nowhere refused; the eight-phase trail; determinism.\ntests/pr11_compiler_stages_5_7.rs (33, from outside the crate, 225 candidates at the G0-DX-01 grain): fixture of 11 named candidates (the durability chain, the isolated hidden e_flush, a diagnostic chain, stage 4's corroborated/uncorroborated pair, TWO `proof` candidates) plus 214 noise; the seven-stage pipeline end to end with two stages refusing; the exact four-cell manifest naming every deciding stage including the refusing one (219 omissions, reconciled); full stage-5 and stage-7 refusal evidence; RFC 0028 C1 across the crate boundary; both INV-013 halves; the audit's four hand-built rejections; a stricter audit; redaction still winning over all three stages with BOTH irretrievable reasons in one manifest; the four tripwires; determinism with a non-vacuous companion.\n\nGATE RESULTS — `maw exec bn-imhw2 -- just check` run in the FOREGROUND to completion, EXIT 0.\nGREEN, all nine recipes: fmt-check; lint (clippy --workspace --all-targets --locked -D warnings); test (cargo test --workspace --locked, 235 `test result: ok` lines, 0 failures); boundaries; covenant; governance (the dep-audit red bn-1kj2n reported is fixed at trunk — bn-sk44r closed); dossier (status pass, spec_debt open []); lean (19 jobs, axiom manifest up to date, every T0/T1 theorem axiom-free). Every cargo invocation was `--locked`; `git diff --stat Cargo.lock` is empty.\n\nDELIBERATE EXCLUSIONS, named rather than implied\n- NO MANIFEST CELL FOR STAGE 7, and no `redactions[]` stub — reasons in delivery 2/4.\n- NO CHANGE TO THE `proof`/`source`/`model` DROP REASONS WHEN THEIR STAGE IS NOT CONFIGURED. A `proof` candidate in a compile that never ran stage 5 keeps the causal order's reason, as before. I considered widening rung 6 of the ladder to \"any kind whose deciding stage did not run is heuristic-cutoff\" and did not: it would change landed stage-1–2/3–4 behaviour for `source`/`model` and break their goldens, and it is a different bone's call. The new `unsupported` rung fires only when a stage RAN and refused.\n- STAGE 5's REFUSAL DOES NOT UN-SELECT a `proof` candidate stage 2 selected as a causal ancestor. That item is in the pack for stage 2's reason and under stage 2's guarantee; `ProofRelevant` is not claimed about it or anything else.\n- OBLIGATIONS ARE NOT CHECKED AGAINST THE CAUSAL ORDER (correspondence subjects and observer attributions ARE). An obligation is a proof-side identity from a subsystem this workspace lacks, so there is nothing here to check it against; inventing one would be a second unchecked authority. The asymmetry is stated in proof.rs and pinned by a test.\n- THE PACK's `verdict` FIELD. `Compilation::inconclusive_reason()` is the typed reason a refusal owes; the verdict itself is the evaluation's, which this crate does not run. Whole-pack assembly (bn-1y4qc) pairs the two; `verdict::Verdict::Inconclusive` already makes an untyped one unspellable at that seam.\n- `continuumd/src/daemon/evidence.rs:1898` declares the assurance envelope's `observer` dimension `Unsupported(\"no-observer-projection\")`. That reading is still true of the DAEMON (context.compile is refused and its evidence lane compiles no pack), but it is now false of the WORKSPACE. Untouched here — daemon wiring is bn-1y4qc's — and flagged for that bone: when context.compile lands, that dimension has a producer to name.\n- NO NEW DEPENDENCY. `continuum-observer` is a scaffold and adding an edge to it would buy nothing; stage 6 reads `continuum-intent`, already a dependency.\n- STAGE 8 (bn-3ub6i), stage 9 and stage 10 untouched.\n\nSURPRISES FOR bn-3ub6i / bn-1y4qc\n- The split's assumption that stage 6 might also be a refusal is FALSE, and the reason generalises: check `continuum-intent` before concluding a §-level input is missing. Several plan-§ artifacts are homed in scaffold crates but their INTENT-side field group is landed.\n- `Name`'s SHORTLEX order bites again: the seven-stage core is [e_ack, e_loss, e_begin, e_flush, s_writer, e_submit].\n- `continuum_intent::observers::ObserverId` is `Ord` but the `Observer` type has a hand-written `PartialEq` and no `Hash`; the `Name`-has-no-`Hash` warning applies to it too.\n- The licence-inventory tripwire (T2) and the source-file inventory (T3) will fail for ANY bone that adds a module to continuum-context or issues a new guarantee licence. That is by design — bn-3ub6i's minimality classes will have to extend both, which is exactly the audit being redone rather than skipped."}	blake3:R8SgMVao2WWC_r4Lu06BwlmrasdsCu-NmmcNcEJSJGo
1786299954272197	continuum-dev	itc:v3:AWKSTzM5JJnJPkQAAAAAQar23VW6voAAAAEymA0		item.comment	bn-imhw2	{"body":"Lead ratification: merged @ 513557e45df1 (workspace destroyed, snapshot retained). Review: stage-6 reversal ACCEPTED — the worker checked the actual input home (continuum-intent's landed ObserverSet field group) instead of trusting the split's hedge, which is exactly the check-continuum-intent-first lesson now recorded for the remaining children. Stage 5/7 refusals are the right INV-008 shapes (IncompleteProofSearch, AbstractionAmbiguity) with source-scanning tripwires; the License-issue call-site inventory {CausallyClosed, PropertyPreserving} is a strong anti-vacuity device — NOTED: bn-3ub6i must extend both inventories or fail T2/T3 by design. Stage 6 never-a-guarantee-by-itself pinned by guarantee-set comparison; stage-6-cannot-undo-stage-3 proven structural. The daemon evidence.rs:1898 no-observer-projection honest-absence flag recorded for bn-1y4qc's reconciliation. Closing."}	blake3:2af2MzyoEU4_3f6OgAzQuaElSJvEsquKr0gfuDu2W4s
